{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt host/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh host/gambit/ffi/verify-digests.sh; git diff -- Makefile jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj host/gambit/boot.ss; cat /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-inv/p1b-inv/shim-registry.edn'","aggregated_output":"#!/bin/sh\n# watchdog.sh N CMD... — run CMD under an external watchdog.\n#\n# If CMD has not exited within N seconds it is SIGKILLed, the script prints\n# \"WATCHDOG: TIMEOUT ...\" on stderr and exits 124, so a deadlock (e.g. the\n# whole Gambit VM frozen inside a blocking foreign call) is a recorded\n# FAILURE, never a hang.\n#\n# The Gambit VM has exactly one OS thread running Scheme execution in the\n# provisioned build, so a Scheme-internal timeout CANNOT fire while a foreign\n# call is blocked — the watchdog must be external to the witness process.\n\nn=\"$1\"; shift\n\n\"$@\" &\npid=$!\n\n( sleep \"$n\"; kill -9 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null ) &\nwd_pid=$!\n\nwait \"$pid\"\nst=$?\n\nkill \"$wd_pid\" 2>/dev/null\nwait \"$wd_pid\" 2>/dev/null\n\nif [ \"$st\" -eq 137 ]; then\n  echo \"WATCHDOG: TIMEOUT after ${n}s — SIGKILLed: $*\" >&2\n  exit 124\nfi\nexit \"$st\"\n# host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt — the pinned inputs of the stage-1 native bridge.\n#\n# The gambitffi* Makefile targets verify these BEFORE building: the bridge is\n# compiled from exactly this source, never an ambient artifact. A source edit\n# that does not update this file fails the gate (the digest is the bootstrap's\n# pinned-input record; regenerate with: sh host/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh).\nhost/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm 8fd20c23de22ddc036e6d04744845f8ab27388e7b0285ba3302f5c49804a24a3\nhost/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture.c cc7c91817e90400b6bb65b25c516d54921e736e2450337f0fbb0fa125ab483bd\nhost/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture2.c d2959a1ba04099845f391dcc599168ec5b38c43d0146c1e8c06a142729721b3c\n#!/bin/sh\n# make-digests.sh — regenerate host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt from the current\n# sources. Run AFTER editing the bridge or fixture sources, as part of the same\n# change (a stale digest fails the gambitffi* gates fail-closed).\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../../..\"\n{\n  echo \"# host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt — the pinned inputs of the stage-1 native bridge.\"\n  echo \"#\"\n  echo \"# The gambitffi* Makefile targets verify these BEFORE building: the bridge is\"\n  echo \"# compiled from exactly this source, never an ambient artifact. A source edit\"\n  echo \"# that does not update this file fails the gate (the digest is the bootstrap's\"\n  echo \"# pinned-input record; regenerate with: sh host/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh).\"\n  shasum -a 256 host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm \\\n                host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture.c \\\n                host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture2.c | awk '{print $2\" \"$1}'\n} > host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt\necho \"DIGESTS.txt regenerated\"\n#!/bin/bash\n# verify-digests.sh — the pinned-input check the gambitffi* builds run BEFORE\n# compiling anything: the bridge and fixture sources must match the digests\n# recorded in host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt. Fail-closed on any mismatch.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../../..\"\n\nout=$(shasum -a 256 host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm \\\n                 host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture.c \\\n                 host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture2.c | awk '{print $2\" \"$1}')\npinned=$(grep -v '^#' host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt | grep -v '^$')\n\nif [ \"$out\" = \"$pinned\" ]; then\n  echo \"gambitffi: pinned inputs verified (3 digests)\"\nelse\n  echo \"gambitffi: bridge/fixture sources do not match host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt —\" >&2\n  echo \"  regenerate with sh host/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh in the same change\" >&2\n  printf '%s\\n' \"$pinned\" > /tmp/gambitffi-pinned\n  printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" > /tmp/gambitffi-out\n  diff /tmp/gambitffi-pinned /tmp/gambitffi-out >&2 || true\n  exit 1\nfi\ndiff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile\nindex b18868cb..f8cad393 100644\n--- a/Makefile\n+++ b/Makefile\n@@ -128,6 +128,7 @@ JOLT-TARGETS-NEEDING-DEPS := \\\n .PHONY: nsaudit kondocheck build install test ci bionic-ci ci-shard ci-shard-list gate-run-test gate-run-ci gate-run-bionic-ci gate-run-ci-shard gate-status hooks attributioncheck noticecheck monitormodel \\\n         gambitcheck gambitkernel gambiteval gambitseed gambitweb gambitprofile \\\n         gambitgen gambitgencheck gambitseedcheck gambitunbound gambitunbound-regen \\\n+        gambitffi gambitffi-abi gambitffi-errno-check gambitffi-load-failure-smoke gambitffi-bridge \\\n         gambitvars gambitvars-regen gambitstatics gambitstatics-regen gambittwins grenadinecheck \\\n         fibersbench dynbench \\\n         fibersresidue\n@@ -2060,6 +2061,111 @@ gambitboot:\n \t  $(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n \tfi\n \n+# ---- P1b-stage1: the gambitffi* gates ----------------------------------------\n+#\n+# The bounded FFI tier qualified per the standing codex C4 PARTIAL-GO ruling:\n+# memory ops, loading, ordinary calls and invocation-local errno capture,\n+# behind the ahead-of-time native bridge (host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm,\n+# compiled by gsc into build/gambit-ffi/joltffi-bridge.o1). Blocking,\n+# callables, runtime signatures and object pinning keep their message-carrying\n+# refusals; the gates assert both the witnesses AND the retained refusals.\n+#\n+# Deterministic bootstrap: every artifact builds from the pinned inputs in\n+# host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt — verified before compiling, output digests\n+# recorded after. No ambient .o1/.dylib is ever trusted. The aggregate target\n+# is fail-closed: it passes only when all three gate scripts pass, and a gate\n+# runs under the P1a-r2 external watchdog (host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh, the\n+# same pattern the p1a witnesses use) so a frozen VM is a recorded failure,\n+# never a hang.\n+\n+GAMBIT-FFI-DIR := host/gambit/ffi\n+GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD := build/gambit-ffi\n+\n+# the pinned inputs must match the recorded digests BEFORE anything compiles\n+gambitffi-verify-digests:\n+\t@sh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/verify-digests.sh\n+\n+$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1: $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-bridge.scm \\\n+\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt\n+\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n+\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n+\t@gsc never overwrites a versioned link file: a stale .o1 here would be\\\n+\t loaded by the adapter while gsc writes .o2/.o3 next to it. rm first.\n+\t@rm -f $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o[0-9]* \\\n+\t       $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.c $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o \\\n+\t       $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.scm\n+\tcp $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-bridge.scm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.scm\n+\tcd $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD) && $(GAMBIT_GSC) joltffi-bridge.scm\n+\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 \\\n+\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1.sha256\n+\n+$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib: $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture.c \\\n+\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt\n+\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n+\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n+\tcc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n+\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture.c\n+\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n+\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib.sha256\n+\n+$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib: $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c \\\n+\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt\n+\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n+\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n+\tcc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n+\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c\n+\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n+\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib.sha256\n+\n+# the present-but-unloadable candidate: a one-symbol dylib linked against a\n+# dependency dylib this recipe then REMOVES, so dlopen fails with the loader's\n+# own preserved reason (a missing dependency, not a missing file)\n+$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib: $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt \\\n+\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c\n+\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n+\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n+\tprintf 'int joltffi_dep_marker(void){return 1;}\\n' > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/dep.c\n+\tcc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/dep.c\n+\tprintf 'extern int joltffi_dep_marker(void);\\nint joltffi_unloadable_probe(void){return joltffi_dep_marker();}\\n' \\\n+\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/unloadable.c\n+\tcc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n+\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/unloadable.c \\\n+\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n+\trm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n+\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n+\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib.sha256\n+\n+# bridge + fixtures, always current: the entry every gambitffi gate depends on\n+gambitffi-bridge: $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 \\\n+                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n+                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n+                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\n+\n+gambitffi-abi: gambitffi-bridge\n+\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n+\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-abi.ss; \\\n+\telse \\\n+\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n+\tfi\n+\n+gambitffi-errno-check: gambitffi-bridge\n+\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n+\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-errno.ss; \\\n+\telse \\\n+\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n+\tfi\n+\n+gambitffi-load-failure-smoke: gambitffi-bridge\n+\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n+\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 90 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-load-failure.ss; \\\n+\telse \\\n+\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n+\tfi\n+\n+# the aggregate: all three, fail-closed (each script exits nonzero on failure)\n+gambitffi: gambitffi-abi gambitffi-errno-check gambitffi-load-failure-smoke\n+\t@echo \"gambitffi: PASS — all stage-1 qualified-tier gates green\"\n+\n # The browser bundle: the whole stack (kernel + seed + compiler + a queue-polling\n # REPL loop) compiled to one JavaScript file by the Gambit backend. ~30s, ~32MB\n # raw / ~4MB gzipped, which is what a web server ships. Point GAMBIT_WEB_OUT at\ndiff --git a/host/gambit/boot.ss b/host/gambit/boot.ss\nindex cc32d83e..63b4c0cd 100644\n--- a/host/gambit/boot.ss\n+++ b/host/gambit/boot.ss\n@@ -127,6 +127,11 @@\n ;; the clojure.core names the excluded java/ tree owns on Chez — after\n ;; post-prelude so these bindings are the last word\n (##include \"host-vars.ss\")\n+;; the jolt.ffi names the excluded java/ffi.ss owns on Chez — P1b-stage1: the\n+;; memory/loader/errno surface behind the qualified tier, with every\n+;; unimplemented row bound to a message-carrying refusal (same rule as\n+;; host-vars.ss: nothing unbound, nothing pretending)\n+(##include \"host-ffi.ss\")\n (set-chez-ns! \"user\")\n (##include \"seed/image.ss\")\n (##include \"../chez/compile-eval.ss\")\ndiff --git a/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj b/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj\nindex cc4362a9..e237e5cb 100644\n--- a/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj\n+++ b/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj\n@@ -480,16 +480,29 @@\n                               \"sa-foreign-procedure-blocking \"\n                               \"sa-foreign-procedure \")\n                        conv \" \" csym signature \")\"))\n-        scoped (str \"(let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \" csym \"))) \"\n-                    \"(and a \"\n-                    (if capture\n-                      (str \"(jolt-ffi-native-error-procedure (\" capture-conv \") a\"\n-                           signature \")\")\n-                      (str \"(foreign-procedure\"\n-                           (when blocking \" __collect_safe\")\n-                           (when vi conv)\n-                           \" a\" signature \")\"))\n-                    \"))\")]\n+        ;; P1b-stage1 gap G-3 — astra: replace the raw Chez scoped-address\n+        ;; emission with adapter operations. On :gambit the scoped branch\n+        ;; routes through the adapter syntaxes too: the adapter shape\n+        ;; registry raises deliberately for unregistered shapes, never leaving\n+        ;; the call to an unbound Chez foreign-procedure identifier.\n+        scoped (if (= :gambit (target))\n+                  (str \"(let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \" csym \"))) \"\n+                       \"(and a \"\n+                       (if capture\n+                         (str \"(jolt-ffi-native-error-procedure (\" capture-conv \") a\"\n+                              signature \")\")\n+                         (str \"(sa-foreign-procedure a\" signature \")\"))\n+                       \"))\")\n+                  (str \"(let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \" csym \"))) \"\n+                       \"(and a \"\n+                       (if capture\n+                         (str \"(jolt-ffi-native-error-procedure (\" capture-conv \") a\"\n+                              signature \")\")\n+                         (str \"(foreign-procedure\"\n+                              (when blocking \" __collect_safe\")\n+                              (when vi conv)\n+                              \" a\" signature \")\"))\n+                       \"))\"))]\n     (str \"(or p (begin (set! p (or \" scoped \" \" by-name \")) p))\")))\n \n ;; jolt.ffi/pointer-fn: the procedure is built against the address in the\n@@ -626,6 +639,23 @@\n         (str \"(lambda args (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException \"\n              (chez-str-lit \"jolt.ffi/pointer-fn: ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n              \"))\")\n+      ;; gap G-2: a by-value aggregate needs define-ftype / (& ftype), unbound\n+      ;; on the gambit boot — refuse in words instead of dying on the ftype\n+      ;; forms the way the pre-stage1 emission did.\n+      (and (= :gambit (target))\n+           (or (some ffi-by-value? at) (ffi-by-value? (:rettype node))))\n+        (str \"(throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException \"\n+             (chez-str-lit \"jolt.ffi/foreign-fn: by-value aggregates are unsupported on the gambit target (no ftype engine behind the stage-1 bridge)\")\n+             \")\")\n+      ;; bare :& compiles a foreign procedure per observed tail shape at run\n+      ;; time (ffi-varargs-compile, an eval of runtime-signature construction) —\n+      ;; exactly the open-ended shape space the finite stage-1 registry cannot\n+      ;; claim. Compile-time refusal; declared-tail varargs still route through\n+      ;; the registry below.\n+      (and (= :gambit (target)) vi (= vi (dec (count at))))\n+        (str \"(throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException \"\n+             (chez-str-lit \"jolt.ffi/foreign-fn: bare :& varargs are unsupported on the gambit target (per-call tail shapes compile at run time, outside the stage-1 registry)\")\n+             \")\")\n       (and vi (= vi (dec (count at)))) (emit-ffi-bare-varargs-fn node vi)\n       :else (emit-ffi-fixed-fn node vi))))\n \n@@ -757,7 +787,14 @@\n ;; The three jolt.ffi IR ops. EMIT lowers a callable's wrapped fn.\n (defn emit-ffi-node [emit node]\n   (case (:op node)\n-    :ffi-layout (emit-ffi-layout node)\n+    ;; gap G-1 (inventory Q1): on :gambit a :ffi-layout emitted Chez\n+    ;; define-ftype/make-ftype-pointer text that died as an unbound identifier\n+    ;; at namespace load; refuse in words, at the form, instead.\n+    :ffi-layout (if (= :gambit (target))\n+                  (str \"(throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException \"\n+                       (chez-str-lit \"jolt.ffi/layout: ffi-layout (ftype aggregates) are unsupported on the gambit target\")\n+                       \")\")\n+                  (emit-ffi-layout node))\n     :ffi-fn (emit-ffi-fn node)\n     :ffi-callable\n     (if (and (= :gambit (target))\ndiff --git a/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj b/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj\nindex c8cb8397..08867cf8 100644\n--- a/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj\n+++ b/jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj\n@@ -74,7 +74,12 @@\n ;; derived spelling degrades to the checked op, safe-and-slower, never wrong.\n (defn target [] @(:target (cur)))\n (def ^:private target-prims\n-  {:chez {:unsafe-prefix \"#3%\"}})\n+  {:chez  {:unsafe-prefix \"#3%\"}\n+   ;; P1b-stage1 (inventory Q4): the entry astra named, made explicit. Gambit\n+   ;; has no unsafe variants, so the prefix is \"\" and every derived spelling\n+   ;; degrades to the checked op — this table now DECIDES that instead of the\n+   ;; (str nil) accident the pre-stage1 lookup degraded through.\n+   :gambit {:unsafe-prefix \"\"}})\n (defn unsafe-prefix [] (get-in target-prims [(target) :unsafe-prefix]))\n \n ;; contagion clone sites (jolt devirt-gated fl* contagion for :num fields): a set of\n;; p1b-inv/shim-registry.edn — initial typed-shim registry (P1b-prep static slice)\n;;\n;; Fork: jolt gambit-ffi-inv @ a6852ef8. Companion artifacts:\n;;   ffi-call-sites.md  (every construction site, file:line)\n;;   CONSUMERS.md       (native consumers' binding surfaces, one row per binding)\n;;\n;; Design ruling implemented (astra §2): \"use typed, generated C shims per call\n;; shape, shared across symbols with identical ABI shapes. Each accepts the\n;; resolved function address. Signature identity includes argument/result types,\n;; calling convention, variadic boundary, and relevant ABI layout. ... a finite\n;; precompiled registry cannot claim arbitrary runtime-signature support.\n;; Unregistered shapes must raise. Generate the initial registry from the native\n;; consumer inventory and test fixtures.\"\n;;\n;; SHAPE IDENTITY = {:args [jolt-type ...] :ret jolt-type\n;;                   :blocking bool :capture-native-error bool\n;;                   :variadic nil | {:fixed-count n :tail [jolt-type ...]}\n;;                   :kind :procedure | :callable | :pointer-call\n;;                   :entry-convention :normal | :collect-safe   (callables)}\n;; Two bindings share a shim iff their shape identity is equal.\n;;\n;; :disposition values\n;;   :shim        a generated C shim is owed by the P2/P3 slice; argument is the\n;;                resolved function address; errno variants save errno inside the\n;;                shim (astra §2 wrapper sequence) before any conversion/cleanup.\n;;   :shim+p2     shape belongs to a named native consumer (jolt-crypto /\n;;                jolt-file / jolt-parser); required for the P2/P3 gates.\n;;   :platform    fork-stdlib shape the Gambit io/socket lanes need (not part of\n;;                the P2/P3 consumer triad but produced by real sites in this fork).\n;;   :fixture     produced only by test/chez fixtures today; registration keeps\n;;                the refusal data honest, the P1b designer decides whether the\n;;                shape ships.\n;;   :raise       a site produces it but the Gambit path must DELIBERATELY raise\n;;                (message-carrying) per astra's P1 boundary: unqualified\n;;                blocking/callable modes, dynamic signature compilation.\n;;\n;; Type vocabulary = jolt.ffi keyword names (stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj docstring,\n;; lines 17-20), marshaled per jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj ffi-types\n;; (16-31) and host/chez/java/ffi.ss ffi-type->chez (685-716). :bool is the\n;; ONE-BYTE C99 _Bool (unsigned-8 on the wire, converted at the boundary).\n\n{:p1b-inv/shim-registry\n {:schema-version 1\n  :fork-sha \"a6852ef8\"\n  :branch \"gambit-ffi-inv\"\n  :generated-by \"p1b-prep static analysis (no builds, no runs)\"\n  :sources\n  {:consumers [\"datomworld:src/jolt/dao/host/hash.jolt\"\n               \"datomworld:src/jolt/dao/host/sign.jolt\"\n               \"datomworld:src/jolt/dao/posix/random.jolt\"\n               \"datomworld:src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/crypto.jolt\"\n               \"datomworld:src/jolt/dao/posix/file.jolt\"\n               \"datomworld:src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt\"\n               \"fork:stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj\"\n               \"fork:stdlib/jolt/io_poller.clj\"\n               \"fork:stdlib/jolt/socket/native.clj\"\n               \"fork:stdlib/jolt/mvn_http.clj\"\n               \"fork:stdlib/jolt/winsock.clj\"]\n   :fixtures [\"test/chez/ffi-widths-test.ss\" \"test/chez/ffi-binding-test.ss\"\n              \"test/chez/ffi-native-error-test.ss/.clj\" \"test/chez/ffi-aggregate-test.ss/.clj\"\n              \"test/chez/jolt-ffi-callback-by-value-test.clj\" \"test/chez/jolt-ffi-pointer-call-test.clj\"\n              \"test/chez/jolt-ffi-scoped-test.clj\" \"test/chez/jolt-ffi-string-arg-test.clj\"\n              \"test/chez/jolt-ffi-string-null-test.clj\" \"test/chez/ffi-gc-stall-test.clj\"\n              \"test/chez/ffi-foreign-thread-test.clj\" \"test/chez/jolt-ffi-callback-preempt-test.clj\"\n              \"test/chez/ffi-stack-args-test.ss\" \"test/chez/jolt-ffi-layout-test.clj\"\n              \"test/chez/jolt-ffi-typed-array-test.clj\" \"test/chez/ffi-layout-test.ss\"]}\n\n  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  ;; Shapes produced by the three native consumers (the P2/P3 seed).\n  ;; One entry per distinct ABI shape; every producing symbol is referenced.\n  ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  :consumer-shapes\n  [;; S-01 — no-argument scalar probes (layout/version/errno-code gates)\n   {:id :shape/s01-noarg-int\n    :args [] :ret :int\n    :blocking false :capture-native-error false :variadic nil :kind :procedure\n    :disposition :shim+p2\n    :produced-by\n    [{:sym \"jolt_crypto_layout_version\" :at \"src/jolt