{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm'","aggregated_output":";; joltffi-bridge.scm — the Gambit FFI stage-1 native bridge (P1b-stage1).\n;;\n;; The typed, per-call-shape C shims astra §2 specifies, compiled AHEAD OF TIME\n;; with gsc (c-lambda is a compiled facility; the interpreter must never expand\n;; one) into build/gambit-ffi/joltffi-bridge.o1 and loaded from gsi with (load).\n;; Every gate target builds it from THIS file alone — no ambient artifacts.\n;;\n;; SCOPE is the standing codex C4 ruling (PARTIAL-GO), verbatim constraints:\n;;   qualified  = memory, loading, ORDINARY calls, invocation-local errno capture\n;;   refused    = GC-safe blocking, blocking+errno, generic foreign-pthread\n;;                callbacks, dynamic closure-backed callables (F6: stock 4.9.8\n;;                has no arm64/x86_64 trampoline generator), runtime-signature\n;;                construction, AOT/FASL/subprocess.\n;; The shim set below therefore covers exactly the non-blocking, non-callable,\n;; non-aggregate shapes registered in p1b-inv/shim-registry.edn\n;; (:p1b-inv/shim-registry, 44 shapes total; every blocking/callable/aggregate/\n;; bare-varargs shape is deliberately absent — a lookup against it raises in the\n;; adapter, never a dereference of the wrong ABI).\n;;\n;; EVERY capture shim implements the astra §2 essential sequence exactly:\n;;\n;;     result = target(args);\n;;     int saved = errno;              IMMEDIATELY after the target returns,\n;;     *errout = saved;                before conversion, cleanup, allocation\n;;     return result;                  or runtime re-entry.\n;;\n;; The errno travels out through a CALLER-ALLOCATED cell (one malloc per call,\n;; allocated by the adapter BEFORE the target call and freed after the Scheme\n;; side reads it) — an invocation-local channel, never a global or TLS \"last\n;; errno\" cell, both of which astra forbids and both of which fail nested and\n;; concurrent calls. Post-capture clobbering (by the target, a later foreign\n;; call, or conversion) cannot reach the captured pair: the W1-r2 negative\n;; controls in joltffi-fixture.c prove the capture position is load-bearing.\n;;\n;; POINTER CONVENTION: pointers cross as exact integers (jolt's own semantics —\n;; a jolt pointer IS a raw address), through the c-lambda `unsigned-long` type\n;; (8 bytes on both supported legs: arm64 macOS, x86_64/arm64 Linux — LP64).\n;; This keeps Gambit pointer-object conversion out of the hot path and makes\n;; address arithmetic behave exactly as Chez's integer pointers do.\n;;\n;; BYTEVECTOR CONVENTION: bulk moves borrow the bytevector's body through\n;; ___BODY_AS(v, ___tU8VECTOR) for the duration of ONE synchronous foreign\n;; call. No collection can run during that call on the provisioned single-\n;; processor runtime (a GC request waits for the blocked processor — codex Q3),\n;; so the borrowed address is stable for the call's duration, exactly the\n;; borrowing argument the Chez adapter makes for its own memcpy moves (which are\n;; deliberately NOT __collect_safe). The bridge never RETAINS a borrowed body.\n;;\n;; errno ATOMICITY at the boundary relies on nothing outside the shim body:\n;; the c-lambda call machinery does not read or write errno (verified: it saves\n;; and restores only Scheme registers — gambit.h FFI macros, codex F2 audit).\n\n(c-declare #<<JOLTFFI-C-BEGIN\n\n#include <errno.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <dlfcn.h>\n#include <stdarg.h>\n\n/* ---- loader flags (compile-time platform, as the Chez loader probes them) ---\n   RTLD_NOW on every POSIX host; RTLD_LOCAL on darwin is 0x4, on Linux 0 (the\n   default, matching Chez's ffi-rtld-flags table in host/chez/java/ffi.ss). */\n#define JOLTFFI_RTLD_NOW   2\n#ifdef __APPLE__\n#define JOLTFFI_RTLD_LOCAL 0x4\n#else\n#define JOLTFFI_RTLD_LOCAL 0\n#endif\n\n/* ---- loader ----------------------------------------------------------------- */\nstatic unsigned long joltffi_c_dlopen (const char *path)\n{ return ___CAST(unsigned long, dlopen (path, JOLTFFI_RTLD_NOW | JOLTFFI_RTLD_LOCAL)); }\n\nstatic unsigned long joltffi_c_dlsym (unsigned long h, const char *name)\n{ return ___CAST(unsigned long, dlsym (___CAST(void *, h), name)); }\n\n/* process-global resolution (RTLD_DEFAULT): the process's own symbols plus\n   RTLD_GLOBAL objects. RTLD_LOCAL loaded natives are deliberately NOT visible\n   here — the scoped-before-global isolation guarantee. */\nstatic unsigned long joltffi_c_dlsym_global (const char *name)\n{ return ___CAST(unsigned long, dlsym (RTLD_DEFAULT, name)); }\n\nstatic unsigned long joltffi_c_dlopen_global (const char *path)\n{ return ___CAST(unsigned long, dlopen (path, JOLTFFI_RTLD_NOW)); }   /* sa-load-shared-object of #f */\n\nstatic char *joltffi_c_dlerror (void)\n{ return ___CAST(char *, dlerror ()); }\n\nstatic int joltffi_c_dlclose (unsigned long h)\n{ return dlclose (___CAST(void *, h)); }\n\n/* ---- memory ----------------------------------------------------------------- */\nstatic unsigned long joltffi_c_malloc (unsigned long n)\n{ return ___CAST(unsigned long, malloc (___CAST(size_t, n))); }\n\nstatic void joltffi_c_free (unsigned long p)\n{ free (___CAST(void *, p)); }\n\nstatic void joltffi_c_zero (unsigned long p, unsigned long n)\n{ memset (___CAST(void *, p), 0, ___CAST(size_t, n)); }\n\n/* foreign -> bytevector. Returns 0 ok, -1 bad count. */\nstatic int joltffi_c_bytes_to_bv (___SCMOBJ bv, unsigned long src, unsigned long n)\n{\n  ___SCMOBJ ___temp; /* the subtype test macros need a temp cell */\n  if (___HAS_TAG_AND_IS_NOT_DOUBLE (bv, ___tSUBTYPED, ___TB) && ___TESTSUBTYPE (bv, ___sU8VECTOR))\n    {\n      size_t len = ___U8VECTORSIZE (bv);\n      if (___CAST(unsigned long, len) < n)\n        return -1;\n      if (n > 0)\n        memcpy (___BODY_AS (bv, ___tU8VECTOR), ___CAST(void *, src), ___CAST(size_t, n));\n      return 0;\n    }\n  return -1;\n}\n\n/* bytevector -> foreign. Returns 0 ok, -1 bad count. */\nstatic int joltffi_c_bytes_from_bv (unsigned long dst, ___SCMOBJ bv, unsigned long n)\n{\n  ___SCMOBJ ___temp; /* the subtype test macros need a temp cell */\n  if (___HAS_TAG_AND_IS_NOT_DOUBLE (bv, ___tSUBTYPED, ___TB) && ___TESTSUBTYPE (bv, ___sU8VECTOR))\n    {\n      size_t len = ___U8VECTORSIZE (bv);\n      if (___CAST(unsigned long, len) < n)\n        return -1;\n      if (n > 0)\n        memcpy (___CAST(void *, dst), ___BODY_AS (bv, ___tU8VECTOR), ___CAST(size_t, n));\n      return 0;\n    }\n  return -1;\n}\n\n/* read one int (4 bytes) from a caller-allocated errno cell */\nstatic int joltffi_c_read_i32 (unsigned long p)\n{ int v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p), 4); return v; }\n\n/* ---- errno-capture control (NEGATIVE control only — NOT a shim) -------------\n   Captures AFTER an intervening clobber: the deliberately wrong order, so the\n   errno gate can prove its assertions DISTINGUISH capture order (the W1-r2\n   shape-G pattern). Never registered; never reached by adapter routing. */\nstatic int joltffi_c_ctrl_wrong_order (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout)\n{\n  int (*f) (void) = ___CAST(int (*)(void), fn);\n  int r;\n  r = f ();\n  errno = 4242;                     /* intervening clobber ... */\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = errno;  /* ... captured AFTER it */\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* ---- typed shims, one per registered ordinary shape ------------------------\n   Each takes the RESOLVED function address first (astra §2: shared across\n   symbols with identical ABI shapes), then the shape's declared arguments.\n   The cast through the exact function-pointer type is the ABI contract. */\n\n/* shape/s01-noarg-int — () -> int\n   producers: jolt_crypto_layout_version, jolt_parser_export_layout_version */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s01 (unsigned long fn)\n{\n  int (*f) (void) = ___CAST(int (*)(void), fn);\n  return f ();\n}\n\n/* shape/s01b-noarg-int32 — () -> int32\n   producers: jolt_file_layout_version, jolt_file_eintr, jolt_file_eexist */\nstatic int32_t joltffi_shim_s01b (unsigned long fn)\n{\n  int32_t (*f) (void) = ___CAST(int32_t (*)(void), fn);\n  return f ();\n}\n\n/* shape/s02-ptr-size-int — (void*, size_t) -> int\n   producer: jolt_crypto_provenance */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s02 (unsigned long fn, unsigned long a0, size_t a1)\n{\n  int (*f) (void *, size_t) = ___CAST(int (*)(void *, size_t), fn);\n  return f (___CAST(void *, a0), a1);\n}\n\n/* shape/s03-ptr-size-void — (void*, size_t) -> void\n   producers: jolt_crypto_cleanse */\nstatic void joltffi_shim_s03 (unsigned long fn, unsigned long a0, size_t a1)\n{\n  void (*f) (void *, size_t) = ___CAST(void (*)(void *, size_t), fn);\n  f (___CAST(void *, a0), a1);\n}\n\n/* shape/s12-s32be-get — (void*, int64) -> int32\n   producer: jolt_file_s32be_get */\nstatic int32_t joltffi_shim_s12 (unsigned long fn, unsigned long a0, int64_t a1)\n{\n  int32_t (*f) (void *, int64_t) = ___CAST(int32_t (*)(void *, int64_t), fn);\n  return f (___CAST(void *, a0), a1);\n}\n\n/* shape/s12b-s32be-put — (void*, int64, int32) -> void\n   producer: jolt_file_s32be_put */\nstatic void joltffi_shim_s12b (unsigned long fn, unsigned long a0, int64_t a1, int32_t a2)\n{\n  void (*f) (void *, int64_t, int32_t) = ___CAST(void (*)(void *, int64_t, int32_t), fn);\n  f (___CAST(void *, a0), a1, a2);\n}\n\n/* shape/s13-strerror — (int64, void*, int64) -> int64\n   producer: jolt_file_strerror */\nstatic int64_t joltffi_shim_s13 (unsigned long fn, int64_t a0, unsigned long a1, int64_t a2)\n{\n  int64_t (*f) (int64_t, void *, int64_t) = ___CAST(int64_t (*)(int64_t, void *, int64_t), fn);\n  return f (a0, ___CAST(void *, a1), a2);\n}\n\n/* shape/s18-ptr-free-ordinary — (void*) -> void\n   producers: jolt_parser_free, jolt_parser_worker_free, freeaddrinfo, freeifaddrs,\n   jolt_parser_worker_free (the Q3 open question rides on the BINDING's blocking\n   mark, not on this shape) */\nstatic void joltffi_shim_s18 (unsigned long fn, unsigned long a0)\n{\n  void (*f) (void *) = ___CAST(void (*)(void *), fn);\n  f (___CAST(void *, a0));\n}\n\n/* shape/s19-noarg-ptr — () -> void*\n   producers: jolt_parser_worker_new, TLS-client-method, BIO-s-mem */\nstatic unsigned long joltffi_shim_s19 (unsigned long fn)\n{\n  void *(*f) (void) = ___CAST(void *(*)(void), fn);\n  return ___CAST(unsigned long, f ());\n}\n\n/* shape/s20-errno-accessor — () -> void*\n   producers: __errno_location, __error, _errno, __errno (the ffi/errno read\n   path; the capture shims do NOT depend on it — they capture internally) */\nstatic unsigned long joltffi_shim_s20 (unsigned long fn)\n{\n  void *(*f) (void) = ___CAST(void *(*)(void), fn);\n  return ___CAST(unsigned long, f ());\n}\n\n/* shape/s21-int-string — (int) -> string (nullable char* return)\n   producer: strerror */\nstatic char *joltffi_shim_s21 (unsigned long fn, int a0)\n{\n  const char *(*f) (int) = ___CAST(const char *(*)(int), fn);\n  return ___CAST(char *, f (a0));\n}\n\n/* shape/s22-varargs-fcntl — (int, int, int) -> int, variadic after 2\n   producer: fcntl (io_poller). The target is invoked through a VARIADIC\n   function-pointer type so the call follows the platform's variadic ABI. */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s22 (unsigned long fn, int a0, int a1, int a2)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, int, ...) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, int, ...), fn);\n  return f (a0, a1, a2);\n}\n\n/* ---- capture shims: result + invocation-local errno, two-value return -------\n   Capture happens IMMEDIATELY after the target returns, before ANYTHING else\n   (the errout write below is adjacent to the capture; nothing between). */\n\n/* shape/s22b-varargs-fcntl-capture — (int, int, int) -> int, varargs after 2, capture\n   producer: fcntl (socket/native) */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s22b (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout, int a0, int a1, int a2)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, int, ...) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, int, ...), fn);\n  int r;\n  int saved;\n  r = f (a0, a1, a2);\n  saved = errno;                    /* capture IMMEDIATELY after the target */\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = saved;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* shape/s22c-varargs-ioctl-capture — (int, unsigned-long, void*) -> int, varargs after 2, capture\n   producer: ioctl (socket/native) */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s22c (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout, int a0, unsigned long a1, unsigned long a2)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, unsigned long, ...) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, unsigned long, ...), fn);\n  int r;\n  int saved;\n  r = f (a0, a1, ___CAST(void *, a2));\n  saved = errno;                    /* capture IMMEDIATELY after the target */\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = saved;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* shape/s23-capture-ordinary — (int, int, int, void*, void*) -> int, capture\n   producers: kevent (change arm), getsockopt */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s23 (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout, int a0, int a1, int a2, unsigned long a3, unsigned long a4)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, int, int, void *, void *) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, int, int, void *, void *), fn);\n  int r;\n  int saved;\n  r = f (a0, a1, a2, ___CAST(void *, a3), ___CAST(void *, a4));\n  saved = errno;\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = saved;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* shape/s26-socket-capture — (int, int, int) -> int, capture\n   producer: socket */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s26 (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout, int a0, int a1, int a2)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, int, int) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, int, int), fn);\n  int r;\n  int saved;\n  r = f (a0, a1, a2);\n  saved = errno;\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = saved;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* shape/s26b-bind-capture — (int, void*, int) -> int, capture\n   producer: bind */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s26b (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout, int a0, unsigned long a1, int a2)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, void *, int) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, void *, int), fn);\n  int r;\n  int saved;\n  r = f (a0, ___CAST(void *, a1), a2);\n  saved = errno;\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = saved;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* shape/s26c-listen-shutdown-capture — (int, int) -> int, capture\n   producers: listen, shutdown, close (io_poller arm) */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s26c (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout, int a0, int a1)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, int) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, int), fn);\n  int r;\n  int saved;\n  r = f (a0, a1);\n  saved = errno;\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = saved;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* shape/s26d-setsockopt-capture — (int, int, int, void*, int) -> int, capture\n   producer: setsockopt */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s26d (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout, int a0, int a1, int a2, unsigned long a3, int a4)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, int, int, void *, int) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, int, int, void *, int), fn);\n  int r;\n  int saved;\n  r = f (a0, a1, a2, ___CAST(void *, a3), a4);\n  saved = errno;\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = saved;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* shape/s26e-getsockname-capture — (int, void*, void*) -> int, capture\n   producers: getsockname, getpeername */\nstatic int joltffi_shim_s26e (unsigned long fn, unsigned long errout, int a0, unsigned long a1, unsigned long a2)\n{\n  int (*f) (int, void *, void *) = ___CAST(int (*)(int, void *, void *), fn);\n  int r;\n  int saved;\n  r = f (a0, ___CAST(void *, a1), ___CAST(void *, a2));\n  saved = errno;\n  if (errout != 0)\n    *___CAST(int *, ___CAST(void *, errout)) = saved;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* ---- typed data-plane access (sa-foreign-ref / sa-foreign-set!) -------------\n   memcpy-based so unaligned offsets behave; no errno semantics here — these are\n   plain readers, not call shims. Each returns through a caller-supplied\n   ___SCMOBJ only for the c-lambda wrapper below to keep ONE conversion shape;\n   the scalar wrappers return the value directly through the c-lambda result\n   conversion instead. */\n\nstatic signed char joltffi_c_ref_i8 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ signed char v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 1); return v; }\nstatic unsigned char joltffi_c_ref_u8 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ unsigned char v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 1); return v; }\nstatic short joltffi_c_ref_i16 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ short v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 2); return v; }\nstatic unsigned short joltffi_c_ref_u16 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ unsigned short v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 2); return v; }\nstatic int32_t joltffi_c_ref_i32 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ int32_t v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 4); return v; }\nstatic uint32_t joltffi_c_ref_u32 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ uint32_t v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 4); return v; }\nstatic int64_t joltffi_c_ref_i64 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ int64_t v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 8); return v; }\nstatic uint64_t joltffi_c_ref_u64 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ uint64_t v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 8); return v; }\nstatic float joltffi_c_ref_f32 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ float v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 4); return v; }\nstatic double joltffi_c_ref_f64 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off)\n{ double v; memcpy (&v, ___CAST(void *, p + off), 8); return v; }\n\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_i8 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, signed char v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 1); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_u8 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, unsigned char v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 1); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_i16 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, short v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 2); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_u16 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, unsigned short v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 2); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_i32 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, int32_t v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 4); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_u32 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, uint32_t v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 4); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_i64 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, int64_t v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 8); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_u64 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, uint64_t v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 8); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_f32 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, float v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 4); }\nstatic void joltffi_c_set_f64 (unsigned long p, unsigned long off, double v)\n{ memcpy (___CAST(void *, p + off), &v, 8); }\n\nJOLTFFI-C-BEGIN\n\n)\n\n;; ---- Scheme wrappers ----------------------------------------------------------\n;; One per shim: the c-lambda IS the conversion boundary (arguments convert at\n;; the call; the C body runs with the converted values). Capture wrappers take\n;; the errout cell address between fn and the declared args; the adapter\n;; allocates and frees the cell around each call.\n\n(define (joltffi-s01 fn) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_shim_s01\") fn))\n(define (joltffi-s01b fn) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long) int32 \"joltffi_shim_s01b\") fn))\n(define (joltffi-s02 fn a0 a1) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long size_t) int \"joltffi_shim_s02\") fn a0 a1))\n(define (joltffi-s03 fn a0 a1) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long size_t) void \"joltffi_shim_s03\") fn a0 a1))\n(define (joltffi-s12 fn a0 a1) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int64) int32 \"joltffi_shim_s12\") fn a0 a1))\n(define (joltffi-s12b fn a0 a1 a2) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int64 int32) void \"joltffi_shim_s12b\") fn a0 a1 a2))\n(define (joltffi-s13 fn a0 a1 a2) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long int64 unsigned-long int64) int64 \"joltffi_shim_s13\") fn a0 a1 a2))\n(define (joltffi-s18 fn a0) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) void \"joltffi_shim_s18\") fn a0))\n(define (joltffi-s19 fn) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long) unsigned-long \"joltffi_shim_s19\") fn))\n(define (joltffi-s20 fn) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long) unsigned-long \"joltffi_shim_s20\") fn))\n(define (joltffi-s21 fn a0) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long int) char-string \"joltffi_shim_s21\") fn a0))\n(define (joltffi-s22 fn a0 a1 a2) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long int int int) int \"joltffi_shim_s22\") fn a0 a1 a2))\n(define (joltffi-s22b fn errout a0 a1 a2) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int int int) int \"joltffi_shim_s22b\") fn errout a0 a1 a2))\n(define (joltffi-s22c fn errout a0 a1 a2) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int unsigned-long unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_shim_s22c\") fn errout a0 a1 a2))\n(define (joltffi-s23 fn errout a0 a1 a2 a3 a4) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int int int unsigned-long unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_shim_s23\") fn errout a0 a1 a2 a3 a4))\n(define (joltffi-s26 fn errout a0 a1 a2) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int int int) int \"joltffi_shim_s26\") fn errout a0 a1 a2))\n(define (joltffi-s26b fn errout a0 a1 a2) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int unsigned-long int) int \"joltffi_shim_s26b\") fn errout a0 a1 a2))\n(define (joltffi-s26c fn errout a0 a1) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int int) int \"joltffi_shim_s26c\") fn errout a0 a1))\n(define (joltffi-s26d fn errout a0 a1 a2 a3 a4) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int int int unsigned-long int) int \"joltffi_shim_s26d\") fn errout a0 a1 a2 a3 a4))\n(define (joltffi-s26e fn errout a0 a1 a2) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int unsigned-long unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_shim_s26e\") fn errout a0 a1 a2))\n\n;; ---- loader wrappers ----------------------------------------------------------\n(define (joltffi-dlopen path)\n  ((c-lambda (char-string) unsigned-long \"joltffi_c_dlopen\") path))\n(define (joltffi-dlopen-global path)\n  ((c-lambda (char-string) unsigned-long \"joltffi_c_dlopen_global\") path))\n(define (joltffi-dlsym handle name)\n  ((c-lambda (unsigned-long char-string) unsigned-long \"joltffi_c_dlsym\") handle name))\n(define (joltffi-dlsym-global name)\n  ((c-lambda (char-string) unsigned-long \"joltffi_c_dlsym_global\") name))\n(define (joltffi-dlerror)\n  ((c-lambda () char-string \"joltffi_c_dlerror\")))\n(define (joltffi-dlclose handle)\n  ((c-lambda (unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_c_dlclose\") handle))\n\n;; ---- memory wrappers ----------------------------------------------------------\n(define (joltffi-malloc n)\n  ((c-lambda (unsigned-long) unsigned-long \"joltffi_c_malloc\") n))\n(define (joltffi-free p)\n  ((c-lambda (unsigned-long) void \"joltffi_c_free\") p))\n(define (joltffi-zero p n)\n  ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) void \"joltffi_c_zero\") p n))\n;; 0 ok / -1 count-too-large: the adapter raises before dereferencing anything.\n(define (joltffi-bytes-to-bv! bv src n)\n  ((c-lambda (scheme-object unsigned-long unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_c_bytes_to_bv\") bv src n))\n(define (joltffi-bytes-from-bv! dst bv n)\n  ((c-lambda (unsigned-long scheme-object unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_c_bytes_from_bv\") dst bv n))\n(define (joltffi-read-i32 p)\n  ((c-lambda (unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_c_read_i32\") p))\n\n;; ---- the negative-control entry (gate-only; see the C comment above) ----------\n(define (joltffi-ctrl-wrong-order fn errout)\n  ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) int \"joltffi_c_ctrl_wrong_order\") fn errout))\n\n\n;; ---- typed data-plane wrappers (sa-foreign-ref / sa-foreign-set!) ------------\n(define (joltffi-ref-i8 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) int8 \"joltffi_c_ref_i8\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-u8 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) unsigned-int8 \"joltffi_c_ref_u8\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-i16 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) int16 \"joltffi_c_ref_i16\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-u16 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) unsigned-int16 \"joltffi_c_ref_u16\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-i32 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) int32 \"joltffi_c_ref_i32\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-u32 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) unsigned-int32 \"joltffi_c_ref_u32\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-i64 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) int64 \"joltffi_c_ref_i64\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-u64 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) unsigned-int64 \"joltffi_c_ref_u64\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-f32 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) float32 \"joltffi_c_ref_f32\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-ref-f64 addr off) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long) float64 \"joltffi_c_ref_f64\") addr off))\n(define (joltffi-set-i8! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int8) void \"joltffi_c_set_i8\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-u8! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long unsigned-int8) void \"joltffi_c_set_u8\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-i16! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int16) void \"joltffi_c_set_i16\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-u16! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long unsigned-int16) void \"joltffi_c_set_u16\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-i32! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int32) void \"joltffi_c_set_i32\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-u32! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long unsigned-int32) void \"joltffi_c_set_u32\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-i64! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long int64) void \"joltffi_c_set_i64\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-u64! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long unsigned-int64) void \"joltffi_c_set_u64\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-f32! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long float32) void \"joltffi_c_set_f32\") addr off v))\n(define (joltffi-set-f64! addr off v) ((c-lambda (unsigned-long unsigned-long float64) void \"joltffi_c_set_f64\") addr off v))\n\n;; ---- the shim registry ---------------------------------------------------------\n;; SHAPE IDENTITY = (argtypes ret) + capture?, exactly p1b-inv/shim-registry.edn's\n;; {:args :ret :capture-native-error} core (kind :procedure, non-blocking). The\n;; tokens are the CHEZ foreign types the compiler emits (ffi-type->chez /\n;; ffi-arg-type->chez); the shape line names the registry entry and its producers.\n;; Blocking, callable, aggregate, pointer-call and bare-varargs registry shapes\n;; are deliberately ABSENT: the adapter refuses them by mode before any lookup.\n(define joltffi-shims\n  ;; CONSTRUCTED, not quoted: the wrapper slot must be the procedure VALUE,\n  ;; not a symbol (the adapter applies it directly).\n  (list\n    ;; :shape/s01-noarg-int — jolt_crypto_layout_version, jolt_parser_export_layout_version\n    (list (list (list) (quote int)) #f joltffi-s01)\n    ;; :shape/s01b-noarg-int32 — jolt_file_layout_version/eintr/eexist\n    (list (list (list) (quote int32)) #f joltffi-s01b)\n    ;; :shape/s02-ptr-size-int — jolt_crypto_provenance\n    (list (list (list (quote void*) (quote size_t)) (quote int)) #f joltffi-s02)\n    ;; :shape/s03-ptr-size-void — jolt_crypto_cleanse\n    (list (list (list (quote void*) (quote size_t)) (quote void)) #f joltffi-s03)\n    ;; :shape/s12-s32be-get — jolt_file_s32be_get\n    (list (list (list (quote void*) (quote integer-64)) (quote int32)) #f joltffi-s12)\n    ;; :shape/s12b-s32be-put — jolt_file_s32be_put\n    (list (list (list (quote void*) (quote integer-64) (quote int32)) (quote void)) #f joltffi-s12b)\n    ;; :shape/s13-strerror — jolt_file_strerror\n    (list (list (list (quote integer-64) (quote void*) (quote integer-64)) (quote integer-64)) #f joltffi-s13)\n    ;; :shape/s18-ptr-free-ordinary — jolt_parser_free/worker_free, freeaddrinfo, freeifaddrs\n    (list (list (list (quote void*)) (quote void)) #f joltffi-s18)\n    ;; :shape/s19-noarg-ptr — jolt_parser_worker_new, TLS-client-method, BIO-s-mem\n    (list (list (list) (quote void*)) #f joltffi-s19)\n    ;; :shape/s20-errno-accessor — __errno_location/__error/_errno/__errno\n    (list (list (list) (quote void*)) #f joltffi-s20)\n    ;; :shape/s21-int-string — strerror\n    (list (list (list (quote int)) (quote string)) #f joltffi-s21)\n    ;; :shape/s22-varargs-fcntl — fcntl (io_poller), declared tail\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote int) (quote int)) (quote int)) #f joltffi-s22)\n    ;; :shape/s22b-varargs-fcntl-capture — fcntl (socket/native)\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote int) (quote int)) (quote int)) #t joltffi-s22b)\n    ;; :shape/s22c-varargs-ioctl-capture — ioctl (socket/native)\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote unsigned-long) (quote void*)) (quote int)) #t joltffi-s22c)\n    ;; :shape/s23-capture-ordinary — kevent change arm, getsockopt\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote int) (quote int) (quote void*) (quote void*)) (quote int)) #t joltffi-s23)\n    ;; :shape/s26-socket-capture — socket\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote int) (quote int)) (quote int)) #t joltffi-s26)\n    ;; :shape/s26b-bind-capture — bind\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote void*) (quote int)) (quote int)) #t joltffi-s26b)\n    ;; :shape/s26c-listen-shutdown-capture — listen, shutdown, close (io_poller arm)\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote int)) (quote int)) #t joltffi-s26c)\n    ;; :shape/s26d-setsockopt-capture — setsockopt\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote int) (quote int) (quote void*) (quote int)) (quote int)) #t joltffi-s26d)\n    ;; :shape/s26e-getsockname-capture — getsockname, getpeername\n    (list (list (list (quote int) (quote void*) (quote void*)) (quote int)) #t joltffi-s26e)))\n\n(define (joltffi-shim-lookup argtypes ret capture?)\n  (let loop ((es joltffi-shims))\n    (if (null? es)\n        #f\n        (let ((e (car es)))\n          (if (and (equal? argtypes (car (car e)))\n                   (equal? ret (cadr (car e)))\n                   (eq? capture? (cadr e)))\n              (car (cdr (cdr e)))\n              (loop (cdr es)))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; cat host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-abi.ss'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; cat host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-abi.ss'","aggregated_output":";; host-ffi.ss — the jolt.ffi host-owned surface for the GAMBIT target\n;; (P1b-stage1). On Chez these vars live in host/chez/java/ffi.ss, which the\n;; gambit boot manifest excludes — without this file every jolt.ffi name was an\n;; unbound global (the same shape the host-vars.ss degradation fixed for\n;; clojure.core). Stage-1 binds the memory/loader/errno surface the qualified\n;; tier backs (the adapter rows + the native bridge), implements what the\n;; stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj public functions call into, and binds EVERYTHING ELSE to\n;; a message-carrying refusal — nothing stays unbound, nothing pretends.\n;;\n;; Loaded after host-vars.ss, before the seed image (same rule: these bindings\n;; are the last word for the names the excluded ffi.ss owned). Requires the\n;; booted kernel (jolt-nil, def-var!, jolt-hash-map, make-pvec, ...) — this\n;; file is boot-world only; the sa-* tier it leans on also loads standalone\n;; under gambitcheck without it.\n\n;; ---- emitted-text helpers the compiler's ordinary-call wrappers lean on -----\n;; The :string conversions invert per direction like the Chez pair; jolt truthy\n;; rule for :bool; jfloat unboxing for :float/:double. jolt-ffi-c->string maps\n;; the adapter's NULL-string #f to jolt-nil (values.ss's sentinel — bound by\n;; the time any of these RUN; the define only closes over it).\n(define (jolt-ffi-string->c x)\n  (cond ((string? x) x)\n        ((jolt-nil? x) #f)                ; nil IS NULL, in both directions\n        (else (throw-jvm 'IllegalArgumentException\n                         (string-append \"jolt.ffi: :string got \" (jolt-pr-str x)\n                                        \" — NULL is spelled nil\")))))\n(define (jolt-ffi-c->string x) (if x x jolt-nil))\n(define (jolt-ffi-bool->c v) (if (or (jolt-nil? v) (eq? v #f)) 0 1))\n(define (jolt-ffi-c->bool raw) (not (eqv? (jnum->exact raw) 0)))\n(define (jolt-ffi-float->c x) (if (jfloat? x) (jfloat-fl x) x))\n\n;; A :string ARGUMENT travels as u8* on Chez (an immobile copy). Gambit has no\n;; immobile allocation and the stage-1 bridge carries no :string-argument shape\n;; (the registry has none), so this raises BEFORE the unbound-identifier fate\n;; the pre-stage1 boot would have dealt: the adapter's shape validation refuses\n;; :string arguments, and this helper — which the emitted wrapper evaluates\n;; first — refuses for any path that might reach it out of order.\n(define (jolt-ffi-string-arg x)\n  (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException\n             \"jolt.ffi: :string arguments are unsupported on the gambit target — no immobile allocation behind the stage-1 bridge\"))\n\n;; The emitted call keeps string copies live until C returns; identity here,\n;; because nothing that evaluates it can have a live foreign reference (the\n;; string-arg path above refuses first). Bound so the emitted TEXT never dies\n;; on an unbound identifier at load.\n(define (keep-live x) x)\n\n;; jolt-ffi-function-pointer: the pointer-call null guard (backend\n;; ffi-pointer-procedure-expr emits it ahead of each call). Pointer-call\n;; bindings are compile-time-refused on :gambit, so this only guards paths that\n;; hand a raw address to the ordinary tier.\n(define (jolt-ffi-function-pointer ptr)\n  (let ((address (if (jolt-nil? ptr) 0 (jnum->exact ptr))))\n    (if (eqv? address 0)\n        (throw-jvm 'NullPointerException \"jolt.ffi: null C function pointer\")\n        address)))\n\n;; jolt-ffi-dlsym-native (the compiler's emitted scoped probe) is defined in\n;; the adapter itself — it must exist in every world the emitted text loads in,\n;; including the adapter-only gambitcheck unit.\n\n;; ---- foreign memory over the adapter tier -------------------------------------\n;; alloc returns the ADDRESS (an exact integer); read/write take the type\n;; keyword and the offset LAST (the babashka.ffi order the stdlib wrapper\n;; keeps). Type keywords arrive as jolt keywords; the stdlib resolves layouts\n;; and places before calling, so these see scalars only.\n(define (joltffi-keyword-name kw)\n  (if (keyword-t? kw) (keyword-t-name kw) kw))\n\n(define (joltffi-type->chez kw)\n  (let ((n (joltffi-keyword-name kw)))\n    (cond\n      ((string=? n \"int\") 'int)\n      ((string=? n \"uint\") 'unsigned-int)\n      ((or (string=? n \"int8\") (string=? n \"i8\")) 'integer-8)\n      ((or (string=? n \"uint8\") (string=? n \"u8\") (string=? n \"byte\")) 'unsigned-8)\n      ((or (string=? n \"int16\") (string=? n \"short\")) 'integer-16)\n      ((or (string=? n \"uint16\") (string=? n \"ushort\")) 'unsigned-16)\n      ((string=? n \"int32\") 'integer-32)\n      ((string=? n \"uint32\") 'unsigned-32)\n      ((string=? n \"long\") 'long)\n      ((string=? n \"ulong\") 'unsigned-long)\n      ((string=? n \"int64\") 'integer-64)\n      ((string=? n \"uint64\") 'unsigned-64)\n      ((string=? n \"size_t\") 'size_t)\n      ((string=? n \"ssize_t\") 'ssize_t)\n      ((string=? n \"iptr\") 'iptr)\n      ((string=? n \"uptr\") 'uptr)\n      ((string=? n \"double\") 'double)\n      ((string=? n \"float\") 'float)\n      ((or (string=? n \"pointer\") (string=? n \"void*\")) 'void*)\n      ((string=? n \"char\") 'char)\n      ((string=? n \"bool\") 'jolt-bool)   ; one byte wide; converted at the boundary\n      ((string=? n \"string\") 'string)\n      ((string=? n \"void\") 'void)\n      (else (error #f (string-append \"jolt.ffi: unknown foreign type :\" n))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-sizeof-chez ct) (sa-foreign-sizeof ct))\n\n(define (joltffi-read ptr ty off)\n  (let ((ct (joltffi-type->chez ty)))\n    (cond\n      ((eq? ct 'jolt-bool)\n       (jolt-ffi-c->bool (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-8 (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))\n      ((eq? ct 'float)\n       (make-jfloat (sa-foreign-ref 'float (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))\n      ((eq? ct 'string)\n       (jolt-ffi-c->string (joltffi-read-string (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))\n      (else (sa-foreign-ref ct (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off))))))\n\n;; a NUL-terminated C string at ptr -> string (adapter-level #f for a NULL\n;; first byte means the caller spelled NULL with 0 — see ptr->string). One bulk\n;; move of the whole window, then a Scheme-side scan; the stdlib's ptr->string\n;; and the :string __read ride on this.\n(define (joltffi-read-string ptr off)\n  (let* ((p (jnum->exact ptr))\n         (o (jnum->exact off))\n         (bv (make-bytevector 257 0)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! (+ p o) bv 256)\n    (let find ((k 0))\n      (cond\n        ((= k 256) #f)                    ; no terminator in the window — refuse\n        ((= (bytevector-u8-ref bv k) 0)\n         (guard (e (#t (list->string (map integer->char\n                                      (bytevector->u8-list (subu8vector bv 0 k))))))\n           (utf8->string (subu8vector bv 0 k))))\n        (else (find (+ k 1)))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-write ptr ty val off)\n  (let ((ct (joltffi-type->chez ty)))\n    (cond\n      ((eq? ct 'jolt-bool)\n       (sa-foreign-set! 'unsigned-8 (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off) (jolt-ffi-bool->c val)))\n      ((memq ct '(float double))\n       (sa-foreign-set! ct (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off) (jolt-ffi-float->c val)))\n      ((eq? ct 'string)\n       (let ((s (jolt-ffi-string->c val)))\n         (if s\n             (let ((bv (string->utf8 s)))\n               (sa-foreign-bytes-set! (jnum->exact ptr) bv (bytevector-length bv))\n               (let ((z (make-bytevector 1 0)))\n                 (sa-foreign-bytes-set! (+ (jnum->exact ptr) (bytevector-length bv)) z 1))\n               jolt-nil)\n             jolt-nil)))\n      (else (sa-foreign-set! ct (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact off) val)))\n    jolt-nil))\n\n;; ---- the size bookkeeping ------------------------------------------------------\n;; jolt.ffi/size answers what jolt was TOLD — arena allocations, segments. One\n;; table, address -> size, guarded by the adapter's loader mutex's sibling.\n(define joltffi-sizes-mu (make-mutex))\n(define joltffi-sizes (make-hashtable eqv? eqv?))\n(define (joltffi-remember-size! ptr n)\n  (jwm-call joltffi-sizes-mu (lambda () (hashtable-set! joltffi-sizes (jnum->exact ptr) (jnum->exact n))))\n  jolt-nil)\n(define (joltffi-forget-sizes!)\n  (jwm-call joltffi-sizes-mu\n    (lambda ()\n      (let ((ks (vector->list (hashtable-keys joltffi-sizes))))\n        (for-each (lambda (k) (hashtable-delete! joltffi-sizes k)) ks))))\n  jolt-nil)\n(define (joltffi-recorded-size ptr)\n  (jwm-call joltffi-sizes-mu (lambda () (hashtable-ref joltffi-sizes (jnum->exact ptr) 0))))\n\n;; ---- alloc/free ------------------------------------------------------------------\n(define (joltffi-alloc nbytes)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact nbytes))\n         (p (sa-foreign-alloc n)))\n    (when (> n 0) (joltffi-remember-size! p n))\n    p))\n(define (joltffi-calloc nbytes)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact nbytes))\n         (p (sa-foreign-alloc n)))\n    (when (> n 0)\n      (sa-foreign-zero! p n)\n      (joltffi-remember-size! p n))\n    p))\n(define (joltffi-free ptr) (sa-foreign-free (jnum->exact ptr)) jolt-nil)\n(define (joltffi-copy src dst n)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact n)) (bv (make-bytevector n)))\n    (when (> n 0)\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! (jnum->exact src) bv n)\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-set! (jnum->exact dst) bv n))\n    jolt-nil))\n(define (joltffi-null? ptr) (and (number? ptr) (= (jnum->exact ptr) 0)))\n(define joltffi-null 0)\n\n;; read/write take (ptr ty [off]) — the babashka.ffi offset-last order\n(define joltffi-read-fn\n  (case-lambda ((ptr ty) (joltffi-read ptr ty 0))\n               ((ptr ty off) (joltffi-read ptr ty off))))\n(define joltffi-write-fn\n  (case-lambda ((ptr ty val) (joltffi-write ptr ty val 0))\n               ((ptr ty val off) (joltffi-write ptr ty val off))))\n\n;; ---- buffer I/O (known length) ---------------------------------------------------\n(define (joltffi-read-bytes ptr n)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact n)) (p (jnum->exact ptr)) (bv (make-bytevector n)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! p bv n)\n    (guard (e (#t (list->string (map integer->char (bytevector->u8-list bv)))))\n      (utf8->string bv))))\n(define (joltffi-write-bytes ptr s)\n  (let* ((bv (string->utf8 s)) (n (bytevector-length bv)) (p (jnum->exact ptr)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-set! p bv n)\n    n))\n\n;; ptr->string: NUL-terminated C string at ptr (NULL/0 -> nil)\n(define (joltffi-ptr->string p)\n  (if (joltffi-null? p)\n      jolt-nil\n      (let ((s (joltffi-read-string p 0)))\n        (if s s jolt-nil))))\n(define (joltffi-string->ptr s)\n  (let* ((bv (string->utf8 (jolt-ffi-string->c s)))\n         (n (bytevector-length bv))\n         (p (sa-foreign-alloc (+ n 1))))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-set! p bv n)\n    (let ((z (make-bytevector 1 0)))\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-set! (+ p n) z 1))\n    (joltffi-remember-size! p (+ n 1))\n    p))\n(define (joltffi-utf8-length s) (bytevector-length (string->utf8 s)))\n\n;; ---- loader surface ---------------------------------------------------------------\n;; load-library: the Chez semantics minus Windows/Termux arms — nil keeps the\n;; boot's process handle; a per-OS map selects this platform's entry; anything\n;; else is one name or an ORDERED candidate list, tried in order, with the\n;; loader's own reason preserved on failure. Answers {:path \"<loaded>\"} or nil.\n(define (joltffi-library-map path)\n  (jolt-hash-map (jolt-keyword \"path\") path))\n\n(define (joltffi-candidate-list name)\n  (if (or (pvec? name) (jolt-seq? name))\n      (map (lambda (c) (if (string? c) c (jolt-str-render-one c))) (seq->list (jolt-seq name)))\n      (list (jolt-str-render-one name))))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-failure-note cands)\n  (let loop ((cs cands) (acc '()))\n    (if (null? cs)\n        (and (pair? acc)\n             (let join ((xs (reverse acc)) (out \"\"))\n               (if (null? xs)\n                   out\n                   (join (cdr xs) (if (string=? out \"\") (car xs)\n                                      (string-append out \"; \" (car xs)))))))\n        (let* ((cand (car cs))\n               (exists (guard (e (#t #f)) (file-exists? cand)))\n               (why (jwm-call joltffi-native-mu\n                      (lambda () (hashtable-ref joltffi-native-failures cand #f)))))\n          (loop (cdr cs)\n                (if exists\n                    (cons (string-append cand \" is there but did not load\"\n                                         (if why (string-append \": \" why) \"\"))\n                          acc)\n                    acc))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-join-candidates cands sep)\n  (let loop ((cs cands) (out \"\"))\n    (cond ((null? cs) out)\n          ((null? (cdr cs)) (string-append out (car cs)))\n          (else (loop (cdr cs) (string-append out (car cs) sep))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-candidates cands)\n  (let loop ((cs cands))\n    (cond\n      ((null? cs)\n       (jolt-throw (jolt-ex-info\n                     (string-append \"jolt.ffi/load-library: cannot load \"\n                                    (if (null? (cdr cands)) \"\" \"any of \")\n                                    (joltffi-join-candidates cands \", \")\n                                    (let ((note (joltffi-load-failure-note cands)))\n                                      (if note (string-append \" — \" note) \"\")))\n                     (jolt-hash-map (jolt-keyword \"candidates\")\n                                    (make-pvec (list->vector cands))))))\n      ((joltffi-load-native (car cs)) (car cs))\n      (else (loop (cdr cs))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-library . args)\n  (cond\n    ((or (null? args) (jolt-nil? (car args)))\n     jolt-nil)\n    ((jolt-map? (car args))\n     (let* ((spec (car args))\n            (key \"darwin\")             ; sa-os-family degrades to 'linux on this\n                                       ; target; darwin's entry is what a macOS leg\n                                       ; declared — the map's key set is platform\n                                       ; data, the LEG decides (see findings)\n            (name (jolt-get-dispatch spec (jolt-keyword \"darwin\") jolt-nil)))\n       (when (jolt-nil? name)\n         (jolt-throw (jolt-ex-info\n                       (string-append \"jolt.ffi/load-library: no :darwin entry in the per-OS spec (gambit target)\")\n                       spec)))\n       (joltffi-library-map (joltffi-load-candidates (joltffi-candidate-list name)))))\n    (else (joltffi-library-map (joltffi-load-candidates (joltffi-candidate-list (car args)))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-loaded? name)\n  (if (joltffi-load-native name) #t #f))\n\n(define (joltffi-system-library-candidates n)\n  (list (string-append \"lib\" n \".dylib\") (string-append n \".dylib\")))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-system-library name)\n  (joltffi-library-map\n   (joltffi-load-candidates\n    (joltffi-system-library-candidates (if (string? name) name (jolt-str-render-one name))))))\n\n(define joltffi-find-symbol\n  (case-lambda\n    ((sym)\n     (let* ((n (if (string? sym) sym (jolt-str-render-one sym)))\n            (a (joltffi-dlsym-loaded n)))\n       (cond (a a)\n             ((guard (e (#t #f)) (sa-foreign-entry? n)) (sa-foreign-entry-address n))\n             (else jolt-nil))))\n    ((lib sym)\n     (if (jolt-nil? lib)\n         (joltffi-find-symbol sym)\n         (let* ((n (if (string? sym) sym (jolt-str-render-one sym)))\n                (path (and (jolt-map? lib)\n                           (jolt-get-dispatch lib (jolt-keyword \"path\") jolt-nil)))\n                (h (and (string? path) (joltffi-library-handle path))))\n           (unless h\n             (jolt-throw (jolt-ex-info\n                           \"jolt.ffi/find-symbol: no handle for this library — pass the map load-library answered for it\"\n                           (jolt-hash-map (jolt-keyword \"library\") lib))))\n           (let ((a (joltffi-dlsym h n)))\n             (if (and a (not (= a 0))) a jolt-nil)))))))\n\n;; the dlopen handle a load-library of PATH registered, or #f\n(define (joltffi-library-handle path)\n  (let loop ((hs joltffi-native-handles))\n    (cond ((null? hs) #f)\n          ((string=? (caar hs) path) (cdar hs))\n          (else (loop (cdr hs))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-defining-libraries sym)\n  (make-pvec\n   (list->vector\n    (map car (joltffi-definers (if (string? sym) sym (jolt-str-render-one sym)))))))\n\n(define (joltffi-load-failure-note-var cands)\n  (joltffi-load-failure-note (if (list? cands) cands (list cands))))\n\n;; ---- refusing rows (message-carrying; the capability stays unqualified) -------\n(define (joltffi-refuse-fn name reason)\n  (lambda args\n    (jolt-throw\n     (jolt-host-throwable\n      \"java.lang.UnsupportedOperationException\"\n      (string-append \"jolt.ffi/\" name \" is unsupported on the gambit target: \" reason)))))\n\n(define (joltffi-refuse-var! name reason)\n  (def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" name (joltffi-refuse-fn name reason)))\n\n;; byte-array moves need the jolt-array runtime (natives-array.ss is excluded\n;; from this boot's manifest) — the SA tier's bulk copies ARE qualified; this\n;; row is the jolt-array half.\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"read-array\" \"byte-array moves need the jolt-array runtime, which this boot's manifest excludes\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"read-into!\" \"byte-array moves need the jolt-array runtime, which this boot's manifest excludes\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"write-array\" \"byte-array moves need the jolt-array runtime, which this boot's manifest excludes\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__read-array\" \"byte-array moves need the jolt-array runtime, which this boot's manifest excludes\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__write-array\" \"byte-array moves need the jolt-array runtime, which this boot's manifest excludes\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__read-into!\" \"byte-array moves need the jolt-array runtime, which this boot's manifest excludes\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__read-into-typed!\" \"typed-array views over foreign memory are not in the stage-1 registry\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__write-array-typed\" \"typed-array views over foreign memory are not in the stage-1 registry\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__byte-buffer\" \"direct ByteBuffers over foreign memory are not in the stage-1 registry\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"free-callable\" \"foreign callables are unqualified (no arm64/x86_64 trampoline generator in stock Gambit 4.9.8)\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"register-export\" \"foreign callables and AOT are unqualified on the gambit target\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__arena-callback\" \"foreign callables are unqualified (no arm64/x86_64 trampoline generator in stock Gambit 4.9.8)\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__auto-guard!\" \"auto arenas (collector-reclaimed) need guardians over foreign memory, unqualified in stage-1\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__auto-reclaimed\" \"auto arenas (collector-reclaimed) need guardians over foreign memory, unqualified in stage-1\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__gc-stall-reporter!\" \"the GC stall watch has no hook on this target (sa-gc-install-stall-watch! answers #f)\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"stack-args-correct?\" \"the Chez #1091 stack-args probe is Chez-ABI-only and is not re-probed under the Gambit ABI in stage-1\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"load-native\" \"superseded by load-library on this target (the adapter's scoped loader is the single dlopen path)\")\n\n;; ---- implemented rows -----------------------------------------------------------\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"load-library\" joltffi-load-library)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"loaded?\" joltffi-loaded?)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"load-system-library\" joltffi-load-system-library)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"system-library-candidates\"\n  (lambda (n) (make-pvec (list->vector (joltffi-system-library-candidates n)))))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"load-failure-note\" joltffi-load-failure-note-var)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"find-symbol\" joltffi-find-symbol)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"dlsym-native\" jolt-ffi-dlsym-native)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"defining-libraries\" joltffi-defining-libraries)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"alloc\" joltffi-alloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"free\" joltffi-free)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__alloc\" joltffi-alloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__free\" joltffi-free)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__calloc\" joltffi-calloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"read\" joltffi-read-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"write\" joltffi-write-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__read\" joltffi-read-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__write\" joltffi-write-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"copy\" joltffi-copy)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__copy\" joltffi-copy)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"sizeof\" (lambda (ty) (joltffi-sizeof-chez (joltffi-type->chez ty))))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__sizeof\" (lambda (ty) (joltffi-sizeof-chez (joltffi-type->chez ty))))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__size\" joltffi-recorded-size)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__remember-size!\" joltffi-remember-size!)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__forget-sizes!\" joltffi-forget-sizes!)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"read-bytes\" joltffi-read-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"write-bytes\" joltffi-write-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__read-bytes\" joltffi-read-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__write-bytes\" joltffi-write-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"null?\" (lambda (p) (if (joltffi-null? p) #t #f)))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"null\" joltffi-null)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"ptr->string\" joltffi-ptr->string)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"string->ptr\" joltffi-string->ptr)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__string->ptr\" joltffi-string->ptr)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__utf8-length\" joltffi-utf8-length)\n;; gambitffi-abi.ss — the gambitffi-abi gate: scalar widths, pointers, byte\n;; copies, return conversion, REGISTERED signatures, symbol parity.\n;;\n;; Run via `make gambitffi-abi` (which builds the bridge + fixtures first, runs\n;; this under an external watchdog, from the repo root). Every row asserts\n;; state-derived behavior against the fixture library's targets — nothing\n;; prints unconditionally.\n\n(##include \"ffi-harness.ss\")\n\n;; ---- prerequisites: the qualified tier is the bridge + fixture ---------------\n\n;; Fail-closed note: with the bridge absent (a bypassed prerequisite), EVERY row\n;; below raises the documented \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target: the\n;; stage-1 native bridge is not built\" message instead of passing — the gate\n;; never skips. The bridge is loaded here; that is what the gate qualifies.\n(let ((pre (guard (e (#t (condition-message e)))\n             (sa-load-shared-object ffi-fixture-path)\n             \"NO-RAISE\")))\n  (if (string=? pre \"NO-RAISE\")\n      (printf \"  ok     fixture library loaded through the adapter loader\\n\")\n      (begin (printf \"  FAIL   fixture load raised: ~s\\n\" pre)\n             (set! ffi-failures (+ ffi-failures 1))\n             (ffi-gate-finish \"gambitffi-abi\"))))\n\n;; ---- scalar widths ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(printf \"== scalar widths (exact, LP64 legs) ==\\n\")\n(ffi-check \"sizeof int\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'int) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-int\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-int) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof integer-8\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'integer-8) 1)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-8\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-8) 1)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof integer-16\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'integer-16) 2)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-16\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-16) 2)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof integer-32\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'integer-32) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-32\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-32) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof integer-64\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'integer-64) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-64\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-64) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof size_t\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'size_t) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof ssize_t\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'ssize_t) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof long\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'long) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-long\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-long) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof iptr\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'iptr) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof uptr\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'uptr) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof double\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'double) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof float\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'float) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof void*\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'void*) 8)\n(ffi-check-raise-message \"sizeof unknown type refuses\"\n                         (lambda () (sa-foreign-sizeof 'jolt-agg)) \"no size for foreign type\")\n\n;; ---- pointers, alloc/free/zero, byte copies -----------------------------------\n\n(printf \"== pointers + bulk byte copies ==\\n\")\n(let ((p (sa-foreign-alloc 64)))\n  (ffi-check-true \"alloc answers a nonzero address\" (and (exact-integer? p) (> p 0)))\n  (sa-foreign-zero! p 64)\n  (let ((bv (make-u8vector 64 255)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! p bv 64)\n    (ffi-check \"zero! + bytes-ref! all-zero\" (u8vector->list bv)\n               (make-list 64 0)))\n  ;; binary-faithful moves: NUL and 0xff included\n  (let ((bv (u8vector 0 1 #xff 0 66 0 0 0)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-set! p bv 8)\n    (let ((out (make-u8vector 8 9)))\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! p out 8)\n      (ffi-check \"bytes-set!/ref! round-trip (NUL + 0xff)\" (u8vector->list out)\n                 '(0 1 #xff 0 66 0 0 0))))\n  ;; unaligned offset write/read through the typed accessors\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'integer-32 p 5 -7)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! unaligned i32\" (sa-foreign-ref 'integer-32 p 5) -7)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'unsigned-64 p 24 9223372036854775807)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! u64 max\" (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-64 p 24) 9223372036854775807)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'integer-64 p 32 -9007199254740993)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! i64 past double range\" (sa-foreign-ref 'integer-64 p 32) -9007199254740993)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'double p 40 1.5)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! double\" (sa-foreign-ref 'double p 40) 1.5)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'float p 48 0.25)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! float (single precision)\" (sa-foreign-ref 'float p 48) 0.25)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'integer-8 p 50 -128)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! i8\" (sa-foreign-ref 'integer-8 p 50) -128)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'unsigned-16 p 52 65535)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! u16\" (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-16 p 52) 65535)\n  (sa-foreign-free p)\n  (printf \"  ok     free answered\\n\"))\n(ffi-check-raise-message \"bytes-ref! past the bytevector refuses\"\n                         (lambda () (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! 1 (make-u8vector 2 0) 3))\n                         \"bulk copy count exceeds the bytevector\")\n\n;; ---- registered signatures through the fixture library ------------------------\n\n(printf \"== registered signatures (fixture targets through the tier) ==\\n\")\n;; Every fixture call below goes through the COMPILER-EMITTED scoped-branch\n;; shape verbatim: (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"sym\"))) ... (sa-foreign-procedure a sig ...)).\n;; By-name construction is exercised separately against process-global symbols\n;; (the by-name fallback's Chez semantics: RTLD_LOCAL scoped libs are invisible\n;; to it — that isolation is the scoped-shadows-global guarantee).\n(let ((clobber (sa-foreign-alloc 32)))\n  ;; pointers are exact integers here: a foreign buffer the fixtures write\n  ;; into, read back through the bulk copies (the copy-in/copy-out design)\n  (sa-foreign-zero! clobber 32)\n  ;; s01: () -> int\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\")))\n    (ffi-check-true \"scoped resolution finds the fixture symbol\" (and a (not (= a 0))))\n    (ffi-check \"s01 () -> int\" ((sa-foreign-procedure a () int)) 42))\n  ;; s01b: () -> int32\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eintr\")))\n    (let ((probe (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eintr_c\")))\n      (ffi-check \"s01b () -> int32 matches its own probe\"\n                 ((sa-foreign-procedure a () int32))\n                 ((sa-foreign-procedure probe () int)))))\n  ;; s02: (void*, size_t) -> int\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_provenance\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a (void* size_t) int)))\n      (ffi-check \"s02 null buffer refusal\" (f 0 0) -1)\n      (ffi-check \"s02 provenance text\"\n                 (let ((n (f clobber 16)))\n                   (let ((out (make-u8vector n)))\n                     (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! clobber out n)\n                     (list n (u8vector->list out))))\n                 (list 15 (map char->integer (string->list \"joltffi-fixture\"))))))\n  ;; s03: (void*, size_t) -> void\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_cleanse\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a (void* size_t) void)))\n      (sa-foreign-set! 'integer-32 clobber 0 305419896)\n      (f clobber 4)\n      (ffi-check \"s03 cleanse zeroed the range\" (sa-foreign-ref 'integer-32 clobber 0) 0)))\n  ;; s12/s12b: BE field get/put\n  (let ((a-get (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_s32be_get\"))\n        (a-put (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_s32be_put\")))\n    (let ((put (sa-foreign-procedure a-put (void* integer-64 int32) void))\n          (get (sa-foreign-procedure a-get (void* integer-64) int32)))\n      (put clobber 4 -2023406815)\n      (ffi-check \"s12b/s12 BE round-trip\" (get clobber 4) -2023406815)))\n  ;; s13: (int64, void*, int64) -> int64\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_strerror\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a (integer-64 void* integer-64) integer-64)))\n      (let ((n (f 3 clobber 16)))\n        (let ((out (make-u8vector n)))\n          (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! clobber out n)\n          (ffi-check \"s13 error-text writer\" (utf8->string out) \"err-3\")))))\n  ;; s19/s18: () -> void* then (void*) -> void\n  (let ((a-new (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_worker_new\"))\n        (a-free (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_free\")))\n    (let ((new (sa-foreign-procedure a-new () void*))\n          (free (sa-foreign-procedure a-free (void*) void)))\n      (let ((w (new)))\n        (ffi-check-true \"s19 answers a nonzero pointer\" (and (exact-integer? w) (> w 0)))\n        (begin (free w) #t)\n        (ffi-check-true \"s18 free answered (a second free of the same block is malloc corruption, not a witness)\" #t))))\n  ;; s20: () -> void* (errno accessor shape)\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_errno_location\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a () void*)))\n      (ffi-check-true \"s20 errno-location answers a nonzero pointer\"\n                      (and (exact-integer? (f)) (> (f) 0)))))\n  ;; s21: (int) -> string (NULL result must surface as #f at this layer)\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_errtext\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a (int) string)))\n      (ffi-check \"s21 string result\" (f 1) \"joltffi-error-one\")\n      (ffi-check \"s21 NULL string result\" (f 0) #f)))\n  ;; s22: declared-tail varargs (int, int, int) -> int\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_vfcntl\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure (__varargs_after 2) a (int int int) int)))\n      (ffi-check \"s22 varargs (2 fixed + 1 tail)\" (f 10 3 100) 113)))\n  ;; by-name construction against PROCESS-GLOBAL symbols (libc): strerror\n  ;; through the registered s21 shape and __error through s20 — the stdlib's\n  ;; own errno-accessor spellings. RTLD_LOCAL scoped libs stay invisible to\n  ;; this path by design (tested in the load-failure gate).\n  (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure \"strerror\" (int) string)))\n    (ffi-check-true \"by-name process-global resolution (strerror, s21)\" (string? (f 1)))\n    (ffi-check-true \"by-name errno accessor (__error, s20)\"\n                    (> ((sa-foreign-procedure \"__error\" () void*)) 0)))\n  ;; symbol parity\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry? fixture symbol\" (sa-foreign-entry? \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\"))\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry? libc symbol\" (sa-foreign-entry? \"malloc\"))\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry? unknown symbol answers #f\"\n                  (not (sa-foreign-entry? \"joltffi_fx_absent_symbol\")))\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry-address matches the scoped resolution\"\n                  (= (sa-foreign-entry-address \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\")\n                     (joltffi-dlsym-loaded \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\")))\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry-address raises for unknown\"\n                  (not (guard (e (#t #f)) (sa-foreign-entry-address \"joltffi_fx_absent_symbol\") #t)))\n  (sa-foreign-free clobber))\n\n(printf \"== native-error capture (ordinary, registered) ==\\n\")\n(let ((clobber (sa-foreign-alloc 32)))\n  (sa-foreign-zero! clobber 32)\n  ;; the errno pre-set target: an s03-shaped call that sets errno=7777 after\n  ;; zeroing, so every \"success preserves the caller's errno\" row below reads a\n  ;; DETERMINISTIC pre-existing value (the target's success path touches no\n  ;; errno, and the capture must carry it through unnormalized)\n  (let ((set-clobber (sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_seterrno_cleanse\") (void* size_t) void))\n        (clob ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_clobber_const\") () int))))\n    ;; s26: (int, int, int) -> int capture; fixture sets EACCES on a<0\n    (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_socketlike\")))\n      (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () a (int int int) int))\n            (eacces ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eacces\") () int))))\n        (ffi-check \"s26 capture failure carries the target's errno\"\n                   (call-with-values (lambda () (f -1 2 3)) list)\n                   (list -1 eacces))\n        (set-clobber clobber 8)\n        (ffi-check \"s26 capture success preserves the caller's errno\"\n                   (call-with-values (lambda () (f 1 2 3)) list)\n                   (list 6 clob))))\n  ;; s23: (int, int, int, void*, void*) -> int capture; EBADF on fd<0\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_getsockoptlike\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () a (int int int void* void*) int))\n          (ebadf ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_ebadf\") () int))))\n      (ffi-check \"s23 capture with pointer args\"\n                 (call-with-values (lambda () (f -5 1 2 0 0)) list)\n                 (list -1 ebadf))\n      (set-clobber clobber 8)\n      (ffi-check \"s23 success path preserves the caller's errno\"\n                 (call-with-values (lambda () (f 4 1 2 clobber clobber)) list)\n                 (list 8 clob))))\n  ;; s26b/s26c/s26d/s26e: the small-arg capture family\n  (let ((bindf (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_bindlike\") (int void* int) int))\n        (listenf (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_listenlike\") (int int) int))\n        (setsockoptf (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_setsockoptlike\") (int int int void* int) int))\n        (getsocknamef (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_getsocknamelike\") (int void* void*) int))\n        (eacces ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eacces\") () int)))\n        (ebadf ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_ebadf\") () int))))\n    (ffi-check \"s26b bind-capture failure\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (bindf -1 0 4)) list) (list -1 eacces))\n    (ffi-check \"s26c listen-capture failure\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (listenf -2 5)) list) (list -1 ebadf))\n    (set-clobber clobber 8)\n    (ffi-check \"s26d setsockopt-capture success preserves the caller's errno\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (setsockoptf 3 1 2 clobber 4)) list) (list 10 clob))\n    (set-clobber clobber 8)\n    (ffi-check \"s26e getsockname-capture success preserves the caller's errno\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (getsocknamef 3 clobber clobber)) list) (list 5 clob)))\n  ;; s22b/s22c: declared-tail varargs WITH capture (errno 99/88 sentinel cmds)\n  (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error ((__varargs_after 2)) (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_vfcntl\") (int int int) int))\n        (g (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error ((__varargs_after 2)) (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_vioctl\") (int unsigned-long void*) int))\n        (eagain ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eagain\") () int)))\n        (ebadf ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_ebadf\") () int))))\n    (ffi-check \"s22b varargs capture failure\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (f 1 99 7)) list) (list -1 eagain))\n    (set-clobber clobber 8)\n    (ffi-check \"s22b varargs capture success preserves the caller's errno\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (f 1 2 7)) list) (list 10 clob))\n    (ffi-check \"s22c varargs+pointer capture failure\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (g 3 88 0)) list) (list -1 ebadf)))\n  (sa-foreign-free clobber)\n  (sa-foreign-free clobber)\n\n\n;; ---- the stage-1 boundary: unregistered shapes raise BEFORE any deref ---------\n\n(printf \"== unregistered shapes raise deliberately ==\\n\")\n(ffi-check-raise-message\n \"an unregistered signature raises with the signature named\"\n (lambda ()\n   ((sa-foreign-procedure \"malloc\" (void*) int)))\n \"unregistered shape on the gambit target\")\n(ffi-check-raise-message\n \"the unregistered refusal names the signature\"\n (lambda ()\n   (sa-foreign-procedure \"malloc\" (void*) void*))\n \"(void*) -> void*\")\n(ffi-check-raise-message\n \":string arguments refuse (no immobile allocation)\"\n (lambda ()\n   (sa-foreign-procedure \"joltffi_fx_absent\" (u8*) int))\n \":string arguments are unsupported on the gambit target\")\n\n(ffi-gate-finish \"gambitffi-abi\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj; sed -n '1840,2065p' Makefile; rg -n 'ffi|gc-collect' host/gambit/check.ss host/gambit/*check* host/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT* TARGET-CONTRACT.md; git diff --numstat; cat host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-load-failure.ss\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj; sed -n '1840,2065p' Makefile; rg -n 'ffi|gc-collect' host/gambit/check.ss host/gambit/*check* host/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT* TARGET-CONTRACT.md; git diff --numstat; cat host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-load-failure.ss\"","aggregated_output":"(ns jolt.backend-scheme.ffi\n  \"jolt.ffi lowering for the Scheme back end: foreign procedures — fixed,\n  declared-tail varargs and bare-marker varargs — foreign callables, aggregate\n  layouts, and the marshaling across the C boundary in both directions.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [jolt.backend-scheme.names :refer [chez-str-lit]]\n            [jolt.backend-scheme.session :refer [fresh-label target]]))\n\n;; jolt.ffi/__cfn -> a Chez foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi). The C symbol + types are\n;; compile-time literals from the analyzer, so this emits a real typed binding;\n;; the resulting Scheme procedure is callable like any jolt fn. The library must\n;; have loaded the shared object (jolt.ffi/load-library) before this def runs.\n;; Keep this in agreement with ffi-type->chez in host/chez/java/ffi.ss: these are\n;; the compile-time signature and runtime memory halves of one public contract.\n;; This table is baked into each checked-in compiler seed.\n(def ^:private ffi-types\n  {\"int\" \"int\" \"uint\" \"unsigned-int\"\n   \"int8\" \"integer-8\" \"i8\" \"integer-8\"\n   \"int16\" \"integer-16\" \"short\" \"integer-16\"\n   \"uint16\" \"unsigned-16\" \"ushort\" \"unsigned-16\"\n   \"int32\" \"integer-32\" \"uint32\" \"unsigned-32\"\n   \"long\" \"long\" \"ulong\" \"unsigned-long\"\n   \"int64\" \"integer-64\" \"uint64\" \"unsigned-64\" \"size_t\" \"size_t\" \"ssize_t\" \"ssize_t\"\n   \"iptr\" \"iptr\" \"uptr\" \"uptr\" \"double\" \"double\" \"float\" \"float\"\n   \"pointer\" \"void*\" \"void*\" \"void*\" \"string\" \"string\" \"void\" \"void\"\n   \"uint8\" \"unsigned-8\" \"u8\" \"unsigned-8\" \"byte\" \"unsigned-8\" \"char\" \"char\"\n   ;; :bool is a ONE-BYTE C boolean (C99 _Bool / stdbool.h), so it travels as\n   ;; unsigned-8 and the value is converted at the boundary — Chez's own\n   ;; `boolean` foreign type is int-sized, which is the wrong width for _Bool\n   ;; and would read three bytes of whatever sat next to it on a return.\n   \"bool\" \"unsigned-8\"})\n(defn ffi-type->chez [t]\n  (or (ffi-types t) (throw (ex-info (str \"jolt.ffi: unknown foreign type :\" t) {}))))\n\n(defn- emit-ffi-layout-ftype [type]\n  (cond\n    (string? type) (ffi-type->chez type)\n    ;; A union is the same member list under Chez's other aggregate ftype, so it\n    ;; gets its size, alignment and (all-equal) member offsets from ftype-sizeof\n    ;; and ftype-&ref exactly as a struct does — no layout arithmetic here.\n    (or (= :struct (:ffi-kind type)) (= :union (:ffi-kind type)))\n    (str \"(\" (if (= :union (:ffi-kind type)) \"union\" \"struct\") \" \"\n         (str/join\n          \" \"\n          (map-indexed\n           (fn [i field]\n             (str \"[f\" i \" \" (emit-ffi-layout-ftype (:type field)) \"]\"))\n           (:fields type)))\n         \")\")\n    (= :array (:ffi-kind type))\n    (str \"(array \" (:count type) \" \" (emit-ffi-layout-ftype (:type type)) \")\")\n    :else\n    (throw (ex-info \"jolt.ffi: invalid analyzed layout type\" {:type type}))))\n\n(declare ffi-layout-descendant-entries)\n\n(def ^:private ffi-layout-index-marker ::ffi-layout-index)\n\n(defn- ffi-layout-entry [type public-path emitted-path]\n  (cons {:path public-path :emitted-path emitted-path :type type}\n        (ffi-layout-descendant-entries type public-path emitted-path)))\n\n(defn- ffi-layout-descendant-entries [type public-path emitted-path]\n  (cond\n    (string? type) []\n    (or (= :struct (:ffi-kind type)) (= :union (:ffi-kind type)))\n    (mapcat\n     (fn [i field]\n       (ffi-layout-entry (:type field)\n                         (conj public-path (:name field))\n                         (conj emitted-path (str \"f\" i))))\n     (range (count (:fields type)))\n     (:fields type))\n    (= :array (:ffi-kind type))\n    (ffi-layout-entry (:type type)\n                      (conj public-path ffi-layout-index-marker)\n                      (conj emitted-path 0))\n    :else\n    (throw (ex-info \"jolt.ffi: invalid analyzed layout type\" {:type type}))))\n\n(defn- ffi-layout-entries\n  ([layout] (ffi-layout-entries layout [] []))\n  ([layout public-path emitted-path]\n   (mapcat\n    (fn [i field]\n      (let [pp (conj public-path (:name field))\n            ep (conj emitted-path (str \"f\" i))]\n        (ffi-layout-entry (:type field) pp ep)))\n    (range (count (:fields layout)))\n    (:fields layout))))\n\n(defn- emit-layout-path [path]\n  (str \"(jolt-vector \"\n       (str/join \" \"\n                 (map (fn [part]\n                        (cond\n                          (= part ffi-layout-index-marker)\n                          \"(keyword \\\"jolt.ffi\\\" \\\"index\\\")\"\n                          (string? part)\n                          (str \"(keyword #f \" (chez-str-lit part) \")\")\n                          :else part))\n                      path))\n       \")\"))\n\n(defn- ffi-layout-array-entries\n  ([layout] (ffi-layout-array-entries layout []))\n  ([type public-path]\n   (cond\n     (string? type) []\n     (or (= :struct (:ffi-kind type)) (= :union (:ffi-kind type)))\n     (mapcat (fn [field]\n               (ffi-layout-array-entries\n                (:type field) (conj public-path (:name field))))\n             (:fields type))\n     (= :array (:ffi-kind type))\n     (cons {:path public-path :count (:count type) :element-type (:type type)}\n           (ffi-layout-array-entries\n            (:type type) (conj public-path ffi-layout-index-marker)))\n     :else\n     (throw (ex-info \"jolt.ffi: invalid analyzed layout type\" {:type type})))))\n\t\t\t\th=$$(/usr/libexec/java_home -v \"$$jdk\" 2>/dev/null) && [ -x \"$$h/bin/java\" ] && JAVA_CMD=\"$$h/bin/java\"; \\\n\t\t\tfi; \\\n\t\t\tif [ -n \"$$JAVA_CMD\" ]; then echo \"certify: JAVA_CMD=$$JAVA_CMD (profile pins JDK $$jdk)\"; export JAVA_CMD; fi; \\\n\t\tfi; \\\n\t\tdeps=\"{:deps {org.clojure/clojure {:mvn/version \\\"$$v\\\"}}}\"; \\\n\t\tclojure $(CERTIFY_JVM_OPTS) -Sdeps \"$$deps\" -M test/conformance/certify.clj --self-test && \\\n\t\tclojure $(CERTIFY_JVM_OPTS) -Sdeps \"$$deps\" -M test/conformance/certify.clj; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\techo \"certify: clojure not on PATH — skipped\"; \\\n\tfi\n\n# Where the gambit gates find gsi and gsc: GAMBIT_PREFIX/bin, brew's\n# gambit-scheme prefix by default (tests.yml builds 4.9.8 from source into\n# /opt/gambit and passes GAMBIT_PREFIX=/opt/gambit). NEVER bare gsc/gsi (gsc on\n# PATH is Ghostscript): always a prefix's binary. Absolute, because gambitboot\n# and unbound-check.sh cd into host/gambit before running it.\nGAMBIT_PREFIX ?= $(shell brew --prefix gambit-scheme 2>/dev/null)\nGAMBIT_GSI := $(abspath $(GAMBIT_PREFIX))/bin/gsi\nGAMBIT_GSC := $(abspath $(GAMBIT_PREFIX))/bin/gsc\n\n# Every gambit gate is detection-gated like certify: no gambit, clean skip. With\n# JOLT_REQUIRE_GAMBIT set the skip is a failure instead — tests.yml sets it, so\n# an install step that quietly stopped installing cannot turn the gates into\n# no-ops that read as green (the boot ran dead for two weeks with every gambit\n# gate skipping on the runner). $@ names the gate in the message.\nGAMBIT-SKIP = if [ -n \"$$JOLT_REQUIRE_GAMBIT\" ]; then \\\n\t  echo \"$@: no gambit at $(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/bin and JOLT_REQUIRE_GAMBIT is set\" >&2; exit 1; \\\n\telse \\\n\t  echo \"$@: gambit-scheme not installed (GAMBIT_PREFIX=$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)) — skipped\"; \\\n\tfi\n\n# Gambit adapter gate (G1, jolt-mj95.2): loads host/gambit/{prelude-shims,\n# scheme-adapter-runtime,hasheq}.ss under native gsi and asserts the\n# CONTRACT.txt names + shim behavior.\n\n# host/gambit/records-gambit.ss is GENERATED from the four host/chez records\n# files — records.ss, records-coll.ss, protocols.ss, records-dispatch.ss — (the\n# define-jrec-family phase wall — see gen-records.ss). Regenerate after every\n# change to any of them.\ngambitgen:\n\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-records.ss\n\n# ...and this is what makes that an invariant rather than a note: regenerate into\n# a temp file and diff. A records-file change that never reached the generated\n# file fails here instead of silently leaving the Gambit host a release behind.\n# Runs on Chez alone, so it gates in CI whether or not gambit is installed.\n# Grenadine ships four namespaces it generates rather than commits, so half the\n# source tree comes from the submodule and half from vendor/grenadine-generated\n# (see the README there). Bumping one without refreshing the other mixes two\n# Grenadine versions, which breaks far from the cause — so it is checked, not\n# documented and hoped for.\n# Compares the COMMIT, not the tag: a submodule checkout does not necessarily\n# carry tags — CI's does not — so `git describe` fails there and a tag\n# comparison would only ever pass on a developer's machine. That is exactly the\n# environment-dependent gate that reads as green where it is never really\n# checked, so the recorded VERSION carries the sha and this reads that.\ngrenadinecheck:\n\t@pinned=$$(git -C vendor/grenadine rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null); \\\n\t  vendored=$$(sed -n 's/^[^#].* //p' vendor/grenadine-generated/VERSION 2>/dev/null | tr -d '[:space:]'); \\\n\t  tag=$$(sed -n 's/^\\([^# ][^ ]*\\) .*/\\1/p' vendor/grenadine-generated/VERSION 2>/dev/null); \\\n\t  if [ -z \"$$pinned\" ]; then \\\n\t    echo \"grenadinecheck: vendor/grenadine is not checked out — run 'git submodule update --init'\" >&2; \\\n\t    exit 1; \\\n\t  elif [ \"$$pinned\" = \"$$vendored\" ]; then \\\n\t    echo \"grenadinecheck: generated sources match the pinned submodule ($$tag $$(echo $$pinned | cut -c1-7))\"; \\\n\t  else \\\n\t    echo \"grenadinecheck: vendor/grenadine is at $$pinned but vendor/grenadine-generated records $$vendored ($$tag)\" >&2; \\\n\t    echo \"  refresh the generated sources — see vendor/grenadine-generated/README.md\" >&2; \\\n\t    exit 1; \\\n\t  fi\n\ngambitgencheck:\n\t@out=$$(mktemp -d)/records-gambit.ss; \\\n\t  GEN_RECORDS_OUT=\"$$out\" $(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-records.ss >/dev/null; \\\n\t  if diff -q \"$$out\" host/gambit/records-gambit.ss >/dev/null; then \\\n\t    echo \"gambitgencheck: records-gambit.ss is current with the records files\"; \\\n\t  else \\\n\t    echo \"gambitgencheck: host/gambit/records-gambit.ss is STALE — run 'make gambitgen'\" >&2; \\\n\t    diff -u host/gambit/records-gambit.ss \"$$out\" | head -40 >&2; \\\n\t    rm -f \"$$out\"; exit 1; \\\n\t  fi; \\\n\t  rm -f \"$$out\"\n\n# Gambit seed-mint gate: re-mint the gambit seed into a temp dir on Chez and\n# require it to match host/gambit/seed/ byte-for-byte. Fails when gen-seed.ss\n# itself cannot run (a chez-only construct reached the emission) or when the\n# chez seed was re-minted without `make gambitseed`. Runs on Chez alone, so it\n# gates in CI whether or not gambit is installed.\ngambitseedcheck:\n\t@out=$$(mktemp -d); \\\n\t  if ! GEN_SEED_OUT_DIR=\"$$out\" $(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-seed.ss > \"$$out/mint.log\" 2>&1; then \\\n\t    tail -20 \"$$out/mint.log\" >&2; \\\n\t    echo \"gambitseedcheck: gen-seed.ss FAILED — the gambit seed cannot be minted from current sources\" >&2; \\\n\t    rm -rf \"$$out\"; exit 1; \\\n\t  fi; \\\n\t  if diff -q \"$$out/prelude.ss\" host/gambit/seed/prelude.ss >/dev/null \\\n\t      && diff -q \"$$out/image.ss\" host/gambit/seed/image.ss >/dev/null; then \\\n\t    echo \"gambitseedcheck: gambit seed is current with the sources\"; \\\n\t    rm -rf \"$$out\"; \\\n\t  else \\\n\t    echo \"gambitseedcheck: host/gambit/seed is STALE — run 'make gambitseed'\" >&2; \\\n\t    rm -rf \"$$out\"; exit 1; \\\n\t  fi\n\ngambitcheck:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\t\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/gambitcheck.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# G2 kernel-test gate (jolt-mj95.4): the full booted manifest on native gsi,\n# driven through the real natives. Same detection-gated shape as gambitcheck;\n# a second on gsi. Run from the repo root (boot's irregex load is cwd-relative).\ngambitkernel:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\t\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/kernel-test.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# G3 eval gate: real jolt source through jolt-compile-eval on the booted\n# manifest + cross-minted seed, renders pinned to Chez captures. Detection-\n# gated like gambitcheck. In the ci list: it is the only gate that runs\n# emitted code on gsi end to end, and while it sat outside ci every row failed\n# for two weeks (jolt-cw2p) with nothing red. Run from the repo root.\ngambiteval:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\t\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/eval-test.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# Every Scheme global the full-profile boot references is defined — Gambit's\n# own linker report over the compiled boot, minus what the record translator\n# evals at runtime, against host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt (untaken paths;\n# a stale line fails). The boot splices most of host/chez, so a Chez-side name\n# reaching a shared file is otherwise an unbound global no Chez gate can see;\n# mirrordrift only compares names defined on BOTH hosts. ~75s: it compiles the\n# seed to js (text only, no C compiler, no node). Detection-gated. Ordered\n# after gambitboot: both regenerate boot-full.ss, and under -j a reader must\n# not open the file mid-rewrite.\ngambitunbound: gambitboot\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tJOLT_GSC=\"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" sh host/gambit/unbound-check.sh; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\ngambitunbound-regen:\n\t@JOLT_GSC=\"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" sh host/gambit/unbound-check.sh --regen\n\n# The jolt half of the same question: every var cell the boot interned is\n# bound. Emitted code reaches a var through its cell, so after the boot the\n# var table holds every var the seed and the compiler image reference — an\n# unbound root is a reference nothing this boot defines (clojure.core/\n# chunk-first, bound by the excluded natives-array.ss, is how every `defn`\n# died). Against host/gambit/unbound-vars-allowlist.txt; a stale line fails.\n# One gsi boot, a few seconds. Detection-gated.\ngambitvars:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\t\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/unbound-vars.ss < /dev/null; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\ngambitvars-regen:\n\t@JOLT_GAMBITVARS=regen \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/unbound-vars.ss < /dev/null\n\n# The third question: every Class/member call and (new Class) the seed emits\n# resolves in the booted statics/constructor registries. The registries are\n# host-static-methods.ss's on Chez and host/gambit/host-statics.ss's here, and\n# nothing else says which of the seed's statics this target carries — a remint\n# reaching a new one degraded silently (parse-long answered \"unsupported\" with\n# every gate green). Reads the seed as text, boots, asks the registries; misses\n# against host/gambit/seed-statics-allowlist.txt, a stale line fails. A grep\n# and one gsi boot, a few seconds. Detection-gated.\ngambitstatics:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tJOLT_GSI=\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" sh host/gambit/seed-statics.sh; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\ngambitstatics-regen:\n\t@JOLT_GSI=\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" sh host/gambit/seed-statics.sh --regen\n\n# Every macro the emitter can put in call position (the op registry's :call\n# names, the numeric op tables) has a same-named function in eval-fns.ss:\n# eval'd code on the Gambit boot cannot see unit macros. grep only, so it\n# gates in CI whether or not gambit is installed.\ngambittwins:\n\t@sh host/gambit/eval-twins-check.sh\n\n# Build profiles: generate the reduced repl profile and check that the language\n# still works while an excluded feature reports itself instead of failing as an\n# unbound name. Cheap (a gsi load, no js compile), so it gates the mechanism.\n# Ordered after gambitboot: gen-boot.ss rewrites boot-active.ss for every\n# profile, and under -j two writers would race on it.\ngambitprofile: gambitboot\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-boot.ss repl; \\\n\t\t\"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/profile-test.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# The full-profile boot comes up on gsi: the js and gsi targets share the boot,\n# and NOTHING else runs its top level end to end — the shipped web REPL hung at\n# boot for a week of commits (unbound jolt-with-mutex at the first keyword\n# intern) while every other gambit gate stayed green. Skipped, like the other\n# gambit gates, when gambit-scheme is absent.\ngambitboot:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t  $(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-boot.ss full; \\\n\t  out=$$(cd host/gambit && \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" boot-probe.scm < /dev/null 2>&1); \\\n\t  case \"$$out\" in \\\n\t    *BOOT-OK*) echo \"gambitboot: full-profile boot OK on gsi\";; \\\n\t    *) printf '%s\\n' \"$$out\" | tail -20; echo \"gambitboot: FAILED — full-profile boot did not reach BOOT-OK\" >&2; exit 1;; \\\n\t  esac; \\\n\telse \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# ---- P1b-stage1: the gambitffi* gates ----------------------------------------\n#\nrg: host/gambit/check.ss: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: TARGET-CONTRACT.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nhost/gambit/unbound-check.ss:66:  (gs-string-suffix? \"/_gambit.js\" path))\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:428:  (check \"sa-gc-collect no-ops\" (sa-gc-collect) #f)\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:430:  ;; the ffi tier: EVERY entry raises a message-carrying condition\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:432:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:434:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:439:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:440:  (check-raise-message \"jolt-ffi-native-error-procedure (target wrapper)\"\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:442:                         (jolt-ffi-native-error-procedure () \"f\" (int) int))\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:443:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:445:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:447:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:449:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:451:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:453:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:455:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss:457:                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\nhost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt:17:# failed that bar stayed on the blocklist (ffi, eval/compile, fasl,\nhost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt:142:# sa-gc-collect may no-op (the JVM gc it maps is only a hint); sa-run-process\nhost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt:178:sa-gc-collect\nhost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt:226:# tier: capability-ffi\nhost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt:230:# ffi-tier native (foreign-alloc/free/ref/set!/sizeof, lock-object/unlock-object,\nhost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt:241:#   jolt.ffi/load-library must surface it as a clean jolt-level error;\nhost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt:246:#   with the ffi capability provides them; without it, jolt.ffi raises cleanly;\nhost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt:395:#   The flonum family, for the typed foreign-array copies (java/ffi.ss): an\n106\t0\tMakefile\n354\t354\thost/chez/seed/image.ss\n5\t0\thost/gambit/boot.ss\n541\t135\thost/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss\n328\t328\thost/gambit/seed/image.ss\n48\t11\tjolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj\n6\t1\tjolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj\n;; gambitffi-load-failure.ss — the gambitffi-load-failure-smoke gate: missing vs\n;; unloadable with the loader's reason preserved, scoped-before-global\n;; isolation, duplicate-definers detection, repeat-load no-op.\n;;\n;; The unloadable candidate is built by the Makefile: libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\n;; is linked against libjoltffi-dep.dylib, and the DEPENDENCY is removed before\n;; the gate runs — so the file is THERE but its dependency is not, the\n;; present-but-unloadable case (jolt-lang/jolt#1127's reason preservation).\n;;\n;; Run via `make gambitffi-load-failure-smoke` (external watchdog, repo root).\n\n(##include \"ffi-harness.ss\")\n\n(printf \"== missing vs unloadable, reason preserved ==\\n\")\n(let ((missing (guard (e (#t (condition-message e)))\n                 (sa-load-shared-object \"/nonexistent/libjoltffi-nope.dylib\")\n                 \"NO-RAISE\"))\n      (unloadable (guard (e (#t (condition-message e)))\n                    (sa-load-shared-object \"build/gambit-ffi/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\")\n                    \"NO-RAISE\")))\n  (ffi-check-true \"missing candidate raises\" (not (string=? missing \"NO-RAISE\")))\n  (ffi-check-true \"unloadable candidate raises\" (not (string=? unloadable \"NO-RAISE\")))\n  ;; the loader's own reason rides the message\n  (ffi-check-true \"missing reason preserved (no such file)\"\n                  (string-contains missing \"no such file\"))\n  (ffi-check-true \"unloadable reason preserved (names the missing dependency)\"\n                  (string-contains unloadable \"libjoltffi-dep.dylib\"))\n  (ffi-check-true \"the two failures are distinguishable\"\n                  (not (string=? missing unloadable))))\n\n(printf \"== scoped-before-global isolation ==\\n\")\n(ffi-check-true \"fixture not loaded yet: scoped probe answers #f\"\n                (not (joltffi-dlsym-loaded \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\")))\n(ffi-load-fixture!)\n(ffi-check-true \"after a scoped load, the scoped probe answers\"\n                (joltffi-dlsym-loaded \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\"))\n;; RTLD_LOCAL: a scoped library's symbols are NOT in the global namespace\n(let ((global-hit (guard (e (#t 0))\n                    (joltffi-dlerror)\n                    (joltffi-dlsym-global \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\")\n                    (if (joltffi-dlerror) 0 1))))\n  (ffi-check \"a scoped library stays invisible to global resolution\" global-hit 0))\n;; ...and once loaded, the tier's own entry probe answers for it\n(ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry? answers for the loaded fixture\"\n                (sa-foreign-entry? \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\"))\n\n(printf \"== repeat load is a no-op with the same handle ==\\n\")\n(let ((h1 (joltffi-handle-of ffi-fixture-path))\n      (h2 (joltffi-handle-of ffi-fixture-path)))\n  (ffi-check-true \"repeat load registered exactly one handle\"\n                  (and h1 h2 (= h1 h2))))\n\n(printf \"== duplicate definers: two addresses, first declared resolves ==\\n\")\n(ffi-load-fixture!)\n(sa-load-shared-object ffi-fixture2-path)\n(let ((defs (joltffi-definers \"joltffi_fx_dup_symbol\"))\n      (a1 (joltffi-dlsym-loaded \"joltffi_fx_dup_symbol\")))\n  (ffi-check \"two distinct addresses across two declared libraries\" (length defs) 2)\n  (ffi-check-true \"the addresses differ\"\n                  (not (= (cdar defs) (cdar (cdr defs)))))\n  (ffi-check-true \"the first declared library wins resolution\"\n                  (= a1 (cdar defs)))\n  ;; the resolved value is the first library's behavior\n  (ffi-check \"first-declared symbol behaves like fixture 1\"\n             ((sa-foreign-procedure \"joltffi_fx_dup_symbol\" () int)) 111))\n\n(ffi-gate-finish \"gambitffi-load-failure-smoke\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
