{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat host/gambit/ffi/gambitffi-abi.ss'","aggregated_output":";; gambitffi-abi.ss — the gambitffi-abi gate: scalar widths, pointers, byte\n;; copies, return conversion, REGISTERED signatures, symbol parity.\n;;\n;; Run via `make gambitffi-abi` (which builds the bridge + fixtures first, runs\n;; this under an external watchdog, from the repo root). Every row asserts\n;; state-derived behavior against the fixture library's targets — nothing\n;; prints unconditionally.\n\n(##include \"ffi-harness.ss\")\n\n;; ---- prerequisites: the qualified tier is the bridge + fixture ---------------\n\n;; Fail-closed note: with the bridge absent (a bypassed prerequisite), EVERY row\n;; below raises the documented \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target: the\n;; stage-1 native bridge is not built\" message instead of passing — the gate\n;; never skips. The bridge is loaded here; that is what the gate qualifies.\n(let ((pre (guard (e (#t (condition-message e)))\n             (sa-load-shared-object ffi-fixture-path)\n             \"NO-RAISE\")))\n  (if (string=? pre \"NO-RAISE\")\n      (printf \"  ok     fixture library loaded through the adapter loader\\n\")\n      (begin (printf \"  FAIL   fixture load raised: ~s\\n\" pre)\n             (set! ffi-failures (+ ffi-failures 1))\n             (ffi-gate-finish \"gambitffi-abi\"))))\n\n;; ---- scalar widths ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(printf \"== scalar widths (exact, LP64 legs) ==\\n\")\n(ffi-check \"sizeof int\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'int) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-int\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-int) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof integer-8\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'integer-8) 1)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-8\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-8) 1)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof integer-16\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'integer-16) 2)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-16\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-16) 2)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof integer-32\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'integer-32) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-32\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-32) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof integer-64\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'integer-64) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-64\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-64) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof size_t\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'size_t) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof ssize_t\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'ssize_t) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof long\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'long) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof unsigned-long\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'unsigned-long) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof iptr\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'iptr) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof uptr\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'uptr) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof double\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'double) 8)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof float\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'float) 4)\n(ffi-check \"sizeof void*\" (sa-foreign-sizeof 'void*) 8)\n(ffi-check-raise-message \"sizeof unknown type refuses\"\n                         (lambda () (sa-foreign-sizeof 'jolt-agg)) \"no size for foreign type\")\n\n;; ---- pointers, alloc/free/zero, byte copies -----------------------------------\n\n(printf \"== pointers + bulk byte copies ==\\n\")\n(let ((p (sa-foreign-alloc 64)))\n  (ffi-check-true \"alloc answers a nonzero address\" (and (exact-integer? p) (> p 0)))\n  (sa-foreign-zero! p 64)\n  (let ((bv (make-u8vector 64 255)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! p bv 64)\n    (ffi-check \"zero! + bytes-ref! all-zero\" (u8vector->list bv)\n               (make-list 64 0)))\n  ;; binary-faithful moves: NUL and 0xff included\n  (let ((bv (u8vector 0 1 #xff 0 66 0 0 0)))\n    (sa-foreign-bytes-set! p bv 8)\n    (let ((out (make-u8vector 8 9)))\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! p out 8)\n      (ffi-check \"bytes-set!/ref! round-trip (NUL + 0xff)\" (u8vector->list out)\n                 '(0 1 #xff 0 66 0 0 0))))\n  ;; unaligned offset write/read through the typed accessors\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'integer-32 p 5 -7)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! unaligned i32\" (sa-foreign-ref 'integer-32 p 5) -7)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'unsigned-64 p 24 9223372036854775807)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! u64 max\" (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-64 p 24) 9223372036854775807)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'integer-64 p 32 -9007199254740993)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! i64 past double range\" (sa-foreign-ref 'integer-64 p 32) -9007199254740993)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'double p 40 1.5)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! double\" (sa-foreign-ref 'double p 40) 1.5)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'float p 48 0.25)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! float (single precision)\" (sa-foreign-ref 'float p 48) 0.25)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'integer-8 p 50 -128)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! i8\" (sa-foreign-ref 'integer-8 p 50) -128)\n  (sa-foreign-set! 'unsigned-16 p 52 65535)\n  (ffi-check \"typed set!/ref! u16\" (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-16 p 52) 65535)\n  (sa-foreign-free p)\n  (printf \"  ok     free answered\\n\"))\n(ffi-check-raise-message \"bytes-ref! past the bytevector refuses\"\n                         (lambda () (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! 1 (make-u8vector 2 0) 3))\n                         \"bulk copy count exceeds the bytevector\")\n\n;; ---- registered signatures through the fixture library ------------------------\n\n(printf \"== registered signatures (fixture targets through the tier) ==\\n\")\n;; Every fixture call below goes through the COMPILER-EMITTED scoped-branch\n;; shape verbatim: (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"sym\"))) ... (sa-foreign-procedure a sig ...)).\n;; By-name construction is exercised separately against process-global symbols\n;; (the by-name fallback's Chez semantics: RTLD_LOCAL scoped libs are invisible\n;; to it — that isolation is the scoped-shadows-global guarantee).\n(let ((clobber (sa-foreign-alloc 32)))\n  ;; pointers are exact integers here: a foreign buffer the fixtures write\n  ;; into, read back through the bulk copies (the copy-in/copy-out design)\n  (sa-foreign-zero! clobber 32)\n  ;; s01: () -> int\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\")))\n    (ffi-check-true \"scoped resolution finds the fixture symbol\" (and a (not (= a 0))))\n    (ffi-check \"s01 () -> int\" ((sa-foreign-procedure a () int)) 42))\n  ;; s01b: () -> int32\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eintr\")))\n    (let ((probe (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eintr_c\")))\n      (ffi-check \"s01b () -> int32 matches its own probe\"\n                 ((sa-foreign-procedure a () int32))\n                 ((sa-foreign-procedure probe () int)))))\n  ;; s02: (void*, size_t) -> int\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_provenance\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a (void* size_t) int)))\n      (ffi-check \"s02 null buffer refusal\" (f 0 0) -1)\n      (ffi-check \"s02 provenance text\"\n                 (let ((n (f clobber 16)))\n                   (let ((out (make-u8vector n)))\n                     (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! clobber out n)\n                     (list n (u8vector->list out))))\n                 (list 15 (map char->integer (string->list \"joltffi-fixture\"))))))\n  ;; s03: (void*, size_t) -> void\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_cleanse\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a (void* size_t) void)))\n      (sa-foreign-set! 'integer-32 clobber 0 305419896)\n      (f clobber 4)\n      (ffi-check \"s03 cleanse zeroed the range\" (sa-foreign-ref 'integer-32 clobber 0) 0)))\n  ;; s12/s12b: BE field get/put\n  (let ((a-get (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_s32be_get\"))\n        (a-put (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_s32be_put\")))\n    (let ((put (sa-foreign-procedure a-put (void* integer-64 int32) void))\n          (get (sa-foreign-procedure a-get (void* integer-64) int32)))\n      (put clobber 4 -2023406815)\n      (ffi-check \"s12b/s12 BE round-trip\" (get clobber 4) -2023406815)))\n  ;; s13: (int64, void*, int64) -> int64\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_strerror\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a (integer-64 void* integer-64) integer-64)))\n      (let ((n (f 3 clobber 16)))\n        (let ((out (make-u8vector n)))\n          (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! clobber out n)\n          (ffi-check \"s13 error-text writer\" (utf8->string out) \"err-3\")))))\n  ;; s19/s18: () -> void* then (void*) -> void\n  (let ((a-new (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_worker_new\"))\n        (a-free (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_free\")))\n    (let ((new (sa-foreign-procedure a-new () void*))\n          (free (sa-foreign-procedure a-free (void*) void)))\n      (let ((w (new)))\n        (ffi-check-true \"s19 answers a nonzero pointer\" (and (exact-integer? w) (> w 0)))\n        (begin (free w) #t)\n        (ffi-check-true \"s18 free answered (a second free of the same block is malloc corruption, not a witness)\" #t))))\n  ;; s20: () -> void* (errno accessor shape)\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_errno_location\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a () void*)))\n      (ffi-check-true \"s20 errno-location answers a nonzero pointer\"\n                      (and (exact-integer? (f)) (> (f) 0)))))\n  ;; s21: (int) -> string (NULL result must surface as #f at this layer)\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_errtext\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure a (int) string)))\n      (ffi-check \"s21 string result\" (f 1) \"joltffi-error-one\")\n      (ffi-check \"s21 NULL string result\" (f 0) #f)))\n  ;; s22: declared-tail varargs (int, int, int) -> int\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_vfcntl\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure (__varargs_after 2) a (int int int) int)))\n      (ffi-check \"s22 varargs (2 fixed + 1 tail)\" (f 10 3 100) 113)))\n  ;; by-name construction against PROCESS-GLOBAL symbols (libc): strerror\n  ;; through the registered s21 shape and __error through s20 — the stdlib's\n  ;; own errno-accessor spellings. RTLD_LOCAL scoped libs stay invisible to\n  ;; this path by design (tested in the load-failure gate).\n  (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure \"strerror\" (int) string)))\n    (ffi-check-true \"by-name process-global resolution (strerror, s21)\" (string? (f 1)))\n    (ffi-check-true \"by-name errno accessor (__error, s20)\"\n                    (> ((sa-foreign-procedure \"__error\" () void*)) 0)))\n  ;; symbol parity\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry? fixture symbol\" (sa-foreign-entry? \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\"))\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry? libc symbol\" (sa-foreign-entry? \"malloc\"))\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry? unknown symbol answers #f\"\n                  (not (sa-foreign-entry? \"joltffi_fx_absent_symbol\")))\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry-address matches the scoped resolution\"\n                  (= (sa-foreign-entry-address \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\")\n                     (joltffi-dlsym-loaded \"joltffi_fx_layout_version\")))\n  (ffi-check-true \"sa-foreign-entry-address raises for unknown\"\n                  (not (guard (e (#t #f)) (sa-foreign-entry-address \"joltffi_fx_absent_symbol\") #t)))\n  (sa-foreign-free clobber))\n\n(printf \"== native-error capture (ordinary, registered) ==\\n\")\n(let ((clobber (sa-foreign-alloc 32)))\n  (sa-foreign-zero! clobber 32)\n  ;; the errno pre-set target: an s03-shaped call that sets errno=7777 after\n  ;; zeroing, so every \"success preserves the caller's errno\" row below reads a\n  ;; DETERMINISTIC pre-existing value (the target's success path touches no\n  ;; errno, and the capture must carry it through unnormalized)\n  (let ((set-clobber (sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_seterrno_cleanse\") (void* size_t) void))\n        (clob ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_clobber_const\") () int))))\n    ;; s26: (int, int, int) -> int capture; fixture sets EACCES on a<0\n    (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_socketlike\")))\n      (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () a (int int int) int))\n            (eacces ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eacces\") () int))))\n        (ffi-check \"s26 capture failure carries the target's errno\"\n                   (call-with-values (lambda () (f -1 2 3)) list)\n                   (list -1 eacces))\n        (set-clobber clobber 8)\n        (ffi-check \"s26 capture success preserves the caller's errno\"\n                   (call-with-values (lambda () (f 1 2 3)) list)\n                   (list 6 clob))))\n  ;; s23: (int, int, int, void*, void*) -> int capture; EBADF on fd<0\n  (let ((a (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_getsockoptlike\")))\n    (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () a (int int int void* void*) int))\n          (ebadf ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_ebadf\") () int))))\n      (ffi-check \"s23 capture with pointer args\"\n                 (call-with-values (lambda () (f -5 1 2 0 0)) list)\n                 (list -1 ebadf))\n      (set-clobber clobber 8)\n      (ffi-check \"s23 success path preserves the caller's errno\"\n                 (call-with-values (lambda () (f 4 1 2 clobber clobber)) list)\n                 (list 8 clob))))\n  ;; s26b/s26c/s26d/s26e: the small-arg capture family\n  (let ((bindf (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_bindlike\") (int void* int) int))\n        (listenf (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_listenlike\") (int int) int))\n        (setsockoptf (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_setsockoptlike\") (int int int void* int) int))\n        (getsocknamef (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error () (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_getsocknamelike\") (int void* void*) int))\n        (eacces ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eacces\") () int)))\n        (ebadf ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_ebadf\") () int))))\n    (ffi-check \"s26b bind-capture failure\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (bindf -1 0 4)) list) (list -1 eacces))\n    (ffi-check \"s26c listen-capture failure\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (listenf -2 5)) list) (list -1 ebadf))\n    (set-clobber clobber 8)\n    (ffi-check \"s26d setsockopt-capture success preserves the caller's errno\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (setsockoptf 3 1 2 clobber 4)) list) (list 10 clob))\n    (set-clobber clobber 8)\n    (ffi-check \"s26e getsockname-capture success preserves the caller's errno\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (getsocknamef 3 clobber clobber)) list) (list 5 clob)))\n  ;; s22b/s22c: declared-tail varargs WITH capture (errno 99/88 sentinel cmds)\n  (let ((f (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error ((__varargs_after 2)) (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_vfcntl\") (int int int) int))\n        (g (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error ((__varargs_after 2)) (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_vioctl\") (int unsigned-long void*) int))\n        (eagain ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_eagain\") () int)))\n        (ebadf ((sa-foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi-dlsym-native \"joltffi_fx_ebadf\") () int))))\n    (ffi-check \"s22b varargs capture failure\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (f 1 99 7)) list) (list -1 eagain))\n    (set-clobber clobber 8)\n    (ffi-check \"s22b varargs capture success preserves the caller's errno\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (f 1 2 7)) list) (list 10 clob))\n    (ffi-check \"s22c varargs+pointer capture failure\"\n               (call-with-values (lambda () (g 3 88 0)) list) (list -1 ebadf)))\n  (sa-foreign-free clobber)\n  (sa-foreign-free clobber)\n\n\n;; ---- the stage-1 boundary: unregistered shapes raise BEFORE any deref ---------\n\n(printf \"== unregistered shapes raise deliberately ==\\n\")\n(ffi-check-raise-message\n \"an unregistered signature raises with the signature named\"\n (lambda ()\n   ((sa-foreign-procedure \"malloc\" (void*) int)))\n \"unregistered shape on the gambit target\")\n(ffi-check-raise-message\n \"the unregistered refusal names the signature\"\n (lambda ()\n   (sa-foreign-procedure \"malloc\" (void*) void*))\n \"(void*) -> void*\")\n(ffi-check-raise-message\n \":string arguments refuse (no immobile allocation)\"\n (lambda ()\n   (sa-foreign-procedure \"joltffi_fx_absent\" (u8*) int))\n \":string arguments are unsupported on the gambit target\")\n\n(ffi-gate-finish \"gambitffi-abi\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,70p' jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj; sed -n '370,445p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; sed -n '1,100p' host/gambit/eval-test.ss; sed -n '390,500p' host/gambit/gambitcheck.ss; rg -n 'seed|CHEZ :|CHEZ |GAMBIT' Makefile | tail -45; sed -n '1,100p' host/gambit/gen-seed.ss; cat /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-inv/p1b-inv/ffi-call-sites.md | tail -95; rg -n 'Q[1-6]' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795020000000-engineer-p1b-inventory.glm-5.3-flash.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,70p' jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj; sed -n '370,445p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; sed -n '1,100p' host/gambit/eval-test.ss; sed -n '390,500p' host/gambit/gambitcheck.ss; rg -n 'seed|CHEZ :|CHEZ |GAMBIT' Makefile | tail -45; sed -n '1,100p' host/gambit/gen-seed.ss; cat /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-inv/p1b-inv/ffi-call-sites.md | tail -95; rg -n 'Q[1-6]' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795020000000-engineer-p1b-inventory.glm-5.3-flash.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns jolt.backend-scheme.ffi\n  \"jolt.ffi lowering for the Scheme back end: foreign procedures — fixed,\n  declared-tail varargs and bare-marker varargs — foreign callables, aggregate\n  layouts, and the marshaling across the C boundary in both directions.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [jolt.backend-scheme.names :refer [chez-str-lit]]\n            [jolt.backend-scheme.session :refer [fresh-label target]]))\n\n;; jolt.ffi/__cfn -> a Chez foreign-procedure (jolt-ffi). The C symbol + types are\n;; compile-time literals from the analyzer, so this emits a real typed binding;\n;; the resulting Scheme procedure is callable like any jolt fn. The library must\n;; have loaded the shared object (jolt.ffi/load-library) before this def runs.\n;; Keep this in agreement with ffi-type->chez in host/chez/java/ffi.ss: these are\n;; the compile-time signature and runtime memory halves of one public contract.\n;; This table is baked into each checked-in compiler seed.\n(def ^:private ffi-types\n  {\"int\" \"int\" \"uint\" \"unsigned-int\"\n   \"int8\" \"integer-8\" \"i8\" \"integer-8\"\n   \"int16\" \"integer-16\" \"short\" \"integer-16\"\n   \"uint16\" \"unsigned-16\" \"ushort\" \"unsigned-16\"\n   \"int32\" \"integer-32\" \"uint32\" \"unsigned-32\"\n   \"long\" \"long\" \"ulong\" \"unsigned-long\"\n   \"int64\" \"integer-64\" \"uint64\" \"unsigned-64\" \"size_t\" \"size_t\" \"ssize_t\" \"ssize_t\"\n   \"iptr\" \"iptr\" \"uptr\" \"uptr\" \"double\" \"double\" \"float\" \"float\"\n   \"pointer\" \"void*\" \"void*\" \"void*\" \"string\" \"string\" \"void\" \"void\"\n   \"uint8\" \"unsigned-8\" \"u8\" \"unsigned-8\" \"byte\" \"unsigned-8\" \"char\" \"char\"\n   ;; :bool is a ONE-BYTE C boolean (C99 _Bool / stdbool.h), so it travels as\n   ;; unsigned-8 and the value is converted at the boundary — Chez's own\n   ;; `boolean` foreign type is int-sized, which is the wrong width for _Bool\n   ;; and would read three bytes of whatever sat next to it on a return.\n   \"bool\" \"unsigned-8\"})\n(defn ffi-type->chez [t]\n  (or (ffi-types t) (throw (ex-info (str \"jolt.ffi: unknown foreign type :\" t) {}))))\n\n(defn- emit-ffi-layout-ftype [type]\n  (cond\n    (string? type) (ffi-type->chez type)\n    ;; A union is the same member list under Chez's other aggregate ftype, so it\n    ;; gets its size, alignment and (all-equal) member offsets from ftype-sizeof\n    ;; and ftype-&ref exactly as a struct does — no layout arithmetic here.\n    (or (= :struct (:ffi-kind type)) (= :union (:ffi-kind type)))\n    (str \"(\" (if (= :union (:ffi-kind type)) \"union\" \"struct\") \" \"\n         (str/join\n          \" \"\n          (map-indexed\n           (fn [i field]\n             (str \"[f\" i \" \" (emit-ffi-layout-ftype (:type field)) \"]\"))\n           (:fields type)))\n         \")\")\n    (= :array (:ffi-kind type))\n    (str \"(array \" (:count type) \" \" (emit-ffi-layout-ftype (:type type)) \")\")\n    :else\n    (throw (ex-info \"jolt.ffi: invalid analyzed layout type\" {:type type}))))\n\n(declare ffi-layout-descendant-entries)\n\n(def ^:private ffi-layout-index-marker ::ffi-layout-index)\n\n(defn- ffi-layout-entry [type public-path emitted-path]\n  (cons {:path public-path :emitted-path emitted-path :type type}\n        (ffi-layout-descendant-entries type public-path emitted-path)))\n\n(defn- ffi-layout-descendant-entries [type public-path emitted-path]\n  (cond\n    (string? type) []\n    (or (= :struct (:ffi-kind type)) (= :union (:ffi-kind type)))\n    (mapcat\n     (fn [i field]\n       (ffi-layout-entry (:type field)\n                         (conj public-path (:name field))\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__auto-guard!\" \"auto arenas (collector-reclaimed) need guardians over foreign memory, unqualified in stage-1\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__auto-reclaimed\" \"auto arenas (collector-reclaimed) need guardians over foreign memory, unqualified in stage-1\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"__gc-stall-reporter!\" \"the GC stall watch has no hook on this target (sa-gc-install-stall-watch! answers #f)\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"stack-args-correct?\" \"the Chez #1091 stack-args probe is Chez-ABI-only and is not re-probed under the Gambit ABI in stage-1\")\n(joltffi-refuse-var! \"load-native\" \"superseded by load-library on this target (the adapter's scoped loader is the single dlopen path)\")\n\n;; ---- implemented rows -----------------------------------------------------------\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"load-library\" joltffi-load-library)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"loaded?\" joltffi-loaded?)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"load-system-library\" joltffi-load-system-library)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"system-library-candidates\"\n  (lambda (n) (make-pvec (list->vector (joltffi-system-library-candidates n)))))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"load-failure-note\" joltffi-load-failure-note-var)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"find-symbol\" joltffi-find-symbol)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"dlsym-native\" jolt-ffi-dlsym-native)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"defining-libraries\" joltffi-defining-libraries)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"alloc\" joltffi-alloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"free\" joltffi-free)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__alloc\" joltffi-alloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__free\" joltffi-free)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__calloc\" joltffi-calloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"read\" joltffi-read-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"write\" joltffi-write-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__read\" joltffi-read-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__write\" joltffi-write-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"copy\" joltffi-copy)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__copy\" joltffi-copy)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"sizeof\" (lambda (ty) (joltffi-sizeof-chez (joltffi-type->chez ty))))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__sizeof\" (lambda (ty) (joltffi-sizeof-chez (joltffi-type->chez ty))))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__size\" joltffi-recorded-size)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__remember-size!\" joltffi-remember-size!)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__forget-sizes!\" joltffi-forget-sizes!)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"read-bytes\" joltffi-read-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"write-bytes\" joltffi-write-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__read-bytes\" joltffi-read-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__write-bytes\" joltffi-write-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"null?\" (lambda (p) (if (joltffi-null? p) #t #f)))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"null\" joltffi-null)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"ptr->string\" joltffi-ptr->string)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"string->ptr\" joltffi-string->ptr)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__string->ptr\" joltffi-string->ptr)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__utf8-length\" joltffi-utf8-length)\n;; eval-test.ss — the G3 gate for the Gambit compiler path (jolt-mj95.4).\n;;\n;; Run via `make gambiteval` (detection-gated, from the repo root). Boots the\n;; full manifest + the cross-minted :gambit seed, then drives real jolt SOURCE\n;; through jolt-compile-eval and compares the jolt-pr-readable rendering\n;; against values captured from the Chez build (bin/jolt -e \"(pr-str EXPR)\").\n;; The same rows run compiled-to-js under node (manual; see the demo recipe in\n;; the site docs) — this gate pins the gsi half.\n\n(##include \"boot.ss\")\n\n(define failures 0)\n\n(define (check src expected)\n  (let ((actual (guard (e (#t \"THREW\"))\n                  (jolt-pr-readable (jolt-compile-eval src \"user\")))))\n    (if (string=? actual expected)\n        (printf \"  ok     ~a => ~a\\n\" src actual)\n        (begin (printf \"  FAIL   ~a: got ~s expected ~s\\n\" src actual expected)\n               (set! failures (+ failures 1))))))\n\n(printf \"== jolt source through jolt-compile-eval on gsi ==\\n\")\n\n;; arithmetic + tower\n(check \"(+ 1 2)\" \"3\")\n(check \"(* 2/3 6)\" \"4\")\n(check \"(+ 9007199254740993 1)\" \"9007199254740994\")\n;; collections + rendering\n(check \"{:a 1 :b 2}\" \"{:a 1, :b 2}\")\n(check \"(conj [1 2] 3)\" \"[1 2 3]\")\n(check \"(assoc {:a 1} :b 2)\" \"{:a 1, :b 2}\")\n;; lazy seqs + HOFs through the prelude\n(check \"(map inc [1 2 3])\" \"(2 3 4)\")\n(check \"(->> (range 100) (filter odd?) (map #(* % %)) (reduce +))\" \"166650\")\n(check \"(->> (range 20) (filter even?) (map inc) (take 5) vec)\" \"[1 3 5 7 9]\")\n;; def + cross-row invocation + recursion\n(check \"(defn fib [n] (if (< n 2) n (+ (fib (- n 1)) (fib (- n 2)))))\" \"#'user/fib\")\n(check \"(fib 20)\" \"6765\")\n;; let/loop\n(check \"(let [x 10] (* x x))\" \"100\")\n(check \"(loop [i 0 acc 0] (if (< i 5) (recur (inc i) (+ acc i)) acc))\" \"10\")\n;; strings + regex\n(check \"(str \\\"jolt on \\\" \\\"gambit\\\")\" \"\\\"jolt on gambit\\\"\")\n(check \"(re-seq #\\\"[a-z]+\\\" \\\"jolt on gambit js\\\")\" \"(\\\"jolt\\\" \\\"on\\\" \\\"gambit\\\" \\\"js\\\")\")\n;; defmacro then use in a later row\n(check \"(defmacro unless2 [c a b] (list 'if c b a))\" \"nil\")\n(check \"(unless2 false :yes :no)\" \":yes\")\n;; try/catch\n(check \"(try (/ 1 0) (catch Exception e :caught))\" \":caught\")\n;; sort with comparator\n(check \"(sort > [3 1 4 1 5 9 2 6])\" \"(9 6 5 4 3 2 1 1)\")\n;; records + protocols\n(check \"(defrecord Pt [x y])\" \"#'user/map->Pt\")\n(check \"(:x (->Pt 3 4))\" \"3\")\n(check \"(pr-str (->Pt 1 2))\" \"\\\"#user.Pt{:x 1, :y 2}\\\"\")\n(check \"(defprotocol Shape (perim [s]))\" \"#'user/perim\")\n(check \"(defrecord Sq [w] Shape (perim [s] (* 4 (:w s))))\" \"nil\")\n(check \"(perim (->Sq 5))\" \"20\")\n;; multimethods\n(check \"(defmulti area :shape)\" \"#'user/area\")\n(check \"(area {:shape :circle :r 21})\" \"THREW\")   ; no method yet -> throws\n(check \"(defmethod area :circle [c] (* 2 (:r c)))\" \"#object[clojure.lang.MultiFn 0x0 \\\"area\\\"]\")\n(check \"(area {:shape :circle :r 21})\" \"42\")\n;; anonymous fns + map results\n(check \"((fn [a b] {:sum (+ a b) :prod (* a b)}) 3 4)\" \"{:sum 7, :prod 12}\")\n;; deftype interface surface: a CharSequence window answers count/seq/nth and the\n;; regex entry points, and a collection deftype prints in its collection's shape.\n;; These live in records.ss, so they reach here only through the GENERATED\n;; records-gambit.ss — a stale generation shows up as a failure on these rows.\n(check (string-append \"(do (deftype Sg [s cnt] CharSequence (length [_] cnt)\"\n                      \" (charAt [_ i] (.charAt s i)) (subSequence [_ a b] (subs s a b))\"\n                      \" (toString [_] (subs s 0 cnt)))\"\n                      \" [(count (->Sg \\\"abcd\\\" 3)) (vec (seq (->Sg \\\"abcd\\\" 3))) (nth (->Sg \\\"abcd\\\" 3) 1)])\")\n       \"[3 [\\\\a \\\\b \\\\c] \\\\b]\")\n(check (string-append \"(do (deftype Sgr [s cnt] CharSequence (length [_] cnt)\"\n                      \" (charAt [_ i] (.charAt s i)) (subSequence [_ a b] (subs s a b))\"\n                      \" (toString [_] (subs s 0 cnt)))\"\n                      \" (re-matches #\\\"a+\\\" (->Sgr \\\"aaa\\\" 3)))\")\n       \"\\\"aaa\\\"\")\n(check (string-append \"(do (deftype Psq [v] clojure.lang.ISeq (seq [_] (seq v))\"\n                      \" (first [_] (first v)) (next [_] (next (seq v))) (more [_] (rest (seq v)))\"\n                      \" (count [_] (count v)) (equiv [_ o] (= (seq v) o)) (empty [_] nil)\"\n                      \" (cons [_ o] (cons o (seq v))))\"\n                      \" [(pr-str (->Psq [1 2 3])) (clojure.string/replace (str (->Psq [1 2 3])) #\\\"@[0-9a-f]+\\\" \\\"@H\\\")])\")\n       ;; str is toString, which a deftype implementing ISeq does not override:\n       ;; Object's Class@hash, as on the JVM\n       \"[\\\"(1 2 3)\\\" \\\"user.Psq@H\\\"]\")\n;; the runtime target must never emit chez unsafe spellings\n(check \"(count \\\"gambit\\\")\" \"6\")\n\n;; ---- host tier: the names the excluded java/ tree owns on Chez ---------------\n;; `time` reaches current-time-ms and the printer's host-writer probe; both were\n;; unbound names before host-vars.ss, so the macro died with a bare Gambit error.\n(check \"(time 1)\" \"1\")\n(check \"(time (reduce + (range 100)))\" \"4950\")\n(check \"(> (current-time-ms) 1700000000000)\" \"true\")\n(check \"(do (flush) :ok)\" \":ok\")\n\n;; A type this target cannot construct answers the question instead of raising.\n(check \"(delay? 1)\" \"false\")\n\n(define (test-sa-surface)\n  (printf \"== sa-* runtime surface ==\\n\")\n  (check \"sa-host-tag\" (sa-host-tag) \"gambit\")\n  (check \"sa-os-family (documented else-default)\" (sa-os-family) 'linux)\n  (check \"sa-arch (degraded)\" (sa-arch) 'other)\n  (check \"sa-endian\" (sa-endian) 'little)\n  (check \"sa-real-time-ms is an exact integer\" (exact-integer? (sa-real-time-ms)) #t)\n  (check \"sa-real-time-ms advances\"\n         (let ((a (sa-real-time-ms)))\n           (thread-sleep! 0.01)\n           (>= (sa-real-time-ms) a)) #t)\n  ;; mtime needs a real file; under the js exe there is no repo cwd (same\n  ;; detection as the contract pass), so these two rows skip there\n  (if (contract-file-path)\n      (begin\n        (check \"sa-file-mtime-ms on an existing file\"\n               (exact-integer? (sa-file-mtime-ms \"host/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt\")) #t)\n        (check \"sa-file-mtime-ms is a plausible epoch-ms (> 1e12)\"\n               (> (sa-file-mtime-ms \"host/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt\") 1000000000000) #t))\n      (printf \"  skip   sa-file-mtime-ms rows (no repo cwd under the js exe)\\n\"))\n  (check \"sa-introspect-enabled? fixed #f\" (sa-introspect-enabled?) #f)\n  (check \"sa-continuation-frames -> '()\" (sa-continuation-frames #f) '())\n  (check \"sa-procedure-info -> #f\" (sa-procedure-info (lambda () 1)) #f)\n  (check \"sa-stats zero vector\" (sa-stats) #(0 0 0 0 0 0 0))\n  (check \"sa-profile-instrument! refuses on\" (sa-profile-instrument! #t) #f)\n  (check \"sa-profile-instrument! off succeeds\" (sa-profile-instrument! #f) #t)\n  (check \"sa-profile-instrumenting? fixed #f\" (sa-profile-instrumenting?) #f)\n  (check \"sa-profile-compile calls its thunk\" (sa-profile-compile (lambda () 7)) 7)\n  (check \"sa-profile-counts -> '()\" (sa-profile-counts) '())\n  (check \"sa-profile-release! -> '()\" (sa-profile-release!) '())\n  (check \"sa-block-profile-dump! -> 0\" (sa-block-profile-dump! \"/nonexistent/p.jpd\" \"release\") 0)\n  (check \"sa-block-profile-load-unit! -> #f\" (sa-block-profile-load-unit! '() \"x.ss\") #f)\n  (check \"sa-stack-walk -> #f\" (sa-stack-walk #f 1 (lambda (c o f) #t)) #f)\n  (check \"sa-frame-source-pair -> #f\" (sa-frame-source-pair #f) #f)\n  (check \"sa-code-name -> #f\" (sa-code-name #f) #f)\n  (check \"sa-thread-cpu-nanos -> 0\" (sa-thread-cpu-nanos) 0)\n  (check \"sa-baked-global -> #f always\" (sa-baked-global 'jolt-baked-version-early) #f)\n  (check \"sa-gc-collect no-ops\" (sa-gc-collect) #f)\n  (check \"sa-gc-max-generation 0\" (sa-gc-max-generation) 0)\n  ;; the ffi tier: EVERY entry raises a message-carrying condition\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-foreign-alloc\" (lambda () (sa-foreign-alloc 16))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-foreign-procedure (syntax)\" (lambda () (sa-foreign-procedure \"f\" (int) int))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-foreign-procedure-native-error (syntax)\"\n                       (lambda ()\n                         (sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error\n                                                            () \"f\" (int) int))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"jolt-ffi-native-error-procedure (target wrapper)\"\n                       (lambda ()\n                         (jolt-ffi-native-error-procedure () \"f\" (int) int))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-foreign-procedure-blocking (syntax)\" (lambda () (sa-foreign-procedure-blocking \"f\" (int) int))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-foreign-callable (syntax)\" (lambda () (sa-foreign-callable (lambda () 1) (int) int))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-foreign-callable-collect-safe (syntax)\" (lambda () (sa-foreign-callable-collect-safe (lambda () 1) (int) int))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-load-shared-object\" (lambda () (sa-load-shared-object \"libx\"))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-lock-object\" (lambda () (sa-lock-object (list 1)))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-foreign-entry?\" (lambda () (sa-foreign-entry? \"f\"))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-foreign-entry-address\" (lambda () (sa-foreign-entry-address \"f\"))\n                       \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-compile-file\" (lambda () (sa-compile-file \"a.ss\" \"a.so\" #f))\n                       \"native compilation is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-make-boot-file\" (lambda () (sa-make-boot-file \"out.boot\" '()))\n                       \"native compilation is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-fasl-write\" (lambda () (sa-fasl-write 42 (open-output-string)))\n                       \"fasl serialization is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-fasl-read\" (lambda () (sa-fasl-read (open-input-string \"\")))\n                       \"fasl serialization is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n  (check-raise-message \"sa-run-process\" (lambda () (sa-run-process \"echo hi\" #f))\n                       \"subprocess support is unsupported on the gambit target\"))\n\n;; ---- continuations tier — the one-shot escape primitive ---------------------\n;; The gambit target IMPLEMENTS this tier rather than degrading, so these rows\n;; assert real behaviour, not an honest-failure message. The two refusals are\n;; the whole reason the adapter wraps call/cc at all: call/cc is multi-shot and\n;; would happily graft control back into a frame that already finished.\n(define (test-continuations)\n  (printf \"== continuations: one-shot escape (call/cc + spent flag) ==\\n\")\n  (check \"escape returns its value\"\n         (sa-call-with-escape-continuation (lambda (k) (k 'escaped) 'not-reached))\n         'escaped)\n  (check \"falling through returns the body value\"\n         (sa-call-with-escape-continuation (lambda (k) 'fell-through))\n         'fell-through)\n  (check \"escape leaves a loop from depth\"\n         (sa-call-with-escape-continuation\n          (lambda (k) (let loop ((i 0)) (if (= i 100) (k i) (loop (+ i 1))))))\n         100)\n  ;; An escape is a real exit: the dynamic-wind chain between the capture and\n  ;; the escape unwinds, which is what makes a jolt `finally` run.\n  (check \"escape unwinds dynamic-wind\"\n         (let ((log '()))\n           (sa-call-with-escape-continuation\n            (lambda (k)\n              (dynamic-wind\n                (lambda () (set! log (cons 'in log)))\n                (lambda () (k 'out))\n                (lambda () (set! log (cons 'out log))))))\n           (reverse log))\n         '(in out))\n  (check-raise-message \"second invocation refused\"\n                       (lambda ()\n                         (let ((saved #f))\n2117:\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n2118:\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib.sha256\n2123:$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib: $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt \\\n2124:\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c\n2126:\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n2127:\tprintf 'int joltffi_dep_marker(void){return 1;}\\n' > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/dep.c\n2128:\tcc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/dep.c\n2130:\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/unloadable.c\n2131:\tcc -O1 -dynamiclib -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n2132:\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/unloadable.c \\\n2133:\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n2134:\trm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n2135:\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n2136:\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib.sha256\n2139:gambitffi-bridge: $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 \\\n2140:                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n2141:                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n2142:                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\n2145:\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n2146:\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-abi.ss; \\\n2148:\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n2152:\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n2153:\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-errno.ss; \\\n2155:\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n2159:\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n2160:\t\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 90 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/gambitffi-load-failure.ss; \\\n2162:\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n2169:# The browser bundle: the whole stack (kernel + seed + compiler + a queue-polling\n2171:# raw / ~4MB gzipped, which is what a web server ships. Point GAMBIT_WEB_OUT at\n2173:#   make gambitweb GAMBIT_WEB_OUT=../jolt-lang.github.io/resources/static/js/jolt-web.js\n2181:GAMBIT_WEB_OUT ?= target/gambit/jolt-web.js\n2183:\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" ]; then \\\n2185:\t\tmkdir -p \"$$(dirname \"$(GAMBIT_WEB_OUT)\")\"; \\\n2186:\t\tout=\"$$(cd \"$$(dirname \"$(GAMBIT_WEB_OUT)\")\" && pwd)/$$(basename \"$(GAMBIT_WEB_OUT)\")\"; \\\n2187:\t\t(cd host/gambit && \"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" -target js -exe -o \"$$out\" repl-main.ss); \\\n2188:\t\techo \"gambitweb: $(GAMBIT_WEB_OUT) ($$(wc -c < \"$$out\" | tr -d ' ') bytes,\\\n2191:\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n2194:# G3 compiler-on-gsi (jolt-mj95.4): cross-mint the Gambit seed from the Chez\n2195:# seed ON CHEZ with the backend target at :gambit (R9), grep-verifying the\n2196:# emission contains no chez-only spelling before writing host/gambit/seed/.\n2197:# Runs on CHEZ (gambitseed), not gsi.\n2198:gambitseed:\n2199:\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-seed.ss\n2201:# Re-mint the seed after changing a seed source (reader/analyzer/backend/core).\n2223:# builds: it touches host/chez/rt.ss and seed/prelude.ss to test its own cache\n;; gen-seed.ss — cross-mint the GAMBIT seed from the Chez seed, ON CHEZ.\n;; jolt-mj95.4 (G3). Run via `make gambitseed`:\n;;   $(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-seed.ss\n;;\n;; WHY: the checked-in Chez seed (host/chez/seed/{prelude,image}.ss) is emitted\n;; with the backend's :chez target — its unsafe #3% op spellings cannot load on\n;; Gambit. This script loads the Chez seed exactly as bootstrap.ss does, flips\n;; the backend target to :gambit (R9 set-target!), re-emits both artifacts on\n;; Chez, and writes them to host/gambit/seed/{prelude,image}.ss. The output is\n;; the SAME compiler (analyzer/emitter/passes) and the same clojure.core prelude,\n;; emitted as portable Scheme: every #3%-derived spelling degrades to the safe\n;; op (unsafe-prefix -> nil -> \"\").\n;;\n;; Safety net: the script greps its own output for \"#3%\" and \"(foreign-procedure\"\n;; and FAILS (nonzero exit, no files written) rather than emitting a chez-flavored\n;; seed — the R9 table is the only sanctioned source of target-specific spelling,\n;; and anything else chez-only that surfaces here must go through the supervisor.\n;;\n;; Generated files, checked in like the chez seed (the seed-mint pattern).\n\n(import (chezscheme))\n\n(load \"host/chez/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss\")  ; before rt.ss: macros + top-levels in rt.ss/java/*.ss call sa-*\n(load \"host/chez/rt.ss\")\n(set-chez-ns! \"clojure.core\")\n(load \"host/chez/seed/prelude.ss\")\n(load \"host/chez/post-prelude.ss\")\n(set-chez-ns! \"user\")\n(load \"host/chez/host-contract.ss\")\n(load \"host/chez/seed/image.ss\")\n(load \"host/chez/compile-eval.ss\")\n(load \"host/chez/emit-image.ss\")\n\n;; Flip the emission target to :gambit (R9). Every unsafe-prim site derives its\n;; spelling from (unsafe-prefix) -> (get-in target-prims [(target) :unsafe-prefix]);\n;; :gambit is not in the table, so the prefix degrades to the checked op.\n;; The target lives on the PUBLISHED unit (backend_scheme.clj (cur) ->\n;; jolt.op-registry/current-unit-box), and emit-image's ei-publish-unit! swaps in\n;; its own fresh unit (new-unit defaults :target to :chez) — so publish FIRST,\n;; then set, or the mint reads :chez.\n(ei-fresh-unit!)\n;; compile-eval.ss turned prelude-mode ON (needed to emit clojure.core refs) on\n;; the unit that was current at ITS load time; the fresh unit we just published\n;; defaults prelude-mode #f — restore it, then set the target.\n(let ((spm (var-deref \"jolt.backend-scheme\" \"set-prelude-mode!\")))\n  (if (procedure? spm) (spm #t)\n      (begin (display \"gen-seed: WARNING set-prelude-mode! not found\\n\") (exit 1))))\n;; Same reason as prelude-mode above: emit-image.ss turned var cell-hoisting ON on\n;; the unit current at ITS load time, and the fresh unit published here defaults it\n;; off. Without this the Gambit seed silently keeps the un-hoisted (var-deref ns\n;; name) shape — correct, but ~102ns per core var reference where the Chez seed\n;; pays ~1ns. dyn-binding.ss (which defines var-cell-deref) is ##included at\n;; boot.ss:83 / boot-full.ss:90, ahead of seed/prelude.ss, so the hoisted reader\n;; is bound before any hoisted cell is read.\n(let ((svc (var-deref \"jolt.backend-scheme\" \"set-var-cache!\")))\n  (if (procedure? svc) (svc #t)\n      (begin (display \"gen-seed: WARNING set-var-cache! not found\\n\") (exit 1))))\n(let ((st (var-deref \"jolt.backend-scheme\" \"set-target!\")))\n  (if (procedure? st)\n      (begin (st (keyword #f \"gambit\"))\n             (display \"gen-seed: backend target -> :gambit\\n\"))\n      (begin (display \"gen-seed: WARNING set-target! not found in seed image\\n\")\n             (exit 1))))\n\n;; Emit both artifacts to strings FIRST, verify, then write. A chez-flavored\n;; emission must fail without producing files.\n(ei-reset-skipped!)\n(define gs-prelude (jolt-emit-prelude))\n(define gs-image (jolt-emit-image))\n\n\n\n;; A \"#3%\" occurrence is a chez-only EMISSION only when it is a USE\n;; (e.g. \"(#3%vector-ref ...)\" / \"(#3%fl+ ...)\" — a paren/whitespace right\n;; before it). A \"#3%\" inside a string literal is DATA — the compiled\n;; target-prims table itself carries the :unsafe-prefix value \"#3%\", and that\n;; literal must survive into the gambit image (the runtime consults it).\n(define (gs-use? text i)\n  (let ((c (if (> i 0) (string-ref text (- i 1)) #\\space)))\n    (or (char=? c #\\() (char=? c #\\space) (char=? c #\\newline))))\n\n(define (gs-verify text what)\n  (let loop ((i 0) (uses '()) (n 0))\n    (let ((j (gs-index-at text \"#3%\" i)))\n      (if (< j 0)\n          (begin\n            (when (pair? uses)\n              (fprintf (current-error-port)\n                       \"gen-seed: FAIL ~a has ~a #3% USE(s) — chez-flavored emission, not writing a gambit seed\\n\"\n                       what (length uses))\n              (for-each (lambda (k)\n                          (let ((lo (max 0 (- k 60))) (hi (min (string-length text) (+ k 80))))\n                            (fprintf (current-error-port) \"gen-seed:   ...~a...\\n\"\n                                     (substring text lo hi))))\n                        (reverse uses))\n              (exit 1))\n            (display (string-append \"gen-seed: \" what \" #3% occurrences: \" (number->string n)\n                                    \" (all inside string data, none as op uses)\\n\")))\n          (let ((use? (gs-use? text j)))\n            (loop (+ j 3)\nconvention selector (`host/chez/rt.ss:359-367`; Gambit adapter defines its own\nrefusing one at `host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:339-343`).\n\nGambit adapter status on this SHA (`host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss`):\nthe entire ffi tier raises `sa-ffi-raise` (313-314) — sa-foreign-procedure\n321-324, native-error 331-334, blocking 349-352, callable 358-360,\ncallable-collect-safe 365-367, procedure-runtime 374-375, data plane 381-420,\npins 428-435, loader 440-461. All message-carrying\n(`\"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\"`).\n\n### Backend primitive table (astra §2 item)\n\n`target-prims` moved from backend_scheme.clj to\n`jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj:76-78`:\n\n```clojure\n(def ^:private target-prims\n  {:chez {:unsafe-prefix \"#3%\"}})\n(defn unsafe-prefix [] (get-in target-prims [(target) :unsafe-prefix]))\n```\n\n- Astra cited backend_scheme.clj:297 — moved (this file is 1714 lines; see §5).\n- What a `:gambit` entry must carry: `{:unsafe-prefix \"\"}` — exactly astra's\n  ruling. Today `:gambit` is absent and the lookup answers `nil`; every\n  spelling site string-concatenates the prefix (`backend_scheme.clj:1248-1249`\n  flonum cast window, `backend_scheme/calls.clj:152` PIC probe; seven sites\n  per session.clj:70-74), so `(str nil)` degrades to the checked op by\n  accident. `host/gambit/gen-seed.ss:34-35` documents the degradation;\n  `host/gambit/eval-test.ss:269-279` pins that `^double` emission carries no\n  `#3%`. The explicit `:gambit {:unsafe-prefix \"\"}` entry is still OPEN work\n  (P1, not P1b).\n\n---\n\n## 4. What the Gambit target does TODAY with each construction path (static reading)\n\n1. **Pointer-call bindings** — refused at compile time with a jolt-level\n   message (ffi.clj:625-628). Good.\n2. **By-value callables** — refused at compile time (ffi.clj:763-771). Good.\n3. **Scalar callables** — emit `(jolt-ffi-register-callable! (sa-foreign-callable …))`;\n   on gambit `sa-foreign-callable` is the refusing macro\n   (gambit adapter:358-360) and is evaluated before the unbound register call\n   (argument evaluation first), so the documented refusal fires. Good — but\n   only because of evaluation order, not by construction.\n4. **Named scalar/aggregate fns** — the emitted `(or p …)` first-call body\n   references `jolt-ffi-dlsym-native` and bare `foreign-procedure` (ffi.clj:483-491).\n   The gambit boot manifest excludes `host/chez/java/ffi.ss` entirely\n   (host/gambit/boot.ss ##include list, lines 47-104: regex-translate,\n   jdk-interfaces, class-hierarchy, records-interop, host-class, java-parse,\n   math, class-model, string-builder, dot-forms, jutil-colls, tree-map,\n   byte-buffer — no ffi.ss), and gsi has no `foreign-procedure` form. **First\n   call therefore dies on an UNBOUND VARIABLE, not the documented\n   message-carrying unsupported error.** GAP G-3: the compiler needs a\n   `:gambit` arm in `ffi-named-procedure-expr` (or an adapter-bound\n   `foreign-procedure` that raises the documented way) so unregistered shapes\n   \"raise deliberately, rather than reach an unbound Chez identifier\"\n   (astra §2, verbatim requirement).\n5. **Layouts (`:ffi-layout`)** — emitted `(define-ftype …)` /\n   `(make-ftype-pointer …)` are unbound on gambit; a `(def … (ffi/layout …))`\n   on the gambit target raises unbound at namespace load. GAP G-1: no gambit\n   guard in `emit-ffi-node` for `:ffi-layout` (ffi.clj:758-772 guards only\n   pointer fns and by-value callables).\n6. **Bare varargs** — the cache constructor references\n   `jolt-ffi-varargs-cache` (unbound on gambit); first call raises unbound.\n   Covered by the same GAP G-3 arm.\n7. **`jolt build --library` launcher** — build.ss:4647-4653 emits Chez-only\n   callable/foreign-procedure text; stays Chez-only (AOT refused on gambit).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-check of astra's citations against THIS fork SHA\n\n| Astra citation | Status on a6852ef8 | Actual |\n|---|---|---|\n| `backend_scheme.clj:2134` scoped symbol calls emit raw Chez `foreign-procedure` | MOVED (backend_scheme.clj is 1714 lines) | `jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj:488-491` (`ffi-named-procedure-expr`, scoped branch); file split into `backend_scheme/` subdirectory |\n| `backend_scheme.clj:297` only-Chez primitive-table entry | MOVED | `jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj:76-78` (`target-prims` `{:chez {:unsafe-prefix \"#3%\"}}`) |\n| `host/chez/java/ffi.ss:1294` runtime varargs eval construction | MOVED (line is now inside the carrier comment block) | `host/chez/java/ffi.ss:1373-1386` (`ffi-varargs-compile`); convention helpers 1364-1371 |\n| `host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:321-459` refusals | HOLDS (±2 lines) | refusal tier spans 307-461; `sa-foreign-procedure` refusal starts at 321, `sa-foreign-callable-entry-point` ends at 461 |\n| `sa-gc-collect` no-op ~81 | HOLDS EXACTLY | `host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss:81-82` — `(define (sa-gc-collect) #f)` |\n| \"Gambit's boot excludes the FFI runtime\" | HOLDS | gambit boot ##include list has no java/ffi.ss (host/gambit/boot.ss:47-104); adapter comment at gambit adapter:17-19 states the manifest exclusion |\n| \"four sa-foreign-* syntaxes\" contract wording | HOLDS — and is worse | TARGET-CONTRACT.md:21-22 still says four; actual constructor surfaces are 7 (§3); CONTRACT.txt's capability-ffi tier additionally OMITS sa-foreign-callable / -collect-safe |\n\n## 6. Site counts (headline)\n\n- Compiler construction sites (§1): **22** sub-sites across 8 constructors\n  (named×3, pointer×3, fixed-fn assembly, bare-varargs×3, callable×5,\n  layout×1) + 13 compile-time refusal rows (§1.8) + 17 shadow-guard names (§1.9).\n- Runtime construction sites (§2): **2** dynamic `eval` constructors\n  (ffi-varargs-compile; sa-foreign-procedure-runtime) + **2** adapter-internal\n  constructor macros (jolt-foreign-proc-safe/-blocking) + ~180 adapter-internal\n  bootstrap binding sites (16 files) + **16** direct foreign-procedure sites\n  inside the Chez adapter file + scoped-address chain (4 sites) + callable\n  machinery (6 sites).\n- Adapter contract surface: 18 CONTRACT.txt names + 2 unlisted callable\n  syntaxes + 1 target-internal convention selector.\n87:   compiler already. But the guards are incomplete (see Open questions Q1/Q2).\n105:- **Q1 (gap G-1):** `emit-ffi-node` guards `:gambit` only for pointer-call fns\n110:- **Q2 (gap G-3):** named scalar/aggregate bindings on `:gambit` emit the same\n116:- **Q3:** `jolt_parser_worker_free` — now pinned with evidence: the C entry\n122:- **Q4:** the `:gambit` target-prims entry (`{:unsafe-prefix \"\"}`,\n125:- **Q5:** should `sa-foreign-callable`/`-collect-safe` be added to\n128:- **Q6:** mvn_http's SSL bindings call blocking-capable C (SSL_connect,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
