{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,85p' host/gambit/eval-test.ss; sed -n '80,94p' host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss; sed -n '715,810p' host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss; sed -n '386,430p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; sed -n '2194,2220p' Makefile; rg -n 'ffi.*target|set-target|foreign' host/gambit/eval-test.ss; command -v scheme; command -v python3; git log -3 --oneline; ls /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/bin; sed -n '226,270p' host/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt; rg --files | rg 'TARGET-CONTRACT'\"","aggregated_output":";; eval-test.ss — the G3 gate for the Gambit compiler path (jolt-mj95.4).\n;;\n;; Run via `make gambiteval` (detection-gated, from the repo root). Boots the\n;; full manifest + the cross-minted :gambit seed, then drives real jolt SOURCE\n;; through jolt-compile-eval and compares the jolt-pr-readable rendering\n;; against values captured from the Chez build (bin/jolt -e \"(pr-str EXPR)\").\n;; The same rows run compiled-to-js under node (manual; see the demo recipe in\n;; the site docs) — this gate pins the gsi half.\n\n(##include \"boot.ss\")\n\n(define failures 0)\n\n(define (check src expected)\n  (let ((actual (guard (e (#t \"THREW\"))\n                  (jolt-pr-readable (jolt-compile-eval src \"user\")))))\n    (if (string=? actual expected)\n        (printf \"  ok     ~a => ~a\\n\" src actual)\n        (begin (printf \"  FAIL   ~a: got ~s expected ~s\\n\" src actual expected)\n               (set! failures (+ failures 1))))))\n\n(printf \"== jolt source through jolt-compile-eval on gsi ==\\n\")\n\n;; arithmetic + tower\n(check \"(+ 1 2)\" \"3\")\n(check \"(* 2/3 6)\" \"4\")\n(check \"(+ 9007199254740993 1)\" \"9007199254740994\")\n;; collections + rendering\n(check \"{:a 1 :b 2}\" \"{:a 1, :b 2}\")\n(check \"(conj [1 2] 3)\" \"[1 2 3]\")\n(check \"(assoc {:a 1} :b 2)\" \"{:a 1, :b 2}\")\n;; lazy seqs + HOFs through the prelude\n(check \"(map inc [1 2 3])\" \"(2 3 4)\")\n(check \"(->> (range 100) (filter odd?) (map #(* % %)) (reduce +))\" \"166650\")\n(check \"(->> (range 20) (filter even?) (map inc) (take 5) vec)\" \"[1 3 5 7 9]\")\n;; def + cross-row invocation + recursion\n(check \"(defn fib [n] (if (< n 2) n (+ (fib (- n 1)) (fib (- n 2)))))\" \"#'user/fib\")\n(check \"(fib 20)\" \"6765\")\n;; let/loop\n(check \"(let [x 10] (* x x))\" \"100\")\n(check \"(loop [i 0 acc 0] (if (< i 5) (recur (inc i) (+ acc i)) acc))\" \"10\")\n;; strings + regex\n(check \"(str \\\"jolt on \\\" \\\"gambit\\\")\" \"\\\"jolt on gambit\\\"\")\n(check \"(re-seq #\\\"[a-z]+\\\" \\\"jolt on gambit js\\\")\" \"(\\\"jolt\\\" \\\"on\\\" \\\"gambit\\\" \\\"js\\\")\")\n;; defmacro then use in a later row\n(check \"(defmacro unless2 [c a b] (list 'if c b a))\" \"nil\")\n(check \"(unless2 false :yes :no)\" \":yes\")\n;; try/catch\n(check \"(try (/ 1 0) (catch Exception e :caught))\" \":caught\")\n;; sort with comparator\n(check \"(sort > [3 1 4 1 5 9 2 6])\" \"(9 6 5 4 3 2 1 1)\")\n;; records + protocols\n(check \"(defrecord Pt [x y])\" \"#'user/map->Pt\")\n(check \"(:x (->Pt 3 4))\" \"3\")\n(check \"(pr-str (->Pt 1 2))\" \"\\\"#user.Pt{:x 1, :y 2}\\\"\")\n(check \"(defprotocol Shape (perim [s]))\" \"#'user/perim\")\n(check \"(defrecord Sq [w] Shape (perim [s] (* 4 (:w s))))\" \"nil\")\n(check \"(perim (->Sq 5))\" \"20\")\n;; multimethods\n(check \"(defmulti area :shape)\" \"#'user/area\")\n(check \"(area {:shape :circle :r 21})\" \"THREW\")   ; no method yet -> throws\n(check \"(defmethod area :circle [c] (* 2 (:r c)))\" \"#object[clojure.lang.MultiFn 0x0 \\\"area\\\"]\")\n(check \"(area {:shape :circle :r 21})\" \"42\")\n;; anonymous fns + map results\n(check \"((fn [a b] {:sum (+ a b) :prod (* a b)}) 3 4)\" \"{:sum 7, :prod 12}\")\n;; deftype interface surface: a CharSequence window answers count/seq/nth and the\n;; regex entry points, and a collection deftype prints in its collection's shape.\n;; These live in records.ss, so they reach here only through the GENERATED\n;; records-gambit.ss — a stale generation shows up as a failure on these rows.\n(check (string-append \"(do (deftype Sg [s cnt] CharSequence (length [_] cnt)\"\n                      \" (charAt [_ i] (.charAt s i)) (subSequence [_ a b] (subs s a b))\"\n                      \" (toString [_] (subs s 0 cnt)))\"\n                      \" [(count (->Sg \\\"abcd\\\" 3)) (vec (seq (->Sg \\\"abcd\\\" 3))) (nth (->Sg \\\"abcd\\\" 3) 1)])\")\n       \"[3 [\\\\a \\\\b \\\\c] \\\\b]\")\n(check (string-append \"(do (deftype Sgr [s cnt] CharSequence (length [_] cnt)\"\n                      \" (charAt [_ i] (.charAt s i)) (subSequence [_ a b] (subs s a b))\"\n                      \" (toString [_] (subs s 0 cnt)))\"\n                      \" (re-matches #\\\"a+\\\" (->Sgr \\\"aaa\\\" 3)))\")\n       \"\\\"aaa\\\"\")\n(check (string-append \"(do (deftype Psq [v] clojure.lang.ISeq (seq [_] (seq v))\"\n                      \" (first [_] (first v)) (next [_] (next (seq v))) (more [_] (rest (seq v)))\"\n                      \" (count [_] (count v)) (equiv [_ o] (= (seq v) o)) (empty [_] nil)\"\n                      \" (cons [_ o] (cons o (seq v))))\"\n                      \" [(pr-str (->Psq [1 2 3])) (clojure.string/replace (str (->Psq [1 2 3])) #\\\"@[0-9a-f]+\\\" \\\"@H\\\")])\")\n       ;; str is toString, which a deftype implementing ISeq does not override:\n          (begin (set-box! b new) #t)\n          #f))))\n\n;; P1b-stage1: the REAL collection, not the pre-stage1 no-op. ##gc is Gambit's\n;; own collection entry (lib/_kernel.scm's (##gc)); a caller that drops its\n;; references before the call observes weak references cleared and the heap\n;; shrink — the behavioral witness in gambitcheck.ss asserts exactly that.\n;; Return value mirrors the Chez adapter's success spelling ('ok).\n(define (sa-gc-collect)\n  (##gc)\n  'ok)\n\n;; (sa-gc-max-generation) -> exact integer\n;; The deepest collectable generation, for callers mapping JVM generations.\n;; Contract: return the maximum generation argument sa-gc-collect accepts.\n    ((integer-8) (joltffi-ref-i8 addr off))\n    ((unsigned-8) (joltffi-ref-u8 addr off))\n    ((integer-16) (joltffi-ref-i16 addr off))\n    ((unsigned-16) (joltffi-ref-u16 addr off))\n    ((integer-32) (joltffi-ref-i32 addr off))\n    ((unsigned-32) (joltffi-ref-u32 addr off))\n    ((integer-64 size_t ssize_t long unsigned-long iptr) (joltffi-ref-i64 addr off))\n    ((unsigned-64 uptr) (joltffi-ref-u64 addr off))\n    ((double) (joltffi-ref-f64 addr off))\n    ((float) (joltffi-ref-f32 addr off))\n    ((void*) (joltffi-ref-u64 addr off))\n    ((char) (joltffi-ref-i8 addr off))\n    (else\n     (error 'sa-foreign-ref\n            (string-append \"jolt.ffi: unsupported foreign type \"\n                           (if (symbol? type) (symbol->string type) (object->string type))\n                           \" on the gambit target\")))))\n\n(define (sa-foreign-set! type addr off v)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'sa-foreign-set!)\n  (case type\n    ((int integer-32) (joltffi-set-i32! addr off v))\n    ((unsigned-int unsigned-32) (joltffi-set-u32! addr off v))\n    ((integer-8) (joltffi-set-i8! addr off v))\n    ((unsigned-8) (joltffi-set-u8! addr off v))\n    ((integer-16) (joltffi-set-i16! addr off v))\n    ((unsigned-16) (joltffi-set-u16! addr off v))\n    ((integer-64 size_t ssize_t long iptr) (joltffi-set-i64! addr off v))\n    ((unsigned-64 unsigned-long uptr) (joltffi-set-u64! addr off v))\n    ((double) (joltffi-set-f64! addr off v))\n    ((float) (joltffi-set-f32! addr off v))\n    ((void*) (joltffi-set-u64! addr off v))\n    ((char) (joltffi-set-i8! addr off v))\n    (else\n     (error 'sa-foreign-set!\n            (string-append \"jolt.ffi: unsupported foreign type \"\n                           (if (symbol? type) (symbol->string type) (object->string type))\n                           \" on the gambit target\")))))\n\n;; bulk octet moves: ONE block copy foreign<->bytevector per call, the same\n;; shape the Chez adapter's memcpy path gives. The bytevector's body is\n;; borrowed for the duration of the synchronous call only (no collection can\n;; run inside it on this runtime); a count past the bytevector's end raises\n;; here, before the bridge dereferences anything.\n(define (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! addr bv n)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref!)\n  (if (not (u8vector? bv))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy target must be a bytevector\"))\n  (if (> n (u8vector-length bv))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy count exceeds the bytevector\" n))\n  (if (not (= 0 (joltffi-bytes-to-bv! bv addr n)))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy refused by the bridge\" n)))\n\n(define (sa-foreign-bytes-set! addr bv n)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'sa-foreign-bytes-set!)\n  (if (not (u8vector? bv))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-set! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy source must be a bytevector\"))\n  (if (> n (u8vector-length bv))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-set! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy count exceeds the bytevector\" n))\n  (if (not (= 0 (joltffi-bytes-from-bv! addr bv n)))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-set! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy refused by the bridge\" n)))\n\n(define (sa-foreign-zero! addr n)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'sa-foreign-zero!)\n  (joltffi-zero addr n))\n\n;; sizes are exact constants for both supported legs (arm64 macOS, x86_64/arm64\n;; Linux — LP64). :bool travels as unsigned-8 (the ONE-BYTE C99 _Bool); the\n;; value conversion happens at the boundary, not in the width.\n(define (sa-foreign-sizeof type)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'sa-foreign-sizeof)\n  (case type\n    ((integer-8 char) 1)\n    ((unsigned-8) 1)\n    ((integer-16 unsigned-16) 2)\n    ((integer-32 unsigned-32 int unsigned-int float) 4)\n    ((integer-64 unsigned-64 size_t ssize_t long unsigned-long iptr uptr double void*) 8)\n    (else\n     (error 'sa-foreign-sizeof\n            (string-append \"jolt.ffi: no size for foreign type \"\n                           (if (symbol? type) (symbol->string type) (object->string type))\n                           \" on the gambit target\")))))\n\n;; (sa-lock-object x) -> never returns\n;; REFUSED (astra §2 Memory): Gambit's collector MOVES objects; rooting\n;; prevents reclamation but not relocation, and no verified pinning mechanism\n;; exists on 4.9.8. Inheriting the non-moving-collector no-op exemption would\n;; be a silent lie — a consistent refusal, never a one-sided pin.\n(define (sa-lock-object x)\n  (error 'sa-lock-object\n         \"object pinning is unsupported on the gambit target — the collector moves objects and no verified pinning mechanism exists\"))\n\n(define (sa-unlock-object x)\n  (error 'sa-unlock-object\n         \"object pinning is unsupported on the gambit target — the collector moves objects and no verified pinning mechanism exists\"))\n\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"alloc\" joltffi-alloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"free\" joltffi-free)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__alloc\" joltffi-alloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__free\" joltffi-free)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__calloc\" joltffi-calloc)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"read\" joltffi-read-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"write\" joltffi-write-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__read\" joltffi-read-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__write\" joltffi-write-fn)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"copy\" joltffi-copy)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__copy\" joltffi-copy)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"sizeof\" (lambda (ty) (joltffi-sizeof-chez (joltffi-type->chez ty))))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__sizeof\" (lambda (ty) (joltffi-sizeof-chez (joltffi-type->chez ty))))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__size\" joltffi-recorded-size)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__remember-size!\" joltffi-remember-size!)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__forget-sizes!\" joltffi-forget-sizes!)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"read-bytes\" joltffi-read-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"write-bytes\" joltffi-write-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__read-bytes\" joltffi-read-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__write-bytes\" joltffi-write-bytes)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"null?\" (lambda (p) (if (joltffi-null? p) #t #f)))\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"null\" joltffi-null)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"ptr->string\" joltffi-ptr->string)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"string->ptr\" joltffi-string->ptr)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__string->ptr\" joltffi-string->ptr)\n(def-var! \"jolt.ffi\" \"__utf8-length\" joltffi-utf8-length)\n# G3 compiler-on-gsi (jolt-mj95.4): cross-mint the Gambit seed from the Chez\n# seed ON CHEZ with the backend target at :gambit (R9), grep-verifying the\n# emission contains no chez-only spelling before writing host/gambit/seed/.\n# Runs on CHEZ (gambitseed), not gsi.\ngambitseed:\n\t$(CHEZ) --script host/gambit/gen-seed.ss\n\n# Re-mint the seed after changing a seed source (reader/analyzer/backend/core).\nremint:\n\t@sh host/chez/remint.sh\n\n# Precompile the runtime to target/dev/flat.so so dev bin/jolt boots ~10x faster\n# (loads the .so instead of compiling ~50 .ss files from source every invocation).\ndevboot: submodules\n\t@$(CHEZ) --script host/chez/make-devboot.ss\n\n# Precompile the gate boot preamble to target/dev/gate.so so a pass gate boots in\n# ~0.2s instead of ~1.5s (it spends nearly all of that loading the same six\n# runtime files from Chez source). Opt-in like devboot: gate-boot.ss uses the\n# image when it is present and newer than every input, and loads from source\n# otherwise, so nothing depends on this target and CI is unaffected. Worth it\n# when iterating on one pass gate; `make ci` runs them in parallel anyway.\ngateboot: submodules\n\t@$(CHEZ) --script host/chez/make-gateboot.ss\n\n# Smoke test: the gate boot image's staleness predicate. Drives\n# gate-boot-image-fresh? over synthetic input lists, so it boots no runtime,\n316:       \"\\\"jolt.ffi/pointer-fn: ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\\\"\")\n318:       \"\\\"jolt.ffi/pointer-fn: ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\\\"\")\n325:       \"\\\"jolt.ffi/foreign-callable: ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\\\"\")\n327:       \"\\\"jolt.ffi/foreign-callable: ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\\\"\")\n/usr/bin/python3\na6852ef8 Regenerate the checked-in seeds for the Sorted change\n46d4090b Honor clojure.lang.Sorted in sorted?, subseq and rsubseq for user types\ndd3c4a4b Merge pull request #1715 from burinc/fix/zone-rules-exception-hierarchy\ngambdoc\ngambuild-C\ngambuild-arm\ngambuild-java\ngambuild-js\ngambuild-php\ngambuild-python\ngambuild-riscv-32\ngambuild-riscv-64\ngambuild-ruby\ngambuild-x86\ngambuild-x86-64\ngambvcs\ngsc\ngsc-script\ngsi\ngsi-script\nscheme-ieee-1178-1990\nscheme-r4rs\nscheme-r5rs\nscheme-srfi-0\nsix\nsix-script\n# tier: capability-ffi\n# OUR OWN definitions in host/chez/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss (loaded FIRST in\n# the runtime manifest), not (chezscheme) exports — a target's adapter must\n# provide these SAME call shapes. Each is a one-liner over a blocklisted\n# ffi-tier native (foreign-alloc/free/ref/set!/sizeof, lock-object/unlock-object,\n# load-shared-object, foreign-entry?/foreign-callable-entry-point, or the\n# Windows-path eval'd foreign-procedure construction); adaptercheck loads the\n# runtime file and probes the combined environment. sa-foreign-procedure and\n# sa-foreign-procedure-blocking are SYNTAX (compile-time-typed lowering to the\n# native foreign-procedure form, __collect_safe in the blocking case) — a target\n# must provide them as macros with the same lowering. Permitted degradation, per\n# entry point:\n# - sa-lock-object/sa-unlock-object may BOTH no-op on a non-moving collector\n#   (never just one — that leaks or crashes);\n# - sa-load-shared-object must raise on targets without dlopen, and\n#   jolt.ffi/load-library must surface it as a clean jolt-level error;\n# - sa-foreign-procedure-blocking may collapse to plain sa-foreign-procedure\n#   ONLY if the collector never stops other threads (the R4 collect-safety\n#   semantic);\n# - the data-plane entries (alloc/free/ref/set!/sizeof) degrade none — a target\n#   with the ffi capability provides them; without it, jolt.ffi raises cleanly;\n# - sa-foreign-bytes-ref!/-set! are the BULK octet moves (a block copy between\n#   foreign memory and a bytevector). A target with no block move may implement\n#   them as a loop over its own foreign-ref/-set! — correct, and the constant\n#   they exist to remove comes back. They pass the bytevector to C by address,\n#   so a target must keep it address-stable for the call's duration and must\n#   NOT make them collect-safe.\nsa-foreign-alloc\nsa-foreign-free\nsa-foreign-ref\nsa-foreign-set!\nsa-foreign-bytes-ref!\nsa-foreign-bytes-set!\nsa-foreign-zero!\nsa-foreign-sizeof\nsa-lock-object\nsa-unlock-object\nsa-load-shared-object\nsa-foreign-entry?\nsa-foreign-entry-address\nsa-foreign-callable-entry-point\nsa-foreign-procedure-runtime\nsa-foreign-procedure\nsa-foreign-procedure-native-error\nsa-foreign-procedure-blocking\nhost/scheme-adapter/TARGET-CONTRACT.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
