{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The registry lookup also drops the variadic boundary. That makes fixed calls such as `socket(int,int,int)` select the `fcntl(int,int,...)` shim, which uses a different ABI on Apple arm64. I’m making that boundary part of shim identity and generating the typed wrappers from an explicit manifest. Blocking, callback, aggregate, and runtime-signature modes will keep deliberate refusals.\n"}}
