{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"env | rg 'THREAD_ID|SESSION_ID|CODEX_THREAD'; sed -n '98,140p' host/gambit/gambitcheck.ss; sed -n '1,90p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; sed -n '540,588p' jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj; sed -n '145,210p' jolt-core/jolt/analyzer/ffi.clj; sed -n '640,688p' jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj; sed -n '308,331p' host/gambit/seed/image.ss | head -c 100\"","aggregated_output":"CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=sess_f3d4cdfb-7255-40fc-bf4e-719726c6f3ba\nCLAUDE_SESSION_ID=sess_f3d4cdfb-7255-40fc-bf4e-719726c6f3ba\nCODEX_SESSION_ID=01a1f1f9-2d2b-71a2-b88a-1675b81dd975\nCODEX_THREAD_ID=01a1f1f9-2d2b-71a2-b88a-1675b81dd975\nZCODE_SESSION_ID=sess_f3d4cdfb-7255-40fc-bf4e-719726c6f3ba\n\n(define (strip-comment s)\n  (let ((n (string-length s)))\n    (let loop ((i 0))\n      (cond\n        ((>= i n) s)\n        ((or (char=? (string-ref s i) #\\#) (char=? (string-ref s i) #\\;))\n         (substring s 0 i))\n        (else (loop (+ i 1)))))))\n\n(define (contract-file-path)\n  ;; #f when unreachable — the js-compiled gate has no repo cwd (Gambit-js\n  ;; current-directory is not the node process cwd, and command-line carries\n  ;; no script path), so the contract-name pass SKIPS there; the unit tests\n  ;; are the behavioral proof. Under gsi via make, the repo-root path exists\n  ;; and the pass is mandatory.\n  (if (file-exists? \"host/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt\")\n      \"host/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt\"\n      (let* ((cl (command-line))\n             (sp (and (pair? cl) (pair? (cdr cl)) (cadr cl))))\n        (if (and sp (file-exists? sp))\n            (let* ((dir (substring sp 0 (- (string-length sp)\n                                           (string-length \"gambitcheck.ss\"))))\n                   (root (substring dir 0 (- (string-length dir)\n                                             (string-length \"host/gambit/\")))))\n              (string-append root \"host/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt\"))\n            #f))))\n\n(define (read-contract-names path)\n  (let ((p (open-input-file path)))\n    (let loop ((acc '()))\n      (let ((l (get-line p)))\n        (if (eof-object? l)\n            (begin (close-port p) (reverse acc))\n            (let ((toks (string->tokens (strip-comment l))))\n              (if (or (null? toks)\n                      (and (>= (length toks) 2)\n                           (string=? (car toks) \"#\")\n                           (string=? (cadr toks) \"tier:\")))\n                  (loop acc)\n                  (loop (cons (string->symbol (car toks)) acc)))))))))\n\n;; Syntax shims the variable-probe below cannot see (eval of a macro name is\n;; host-ffi.ss — the jolt.ffi host-owned surface for the GAMBIT target\n;; (P1b-stage1). On Chez these vars live in host/chez/java/ffi.ss, which the\n;; gambit boot manifest excludes — without this file every jolt.ffi name was an\n;; unbound global (the same shape the host-vars.ss degradation fixed for\n;; clojure.core). Stage-1 binds the memory/loader/errno surface the qualified\n;; tier backs (the adapter rows + the native bridge), implements what the\n;; stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj public functions call into, and binds EVERYTHING ELSE to\n;; a message-carrying refusal — nothing stays unbound, nothing pretends.\n;;\n;; Loaded after host-vars.ss, before the seed image (same rule: these bindings\n;; are the last word for the names the excluded ffi.ss owned). Requires the\n;; booted kernel (jolt-nil, def-var!, jolt-hash-map, make-pvec, ...) — this\n;; file is boot-world only; the sa-* tier it leans on also loads standalone\n;; under gambitcheck without it.\n\n;; ---- emitted-text helpers the compiler's ordinary-call wrappers lean on -----\n;; The :string conversions invert per direction like the Chez pair; jolt truthy\n;; rule for :bool; jfloat unboxing for :float/:double. jolt-ffi-c->string maps\n;; the adapter's NULL-string #f to jolt-nil (values.ss's sentinel — bound by\n;; the time any of these RUN; the define only closes over it).\n(define (jolt-ffi-string->c x)\n  (cond ((string? x) x)\n        ((jolt-nil? x) #f)                ; nil IS NULL, in both directions\n        (else (throw-jvm 'IllegalArgumentException\n                         (string-append \"jolt.ffi: :string got \" (jolt-pr-str x)\n                                        \" — NULL is spelled nil\")))))\n(define (jolt-ffi-c->string x) (if x x jolt-nil))\n(define (jolt-ffi-bool->c v) (if (or (jolt-nil? v) (eq? v #f)) 0 1))\n(define (jolt-ffi-c->bool raw) (not (eqv? (jnum->exact raw) 0)))\n(define (jolt-ffi-float->c x) (if (jfloat? x) (jfloat-fl x) x))\n\n;; A :string ARGUMENT travels as u8* on Chez (an immobile copy). Gambit has no\n;; immobile allocation and the stage-1 bridge carries no :string-argument shape\n;; (the registry has none), so this raises BEFORE the unbound-identifier fate\n;; the pre-stage1 boot would have dealt: the adapter's shape validation refuses\n;; :string arguments, and this helper — which the emitted wrapper evaluates\n;; first — refuses for any path that might reach it out of order.\n(define (jolt-ffi-string-arg x)\n  (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException\n             \"jolt.ffi: :string arguments are unsupported on the gambit target — no immobile allocation behind the stage-1 bridge\"))\n\n;; The emitted call keeps string copies live until C returns; identity here,\n;; because nothing that evaluates it can have a live foreign reference (the\n;; string-arg path above refuses first). Bound so the emitted TEXT never dies\n;; on an unbound identifier at load.\n(define (keep-live x) x)\n\n;; jolt-ffi-function-pointer: the pointer-call null guard (backend\n;; ffi-pointer-procedure-expr emits it ahead of each call). Pointer-call\n;; bindings are compile-time-refused on :gambit, so this only guards paths that\n;; hand a raw address to the ordinary tier.\n(define (jolt-ffi-function-pointer ptr)\n  (let ((address (if (jolt-nil? ptr) 0 (jnum->exact ptr))))\n    (if (eqv? address 0)\n        (throw-jvm 'NullPointerException \"jolt.ffi: null C function pointer\")\n        address)))\n\n;; jolt-ffi-dlsym-native (the compiler's emitted scoped probe) is defined in\n;; the adapter itself — it must exist in every world the emitted text loads in,\n;; including the adapter-only gambitcheck unit.\n\n;; ---- foreign memory over the adapter tier -------------------------------------\n;; alloc returns the ADDRESS (an exact integer); read/write take the type\n;; keyword and the offset LAST (the babashka.ffi order the stdlib wrapper\n;; keeps). Type keywords arrive as jolt keywords; the stdlib resolves layouts\n;; and places before calling, so these see scalars only.\n(define (joltffi-keyword-name kw)\n  (if (keyword-t? kw) (keyword-t-name kw) kw))\n\n(define (joltffi-type->chez kw)\n  (let ((n (joltffi-keyword-name kw)))\n    (cond\n      ((string=? n \"int\") 'int)\n      ((string=? n \"uint\") 'unsigned-int)\n      ((or (string=? n \"int8\") (string=? n \"i8\")) 'integer-8)\n      ((or (string=? n \"uint8\") (string=? n \"u8\") (string=? n \"byte\")) 'unsigned-8)\n      ((or (string=? n \"int16\") (string=? n \"short\")) 'integer-16)\n      ((or (string=? n \"uint16\") (string=? n \"ushort\")) 'unsigned-16)\n      ((string=? n \"int32\") 'integer-32)\n      ((string=? n \"uint32\") 'unsigned-32)\n      ((string=? n \"long\") 'long)\n      ((string=? n \"ulong\") 'unsigned-long)\n      ((string=? n \"int64\") 'integer-64)\n      ((string=? n \"uint64\") 'unsigned-64)\n      ((string=? n \"size_t\") 'size_t)\n      ((string=? n \"ssize_t\") 'ssize_t)\n      ((string=? n \"iptr\") 'iptr)\n      ((string=? n \"uptr\") 'uptr)\n      ((string=? n \"double\") 'double)\n      ((string=? n \"float\") 'float)\n(defn- ffi-aggregate-args\n  \"Index -> {:name :type} for each by-value aggregate argument, each with a fresh\n  ftype name.\"\n  [types]\n  (->> types\n       (map-indexed (fn [i type]\n                      (when (ffi-by-value? type)\n                        [i {:name (fresh-label \"jolt_ffi_arg\") :type (:type type)}])))\n       (remove nil?)\n       (into (sorted-map))))\n\n;; The Chez signature: each argument's foreign type, an aggregate as a pointer to\n;; its ftype, then the result's. SCALAR->CHEZ maps the rest: a foreign-fn sends a\n;; :string as u8* (ffi-arg-type->chez), a callback receives it as Chez's string.\n(defn- ffi-signature [types aggregates emitted-return scalar->chez]\n  (let [emitted-types (map-indexed (fn [i type]\n                                     (if-let [entry (get aggregates i)]\n                                       (str \"(& \" (:name entry) \")\")\n                                       (scalar->chez type)))\n                                   types)]\n    (str \" (\" (str/join \" \" emitted-types) \") \" emitted-return)))\n\n;; The define-ftype forms for the aggregates a binding passes or returns.\n(defn- ffi-ftype-defs [aggregates return-name rettype]\n  (concat\n   (map (fn [entry]\n          (str \"(define-ftype \" (:name entry) \" \"\n               (emit-ffi-layout-ftype (:type entry)) \")\"))\n        (vals aggregates))\n   (when return-name\n     [(str \"(define-ftype \" return-name \" \"\n           (emit-ffi-layout-ftype (:type rettype)) \")\")])))\n\n(defn- emit-ffi-fixed-fn [node vi]\n  (let [at (:argtypes node)\n        rettype (:rettype node)\n        ret-aggregate? (ffi-by-value? rettype)\n        types (if vi (vec (concat (subvec at 0 vi) (subvec at (inc vi)))) at)\n        params (ffi-params (count types))\n        return-param (when ret-aggregate? \"destination\")\n        aggregates (ffi-aggregate-args types)\n        return-name (when ret-aggregate? (fresh-label \"jolt_ffi_return\"))\n        signature (ffi-signature types aggregates\n                                 (if ret-aggregate?\n                                   (str \"(& \" return-name \")\")\n                                   (ffi-type->chez rettype))\n                                 ffi-arg-type->chez)\n        string-params (vec (keep-indexed (fn [i param]\n                                           (when (= \"string\" (nth types i)) param))\n                        \"\"\n                        \" — declare :pointer and read the member you know applies\"))))\n        {:ffi-kind :by-value\n         :type analyzed})\n    :else\n      (analysis-error :ffi/invalid-type (str \"jolt.ffi \" position\n                  \" type must be a keyword or [:by-value [:struct ...]], got \"\n                  (pr-str form)))))\n\n;; jolt.ffi/__cfn: the low-level foreign-function form a jolt library\n;; uses (via the jolt.ffi/foreign-fn macro) to bind native code. Shape:\n;;   (jolt.ffi/__cfn \"c_symbol\" [:argtype ...] :rettype)             ; non-blocking\n;;   (jolt.ffi/__cfn \"c_symbol\" [:argtype ...] :rettype :blocking)   ; may block\n;;   (jolt.ffi/__cfn \"c_symbol\" [:argtype ...] :rettype {opts})      ; options map\n;; The C symbol is a string literal and the types are literal keywords, read here\n;; at compile time; the Chez back end lowers it to a real `foreign-procedure`\n;; (typed marshaling, no runtime eval). A :blocking call is emitted __collect_safe\n;; so it deactivates the thread for the call — a blocking call (accept/recv/...)\n;; must not pin the stop-the-world collector. A leaf IR node.\n;;\n;; Normalize the optional form to the two literal Boolean flags understood by\n;; the back end. Direct __cfn calls and the public macros share this fail-closed\n;; validation: keys must be unqualified keywords, values literal Booleans, and\n;; unknown keys are rejected rather than ignored.\n(defn- ffi-option\n  ([]\n   {:blocking false :capture-native-error false})\n  ([opt]\n   (cond\n     (and (form-keyword? opt)\n          (nil? (namespace opt))\n          (= \"blocking\" (name opt)))\n     {:blocking true :capture-native-error false}\n\n     (form-map? opt)\n     (reduce\n       (fn [res pr]\n         (let [k (nth pr 0) v (nth pr 1)]\n           (when-not (and (form-keyword? k) (nil? (namespace k)))\n             (analysis-error :ffi/invalid-option (str \"jolt.ffi: option key must be an unqualified keyword, got: \" k)))\n           (let [kn (name k)]\n             (when-not (or (= kn \"blocking\") (= kn \"capture-native-error\"))\n               (analysis-error :ffi/invalid-option (str \"jolt.ffi: unknown option :\" kn)))\n             (when-not (or (true? v) (false? v))\n               (analysis-error :ffi/invalid-option (str \"jolt.ffi: option :\" kn\n                           \" must be a literal Boolean, got: \" v)))\n             (assoc res\n                    (if (= kn \"blocking\") :blocking :capture-native-error)\n                    v))))\n       {:blocking false :capture-native-error false}\n       (form-map-pairs opt))\n\n     :else\n     (analysis-error :ffi/invalid-option (str \"jolt.ffi: option must be :blocking or an options map, got: \" opt)))))\n\n(defn- analyze-ffi-signature [argtypes-form rettype-form opt-forms]\n  (let [rettype (analyze-ffi-signature-type rettype-form \"return\")\n        opt (if (seq opt-forms) (ffi-option (first opt-forms)) (ffi-option))\n        blocking (:blocking opt)\n        capture (:capture-native-error opt)]\n    (when (and capture (= rettype \"void\"))\n      (analysis-error :ffi/invalid-option (str \"jolt.ffi: :capture-native-error is not supported for :void \"\n                  \"(no stable native result to pair with the error code)\")))\n    (when (and capture (map? rettype))\n      (analysis-error :ffi/invalid-option \"jolt.ffi: :capture-native-error is not supported for by-value returns\"))\n    {:op :ffi-fn\n        (str \"(lambda args (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException \"\n             (chez-str-lit \"jolt.ffi/pointer-fn: ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\")\n             \"))\")\n      ;; gap G-2: a by-value aggregate needs define-ftype / (& ftype), unbound\n      ;; on the gambit boot — refuse in words instead of dying on the ftype\n      ;; forms the way the pre-stage1 emission did.\n      (and (= :gambit (target))\n           (or (some ffi-by-value? at) (ffi-by-value? (:rettype node))))\n        (str \"(throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException \"\n             (chez-str-lit \"jolt.ffi/foreign-fn: by-value aggregates are unsupported on the gambit target (no ftype engine behind the stage-1 bridge)\")\n             \")\")\n      ;; bare :& compiles a foreign procedure per observed tail shape at run\n      ;; time (ffi-varargs-compile, an eval of runtime-signature construction) —\n      ;; exactly the open-ended shape space the finite stage-1 registry cannot\n      ;; claim. Compile-time refusal; declared-tail varargs still route through\n      ;; the registry below.\n      (and (= :gambit (target)) vi (= vi (dec (count at))))\n        (str \"(throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException \"\n             (chez-str-lit \"jolt.ffi/foreign-fn: bare :& varargs are unsupported on the gambit target (per-call tail shapes compile at run time, outside the stage-1 registry)\")\n             \")\")\n      (and vi (= vi (dec (count at)))) (emit-ffi-bare-varargs-fn node vi)\n      :else (emit-ffi-fixed-fn node vi))))\n\n(defn- ffi-callable-wrapper\n  \"The lambda that converts a callback's arguments and result around FN-NODE.\"\n  [emit fn-node argtypes rettype aggregates ret-aggregate?]\n  ;; The fn is bound to a fresh name rather than inlined into the lambda\n  ;; body so it is evaluated once, at callable-construction time, not on\n  ;; every call C makes through the entry point.\n  (let [fname (fresh-label \"jolt_ffi_cb\")\n        params (ffi-params (count argtypes))\n        args (vec (map-indexed\n                   (fn [i param]\n                     (if (get aggregates i)\n                       (str \"(ftype-pointer-address \" param \")\")\n                       (ffi-c->jolt (nth argtypes i) param)))\n                   params))\n        args (if ret-aggregate?\n               (into [\"(ftype-pointer-address destination)\"] args)\n               args)\n        invoke (str \"(\" fname (when (seq args) (str \" \" (str/join \" \" args))) \")\")]\n    (str \"(let ((\" fname \" \" (emit fn-node) \")) \"\n         \"(lambda (\" (str/join \" \" (if ret-aggregate? (cons \"destination\" params) params)) \") \"\n         (if ret-aggregate? invoke (ffi-jolt->c rettype invoke))\n         \"))\")))\n\n(defn- ffi-collect-safe-entry\n  \"TARGET wrapped so each call C makes counts itself in and out.\"\n  [target arity]\n  (def-var-with-meta! \"jolt.analyzer\" \"gensym-counter\" (let ((_kc$27280 (jolt-var \"clojure.core\" \"at","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh <<'SH'\n#\"'!/bin/sh\n# External deadline kills the entire gate process group, including make'\"'s children.\nexec python3 - \\\"\"'$@\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport os, signal, subprocess, sys\nseconds = float(sys.argv[1])\np = subprocess.Popen(sys.argv[2:], start_new_session=True)\ntry:\n    status = p.wait(timeout=seconds)\nexcept subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n    os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n    p.wait()\n    print('WATCHDOG: TIMEOUT after %ss: %s' % (seconds, ' '.join(sys.argv[2:])), file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(124)\nsys.exit(status if status >= 0 else 128 - status)\nPY\nSH\nsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 240 make gambitffi GAMBIT_PREFIX=/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8 > /tmp/p1b-ffi.log 2>&1; st=\"'$?; tail -20 /tmp/p1b-ffi.log; exit \"$st\"'","aggregated_output":"  ok     scalar ssize_t\n  ok     scalar float\n  ok     scalar double\n  ok     scalar void*\n== generated capture shapes ==\n  ok     fixed capture (distinct from variadic s22b)\n  ok     s26b\n  ok     s26c\n  ok     s26d\n  ok     s26e\n  ok     s23\n  ok     s22b variadic tail\n  ok     s22c variadic pointer tail\n  FAIL   unregistered signature names its shape: got \"NO-RAISE\" expected message containing \"(void*) -> void*\"\n  ok     wrong variadic boundary refuses before dereference -> jolt.ffi: no gambit shim for signature (int int int) -> int — unregistered shape on the gambit target (the stage-1 registry covers the non-blocking p1b-inv shapes only; see p1b-inv/shim-registry.edn)\n  ok     string arguments refuse -> jolt.ffi: :string arguments are unsupported on the gambit target — no immobile allocation behind the stage-1 bridge (signature: u8* argument)\n\ngambitffi-abi: 76 check(s), 2 failure(s)\ngambitffi-abi: FAILED\nmake: *** [gambitffi-abi] Error 1\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
