{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1020,1044p' Makefile; cat test/chez/ffi-widths-test.sh | head -65; sed -n '1514,1524p' Makefile; tail -14 /tmp/p1b-final-gates.log; rg 'FAIL|HOST-ERROR' /tmp/p1b-final-gates.log\"","aggregated_output":"# the collect-safe convention cannot carry, which jolt must refuse in its own\n# words rather than leave to Chez's expander.\nffi:\n\t@$(CHEZ) --script test/chez/ffi-binding-test.ss\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-widths-test.sh \"$(CHEZ)\"\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-layout-test.sh \"$(CHEZ)\"\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-aggregate-test.sh \"$(CHEZ)\"\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-pointer-call-test.sh\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-callable-by-value-test.sh\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-stack-args-test.sh \"$(CHEZ)\"\n\t@bin/jolt run test/chez/jolt-ffi-scoped-test.clj\n\t@bin/jolt run test/chez/jolt-ffi-arena-test.clj\n\t@bin/jolt run test/chez/jolt-ffi-typed-array-test.clj\n\t@bin/jolt run test/chez/jolt-ffi-callback-preempt-test.clj\n\t@bin/jolt run test/chez/jolt-ffi-string-arg-test.clj\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-native-error-test.sh \"$(CHEZ)\"\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-foreign-thread-test.sh\n\t@sh test/chez/ffi-gc-stall-test.sh\n\t@sh test/chez/collect-safe-activation-test.sh \"$(CHEZ)\"\n\n# zlib bindings (host/chez/java/zlib.ss): the z_stream layout, entry-point\n# resolution, checksums, round trips, error codes, dictionaries, parameter\n# changes, close, and the guardian drain.\nzlibunit:\n\t@$(CHEZ) --script test/chez/zlib-test.ss\n#!/bin/sh\n# Build the exact-width C witness outside the tree, run it, and retain the\n# complete temporary directory on failure for diagnosis.\nset -u\n\nCHEZ=${1-}\n[ -n \"$CHEZ\" ] || { echo \"usage: $0 <chez>\" >&2; exit 2; }\nC=test/chez/ffi-widths-helper.c\n[ -f \"$C\" ] || { echo \"missing $C (run from repo root)\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\nOUT=$(mktemp -d) || {\n  echo \"failed to create ffi-widths artifact directory\" >&2\n  exit 1\n}\n[ -n \"$OUT\" ] && [ -d \"$OUT\" ] || {\n  echo \"mktemp returned no usable ffi-widths artifact directory\" >&2\n  exit 1\n}\ncase \"$(uname -s)\" in\n  Darwin) EXT=dylib ;;\n  MINGW*|MSYS*|CYGWIN*) EXT=dll ;;\n  *) EXT=so ;;\nesac\nSO=$OUT/jolt-ffi-widths-helper.$EXT\ncleanup() {\n  status=$?\n  if [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    rm -f \"$SO\"\n    rmdir \"$OUT\"\n  else\n    echo \"retained ffi-widths artifacts: $OUT\" >&2\n  fi\n}\ntrap cleanup EXIT\nCC_BIN=${CC:-cc}\n\ncase \"$(uname -s)\" in\n  Darwin) \"$CC_BIN\" -dynamiclib -o \"$SO\" \"$C\" ;;\n  MINGW*|MSYS*|CYGWIN*) \"$CC_BIN\" -shared -o \"$SO\" \"$C\" ;;\n  *) \"$CC_BIN\" -shared -fPIC -o \"$SO\" \"$C\" ;;\nesac || { echo \"cc failed to build $C\" >&2; exit 1; }\n\nJOLT_FFI_WIDTHS_HELPER=$SO \"$CHEZ\" --script test/chez/ffi-widths-test.ss\n# contract file lists a name Chez does not provide.\nadaptercheck:\n\t@$(CHEZ) --script host/scheme-adapter/chez.ss\n\n# The three derived host properties (sa-os-family / sa-arch / sa-endian) are all\n# host logic may ask about the platform, so one wrong row is a wrong SIGCHLD,\n# LC_TIME and struct-stat offset at once. The row that broke in #796 — a\n# portable-bytecode tag, which names no OS — is only reachable from a host we do\n# not build on, so the table is pinned per tag rather than per running machine.\nhostprops:\n\t@$(CHEZ) --script test/chez/host-derived-props-test.ss\n  ok     after a scoped load, the scoped probe answers\n  ok     a scoped library stays invisible to global resolution\n  ok     sa-foreign-entry? answers for the loaded fixture\n== repeat load is a no-op with the same handle ==\n  ok     repeat load registered exactly one handle\n== duplicate definers: two addresses, first declared resolves ==\n  ok     two distinct addresses across two declared libraries\n  ok     the addresses differ\n  ok     the first declared library wins resolution\n  ok     first-declared symbol behaves like fixture 1\n\ngambitffi-load-failure-smoke: 14 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-load-failure-smoke: PASS\ngambitffi: PASS — all stage-1 qualified-tier gates green\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
