{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1140,1166p' host/chez/java/ffi.ss; sed -n '1192,1228p' host/chez/java/ffi.ss; sed -n '170,205p' host/gambit/host-ffi.ss; rg -n 'unsupported|refus|qualified|string-contains|int32|both supported' host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss | head -36; rg 'gambitffi.*check\\\\(s\\\\)|gambit.*PASS|kernel-test:|eval-test:' /tmp/p1b-final-gates.log | tail -20; git diff --numstat\"","aggregated_output":";; --- string / bytevector marshaling ------------------------------------------\n;; A C string result already comes back as a jolt string (the `string` foreign\n;; type). For a `void*` that points at a NUL-terminated C string, read it here.\n;;\n;; A LIMIT bounds the scan: without one this walks to the first NUL wherever it\n;; is, which on a buffer that has none reads past the allocation and can stop\n;; the process. With one, a missing NUL inside `limit` bytes raises instead —\n;; the caller knows how big the buffer is, so it can say so.\n(define ffi-ptr->string\n  (case-lambda\n    ((ptr) (ffi-ptr->string* ptr #f))\n    ((ptr limit)\n     (ffi-ptr->string* ptr (if (jolt-nil? limit) #f (jnum->exact limit))))))\n(define (ffi-ptr->string* ptr limit)\n  (if (ffi-null? ptr) jolt-nil\n      (let ((p (jnum->exact ptr)))\n        (let loop ((i 0) (acc '()))\n          (cond\n            ((and limit (>= i limit))\n             (jolt-throw (jolt-ex-info\n                           \"jolt.ffi/ptr->string: no NUL byte within the limit\"\n                           (jolt-hash-map (jolt-keyword \"limit\") limit))))\n            (else\n             (let ((b (sa-foreign-ref 'unsigned-8 p i)))\n               (if (= b 0) (utf8->string (u8-list->bytevector (reverse acc)))\n                   (loop (+ i 1) (cons b acc))))))))))\n;; Copy a jolt string's UTF-8 bytes into a freshly alloc'd NUL-terminated buffer;\n        (ja-bytes->bv! s 0 bv 0 n)\n        bv)\n      (string->utf8 (jolt-str-render-one s))))\n\n(define (ffi-string->ptr s)\n  (if (jolt-nil? s)\n      ffi-null\n      ;; ONE block move plus the terminator. This used to be a per-byte\n      ;; sa-foreign-set! loop, ~30ns a byte across the boundary — the cost this\n      ;; file's buffer-I/O section exists to avoid, on the one path that had\n      ;; kept it.\n      (let* ((bv (ffi-value-octets s))\n             (n (bytevector-length bv))\n             (p (sa-foreign-alloc (+ n 1))))\n        ;; free on a mid-copy throw — the caller only ever sees a whole buffer\n        (guard (e (#t (guard (_ (#t #f)) (sa-foreign-free p)) (raise e)))\n          (when (> n 0) (sa-foreign-bytes-set! p bv n))\n          (sa-foreign-set! 'unsigned-8 p n 0)\n          p))))\n\n;; The octet count string->ptr just copied, less the NUL, so an arena can record\n;; the block's size without scanning for the NUL again.\n(define (ffi-utf8-length s)\n  (if (jolt-nil? s) 0 (bytevector-length (ffi-value-octets s))))\n\n;; --- bare :& — per-call variadic tail inference ------------------------------\n;; babashka.ffi's BARE :& is one binding serving every tail shape: no types\n;; follow the marker, and each call's tail is read off the values it is given.\n;;\n;;   (ffi/defcfn c-open \"open\" [:string :int :&] :int)\n;;   (c-open path O_RDONLY)        ; empty tail\n;;   (c-open path flags #o644)     ; one-int tail, same binding\n;;\n;; A Chez foreign-procedure has its argument and result types fixed when it is\n;; COMPILED, so a call has nothing to compile a new one from. The binding is\n;; therefore a DISPATCHER over a cache of compiled procedures, one per observed\n;; tail shape, rather than a single procedure: on a miss it builds the\n                (seq->list (jolt-seq ps)))))\n  jolt-nil)\n(define (joltffi-recorded-size ptr)\n  (jwm-call joltffi-sizes-mu (lambda () (hashtable-ref joltffi-sizes (jnum->exact ptr) 0))))\n\n;; ---- alloc/free ------------------------------------------------------------------\n(define (joltffi-alloc nbytes)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact nbytes))\n         (p (sa-foreign-alloc n)))\n    (when (> n 0) (joltffi-remember-size! p n))\n    p))\n(define (joltffi-calloc nbytes)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact nbytes))\n         (p (sa-foreign-alloc n)))\n    (when (> n 0)\n      (sa-foreign-zero! p n)\n      (joltffi-remember-size! p n))\n    p))\n(define (joltffi-host-free ptr) (sa-foreign-free (jnum->exact ptr)) jolt-nil)\n(define (joltffi-copy src dst n)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact n)) (bv (make-bytevector n)))\n    (when (> n 0)\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! (jnum->exact src) bv n)\n      (sa-foreign-bytes-set! (jnum->exact dst) bv n))\n    jolt-nil))\n(define (joltffi-null? ptr) (and (number? ptr) (= (jnum->exact ptr) 0)))\n(define joltffi-null 0)\n\n;; read/write take (ptr ty [off]) — the babashka.ffi offset-last order\n(define joltffi-read-fn\n  (case-lambda ((ptr ty) (joltffi-read ptr ty 0))\n               ((ptr ty off) (joltffi-read ptr ty off))))\n(define joltffi-write-fn\n  (case-lambda ((ptr ty val) (joltffi-write ptr ty val 0))\n               ((ptr ty val off) (joltffi-write ptr ty val off))))\n\n20:;;            keeps its message-carrying refusal, and with the bridge absent\n24:;;            jolt.image treat the raise as a clean cache disable / unsupported.\n37:;; subprocess support must raise 'unsupported — every caller genuinely needs\n41:  (error 'sa-run-process \"subprocess support is unsupported on the gambit target\" cmd))\n303:;; name + captured values. Degradation: #f — the image writer refuses the\n321:;; the qualified set keeps its message-carrying refusal:\n330:;; message-carrying unsupported error again. Unregistered shapes raise BEFORE\n334:  (error who \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target\"))\n356:;; error. Loading is attempted once; a failed load leaves the tier refusing.\n379:                    \"ffi is unsupported on the gambit target: the stage-1 native\"\n396:  (not (string-contains? name \"/\")))\n507:;; provide (moving collector, no immobile allocation) — refused with a\n515:                 \"jolt.ffi: :string arguments are unsupported on the gambit target\"\n522:;; :gambit arm refuses them earlier; this is the defensive layer behind it).\n526:             (string-append \"jolt.ffi: aggregate results are unsupported on the\"\n596:;; only NORMALIZE; every decision (bridge presence, registration, refusal) is a\n627:;; () for ordinary capture, (__collect_safe) for the refused blocking\n630:  `(sa-foreign-procedure-native-error unsupported-native-error ,@form))\n633:;; REFUSED (codex C4): GC-safe blocking is unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 — a\n640:         \"blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target — GC-safe blocking is unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 (no verified release/claim transition)\"))\n652:         \"foreign callables are unsupported on the gambit target — dynamic closure-backed callables are unqualified (no arm64/x86_64 trampoline generator in stock Gambit 4.9.8)\"))\n659:         \"foreign-thread callbacks are unsupported on the gambit target — generic foreign-pthread entry is unqualified (no verified attachment/claim protocol)\"))\n669:         \"runtime-signature ffi construction is unsupported on the gambit target — a finite shim registry cannot claim runtime-discovered signatures\"))\n671:;; ---- memory ops (qualified; through the bridge) -------------------------------\n710:            (string-append \"jolt.ffi: unsupported foreign type \"\n731:            (string-append \"jolt.ffi: unsupported foreign type \"\n747:      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy refused by the bridge\" n)))\n756:      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-set! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy refused by the bridge\" n)))\n762:;; sizes are exact constants for LP64 layouts (LP64; only macOS arm64 is qualified here). :bool travels as unsigned-8 (the ONE-BYTE C99 _Bool); the\n782:;; be a silent lie — a consistent refusal, never a one-sided pin.\n785:         \"object pinning is unsupported on the gambit target — the collector moves objects and no verified pinning mechanism exists\"))\n789:         \"object pinning is unsupported on the gambit target — the collector moves objects and no verified pinning mechanism exists\"))\n791:;; ---- loading and resolution (qualified; scoped-first) ------------------------\n869:  (error 'sa-compile-file \"native compilation is unsupported on the gambit target\" src))\n876:  (error 'sa-make-boot-file \"native compilation is unsupported on the gambit target\" out))\n881:;; unsupported error carrying the condition's message; the raise must be\ngambitffi-abi: 78 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-abi: PASS\ngambitffi-public: 28 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-public: PASS — :gambit compiler + native gsi\ngambitffi-errno-check: 9 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-errno-check: PASS\ngambitffi-load-failure-smoke: 14 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-load-failure-smoke: PASS\ngambitffi: PASS — all stage-1 qualified-tier gates green\ngambitcheck: PASS — gambit adapter + shims verified on native gsi\ngambitffi-public: 28 check(s), 0 failure(s)\ngambitffi-public: PASS — :gambit compiler + native gsi\nkernel-test: 0 failure(s)\nkernel-test: PASS — booted kernel + natives verified on native gsi\neval-test: 0 failure(s)\neval-test: PASS — jolt compiles and evaluates on native gsi\n121\t4\tMakefile\n355\t354\thost/chez/seed/image.ss\n5\t0\thost/gambit/boot.ss\n54\t29\thost/gambit/gambitcheck.ss\n1\t1\thost/gambit/gen-seed.ss\n522\t136\thost/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss\n330\t328\thost/gambit/seed/image.ss\n5\t0\thost/scheme-adapter/CONTRACT.txt\n7\t3\thost/scheme-adapter/TARGET-CONTRACT.md\n52\t27\tjolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj\n6\t1\tjolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/session.clj\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
